E["item:alaric-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Alaric's Remains",z="silverpine",s="Alaric's Remains are the recovered bones of an individual once interred in a shallow grave along Silverpine Forest. His lingering spirit bids travelers to carry what is left of him past the Rot Hide gnolls into the towers of Fenris Keep.",h="Alaric's Remains are the recovered bones of an individual once interred in a shallow grave along Silverpine...",sec={{t="A Final Request",b="Unearthed from an unremarkable shallow grave in Silverpine Forest, the remains belong to Alaric, a former resident of Fenris Isle. Rather than linger in an exposed pit, his spirit yearns for the place he cherished in life. He asks whoever unearths his bones to leave his ill-fitting boots behind and bring his skeletal remains directly into the keep, seeking quiet sanctuary far away from the scavengers prowling the mainland.",sp=0},{t="The Alcove in the Keep",b="Alaric guides the carrier to the southwestern tower of Fenris Keep, past the infested lower grounds into a quiet chamber. Tucked behind a dusty shelf lies a concealed niche containing an artifact once valued by Thule Ravenclaw and his fellow mages. In exchange for granting him an undisturbed resting place sealed away from the ravenous Rot Hide gnolls, Alaric yields the hidden trinkets to those who carried his bones home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Alaric?",a="Alaric was an inhabitant of Fenris Keep before its ruin, spending what he considered the finest days of his life within its halls. Following his death, he was buried hastily in a shallow grave in Silverpine Forest until his spirit directed a passerby to carry his bones back home.",al={"who is alaric","alaric lore","who was this guy"},it="identity"},{q="Where are Alaric's remains supposed to go?",a="His remains are meant to be placed into a concealed alcove behind a dusty shelf in the southwestern tower of Fenris Keep, situated on Fenris Isle.",al={"where do i bring alaric","dusty shelf location","where is the niche"},it="target"},{q="Why does Alaric want his remains sealed behind a shelf?",a="Fenris Keep brought him great comfort in life, and he wishes to rest within its stone walls rather than in a dirt ditch. Sealing the hidden alcove tightly also protects his skeleton from being devoured or desecrated by the Rot Hide gnolls roaming the keep.",al={"why fenris keep","why the niche","why hide the body"},it="purpose"},{q="Why did he say to leave his boots behind?",a="When directing the recovery of his bones from the shallow grave, Alaric casually noted that his boots never fit him in life anyway, leaving them behind as useless clutter.",al={"leave the boots","alaric's boots","boots never fit"}},{q="What is inside the hidden alcove besides a resting place?",a="The secret niche holds an item once treasured by Thule Ravenclaw and his former associates, alongside magical belongings Alaric willingly bequeaths to anyone willing to bear his remains to rest.",al={"hidden niche treasure","what is behind the shelf","thule's item"}},{q="What are Alaric's Remains?",a="These are the physical bones and bodily remnants of Alaric, a former inhabitant of Fenris Keep who died and was hastily buried in Silverpine Forest. His lingering spirit retains consciousness within his bones, urging travelers to recover him from the dirt so he can find a final, peaceful resting place.",al={"what is alarics remains","alaric corpse","alarics remains item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do Alaric's Remains come from?",a="You exhume them from a crude, shallow grave dug in the wilderness of Silverpine Forest, minus the ill-fitting boots he was buried in. Alaric perished out in the wilds away from his former home, leaving his unhallowed remains trapped in the earth until someone unearthed him.",al={"where did alaric die","shallow grave alaric","who made alarics remains"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Alaric want his remains recovered?",a="Alaric spent the happiest years of his life inside Fenris Keep, and resting in the wilds brings him no peace. He wants his remains brought back to the keep and tucked securely inside a hidden alcove behind a dusty bookshelf, safe from the scavenging Rot Hide gnolls infesting the grounds.",al={"why take alarics remains","why does alaric want his body moved","why move alaric"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken travelers often empathize with spirits whose mortal rest was interrupted, though Alaric seeks peaceful seclusion rather than service under the Dark Lady.",["class:Mage"]="The hidden cache Alaric reveals contains relics connected to Thule Ravenclaw and the Dalaran-trained arcanists who once studied and schemed inside Fenris Keep."},kw={"alaric","alaric's remains","fenris keep","rot hide","shallow grave","silverpine forest","the hidden niche","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:461","quest:460","subzone:fenris-keep","zone:silverpine","quest:491"},src={"Alaric's Remains","The Hidden Niche"}}
E["item:ataeric-s-staff"] = {t="item",n="Ataeric's Staff",z="silverpine",s="Ataeric's Staff is a powerful magical conduit wielded by Archmage Ataeric, a senior Dalaran wizard in Silverpine Forest. It serves as both a focus for manipulating local ley lines and physical proof of the archmage's defeat for the Forsaken at the Sepulcher.",h="Ataeric's Staff is a powerful magical conduit wielded by Archmage Ataeric, a senior Dalaran wizard in...",sec={{t="A Conduit of Ley Magic",b="Carried by Archmage Ataeric, this staff was used to direct and harness ley energies in southern Silverpine Forest. Under Dalaran's direction, Ataeric attempted to reactivate an ancient ley energy node near the borders of the magocracy's territory. The staff acted as a vital tool for weaving these immense ambient currents, rendering the archmage a formidable threat to nearby Forsaken settlements.",sp=0},{t="Trophy of the Sepulcher",b="Alarmed by Dalaran's magical expansion, Shadow Priest Allister ordered Ataeric's assassination and demanded the recovery of the staff. With Ataeric slain and his staff recovered, the concentrated ley energies collapsed back into dormancy. Bringing the staff to the Sepulcher marked a decisive victory against Dalaran's ambitions, though the Forsaken remain watchful of the latent power remaining in the earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who does Ataeric's Staff belong to?",a="The staff belongs to Archmage Ataeric, a high-ranking Dalaran wizard stationed in Silverpine Forest to oversee the reactivation of a potent ley node.",al={"who owns ataerics staff","ataeric owner","who dropped this staff"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister want Ataeric's Staff?",a="Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher wants the staff as confirmation of Archmage Ataeric's death and to ensure that Dalaran's efforts to manipulate the region's ley lines are completely broken.",al={"why allister want staff","staff purpose sepulcher","who takes the staff"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens once the staff is taken from Archmage Ataeric?",a="Once Ataeric is slain and his staff removed, the ley energies Dalaran was weaving dissipate and settle into dormancy, ending the immediate magical threat to the Forsaken.",al={"what happens to the ley line","after defeating ataeric"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Where is Ataeric's Staff found?",a="It is recovered directly from the body of Archmage Ataeric, who is found among other Dalaran mages and warders near Dalaran's presence in southern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to get ataeric staff","ataeric location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Recovering the staff halts Dalaran's expanding grip over Silverpine's magical reserves, securing the Forsaken's western borders.",["class:Mage"]="The staff exemplifies the focused implements Dalaran's archmagi use to tap into and reawaken slumbering ley nodes."},kw={"archmage ataeric","ataeric's staff","dalaran","ley node","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest","the weaver"},rel={"quest:480","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran","topic:mage","topic:priest"},src={"Ataeric's Staff","The Weaver (quest)"}}
E["item:bethor-s-scroll"] = {t="item",n="Bethor's Scroll",z="silverpine",s="Bethor's Scroll contains magical incantations scribed by Bethor Iceshard to counter the dark sorcery of his former colleague, Thule Ravenclaw. Created to aid Apothecary Renferrel in brewing a protective draught, the scroll is vital for surviving the Scourge necromancy guarding Fenris Isle.",h="Bethor's Scroll contains magical incantations scribed by Bethor Iceshard to counter the dark sorcery of his...",sec={{t="A Colleague's Betrayal",b="Upon examining tainted ichor recovered from Rot Hide gnolls, Bethor Iceshard recognized the handiwork of Thule Ravenclaw. Once a promising young mage of the Kirin Tor, Thule betrayed his brethren to serve the Lich King when the Scourge rose to power. Learning that Thule had survived and was directing Rot Hide attacks across Silverpine Forest from Fenris Isle, Bethor drew upon his intimate knowledge of his former colleague's spellcraft to author this scroll.",sp=0},{t="Countering the Necromancer",b="The scroll is saturated with potent arcane formulas designed not as an offensive weapon, but as a brewing guide for the Royal Apothecary Society. Handed to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher, the scroll provides the exact counter-incantations required to synthesize a restorative potion capable of dispelling the debilitating hexes Thule weaves around his fortress.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written on Bethor's Scroll?",a="The scroll details specialized arcane incantations formulated by Bethor Iceshard. Having once studied alongside Thule Ravenclaw, Bethor knew the necromancer's preferred spells and inscribed the precise formulas needed to brew an alchemical counter-potion.",al={"what does the scroll say","contents of bethors scroll","what is on the scroll"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives this scroll?",a="The scroll must be delivered to Apothecary Renferrel, stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Renferrel uses the magic bound within it to create a protective draught.",al={"who do i give the scroll to","bethors scroll turn in","who gets the scroll"},gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel need magical incantations for a potion?",a="Apothecary Renferrel specializes in alchemy rather than traditional sorcery, admitting he rarely weaves such overt forces into his concoctions. However, ordinary anti-toxins cannot pierce the Scourge curses shielding Thule, requiring Bethor's arcane formulas to make the brew effective.",al={"why does an apothecary need spells","magic potion renferrel"},it="purpose"},{q="Who was Thule Ravenclaw before turning to the Scourge?",a="Before the Third War, Thule was a promising young human mage and an associate of Bethor Iceshard. When the Lich King marshaled his undead armies, Thule abandoned his fellow spellcasters and pledged his loyalty to the Scourge.",al={"who is thule ravenclaw","thule backstory","thule and bethor"},it="history"},{q="Where does Bethor's Scroll come from, and who made it?",a="The scroll is penned by Bethor Iceshard, an undead mage serving the Forsaken from his tower in the Undercity. Recognizing the magical signature on vile ichor recovered from Rot Hide gnolls, Bethor realized his former colleague Thule Ravenclaw had survived and turned to the Scourge. Drawing on his intimate knowledge of Thule's arcane techniques, Bethor transcribed counter-incantations onto this parchment to aid in defeating his rogue former peer.",al={"who wrote bethor's scroll","who made bethor's scroll","where did bethors scroll come from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why is Bethor's Scroll needed?",a="Apothecary Renferrel requires the magical incantations inscribed upon the scroll to brew a protective counter-agent. Thule Ravenclaw wields potent, debilitating hexes from his stronghold on Fenris Isle. By infusing Bethor's arcane formulae into an alchemical draught, the Royal Apothecary Society can produce a specialized potion that shields you against Thule's dark sorcery when you confront him.",al={"why want bethor's scroll","why is bethors scroll important","what is bethor's scroll used for"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The scroll illustrates the Kirin Tor's fractured past, showing how intimate knowledge of a fellow spellcaster's signature magic can be turned into a potent countermeasure.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken spellcasters and apothecaries combine their distinct talents through this parchment, blending Dalaran's old arcane training with the new alchemical craft of the Sepulcher."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","bethor's scroll","fenris isle","rot hide","silverpine","the sepulcher","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:446","quest:442","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:sepulcher","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:scourge","zone:silverpine"},src={"Bethor's Scroll","Thule Ravenclaw (quest)"}}
E["item:clarice-s-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Clarice's Pendant",z="silverpine",s="Clarice's Pendant is a small keepsake belonging to Clarice Foster, an undead resident of the Sepulcher. Once a token from her former husband, Yuriv, the jewelry now serves only as a bitter reminder of abandoned family and misplaced devotion to the Light.",h="Clarice's Pendant is a small keepsake belonging to Clarice Foster, an undead resident of the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Bitter Token",b="Clarice's Pendant represents the fractured human past common to many of the Forsaken. Before the Third War consumed Lordaeron, Clarice's husband Yuriv abandoned her and their children to join the fight against the undead, proclaiming that devotion to the Holy Light took precedence over all else. Instead of saving his home, Yuriv perished, leaving his family behind to ultimately succumb to the very Scourge he set out to fight. For Clarice, the pendant is not a cherished memento, but an insulting trinket symbolizing a lifetime spent coming second to zealotry and duty.",sp=0},{t="Resting upon Yuriv's Tomb",b="Wishing to sever the remaining emotional ties to her former life and unfaithful husband, Clarice sends an adventurer to return the piece of jewelry directly to Yuriv's grave at the Sepulcher. The tomb is neglected and vandalized, buried beneath weeds and trash. When the pendant is finally laid across the sculpted hands of the coffin, its gemstone turns noticeably dull, extinguishing the last lingering warmth of Clarice's former life.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who owns Clarice's Pendant?",a="The pendant belongs to Clarice Foster, a Forsaken woman residing at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. It was given to her in life by her husband, Yuriv, before he marched off to war.",al={"who does the pendant belong to","whose pendant is this","clarice foster"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Yuriv?",a="Yuriv was Clarice's husband in life. He abandoned Clarice and their children to fight the rising undead threat in the name of the Holy Light, only to perish and end up buried in a neglected grave at the Sepulcher.",al={"clarice husband","who is yuriv","yuriv tomb"},it="people"},{q="Why does Clarice want to get rid of the pendant?",a="Clarice resents Yuriv for prioritizing his crusade and devotion to the Light over her and their children. His sacrifice accomplished nothing—he died anyway, and she was left behind only to end up raised in undeath, the very condition he sought to eradicate.",al={"why throw away pendant","why does clarice hate yuriv","clarice pendant quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when the pendant is placed on Yuriv's grave?",a="When placed atop the relief sculpted on Yuriv's tomb, the gemstone set within the pendant noticeably dulls, symbolizing a final, cold end to the connection between them as a chill wind passes through the graveyard.",al={"what happens at yuriv tomb","pendant on grave"},sp=1,it="power"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The pendant highlights the tragedy and bitterness common to many Forsaken, whose living loved ones often abandoned them for crusades that ultimately failed to protect anyone.",["class:Paladin"]="Clarice's contempt for Yuriv's crusade is an uncomfortable reminder of the personal cost and broken homes left in the wake of holy zeal."},kw={"clarice foster","clarice's pendant","forsaken","sepulcher","silverpine forest","tomb","until death do us part","yuriv"},rel={"quest:264","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:light"},src={"Clarice's Pendant","Until Death Do Us Part"}}
E["item:dalaran-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Dalaran Pendant",z="silverpine",s="Dalaran Pendants are magical talismans carried by the Kirin Tor wizards stationed at the village of Ambermill in Silverpine Forest. The Forsaken seek to collect these pendants to disrupt the magi's arcane workings and trace the source of their power.",h="Dalaran Pendants are magical talismans carried by the Kirin Tor wizards stationed at the village of Ambermill...",sec={{t="Amulets of Ambermill",b="In the village of Ambermill, Kirin Tor sorcerers, conjurers, and protectors actively weave formidable arcane spells threatening Forsaken control over southern Silverpine Forest. Each operative carries an attuned Dalaran Pendant. At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister tasks Forsaken operatives with recovering these pendants to slow down the mages' efforts and uncover who is guiding their magical weave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Dalaran Pendant?",a="It is an arcane amulet worn by Kirin Tor conjurers, mages, and protectors stationed in Ambermill. The Forsaken recover them to interrupt the wizards' ritual workings and examine their magical craft.",al={"what is dalaran pendant","kirin tor necklace silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Who carries these pendants?",a="They are carried by the human mages, conjurers, and protectors of Dalaran occupying Ambermill in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who drops dalaran pendant","where to get dalaran pendant"},it="people"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister want them?",a="Shadow Priest Allister and his ally Dalar need the pendants to slow the wizards' spellcasting and pinpoint the powerful mage directing the weave of magical energy in Ambermill.",al={"why allister wants pendants","ambermill investigations pendant"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Ambermill located?",a="Ambermill lies in southern Silverpine Forest. Travelers heading south from the Sepulcher take the eastern fork off the main road to find the village.",al={"ambermill location","how to get to ambermill"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Stripping these pendants from the Kirin Tor is a vital step in securing Silverpine Forest against human sorcerers attempting to re-establish their foothold.",["class:Mage"]="The pendants serve as focuses for Kirin Tor weaving, showcasing how Dalaran sorcerers coordinate complex, collective magic."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalaran pendant","kirin tor","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"quest:479","subzone:ambermill","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran","topic:mage","topic:priest"},src={"Dalaran Pendant","Ambermill Investigations"}}
E["item:darksoul-shackle"] = {t="item",n="Darksoul Shackle",z="silverpine",s="A Darksoul Shackle is an enchanted fetter worn by the Moonrage Darksoul worgen stalking Silverpine Forest. Crafted under the direction of Archmage Arugal, these implements are sought by Forsaken mages at the Sepulcher seeking to unravel the feral magic gripping the region.",h="A Darksoul Shackle is an enchanted fetter worn by the Moonrage Darksoul worgen stalking Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Crutch for Faltering Magic",b="When Archmage Arugal unleashed the worgen upon Silverpine Forest, his own arcane mastery proved insufficient to fully direct and sustain the otherworldly beasts. To compensate for his shortcomings, he bound enchanted implements, such as Darksoul Shackles, to his creations. These fetters channel external sorcery into the Moonrage Darksouls, reinforcing their supernatural strength and anchoring the curse that keeps them thrall to Shadowfang Keep.",sp=0},{t="Kirin Tor Scrutiny",b="At the Sepulcher, the Forsaken mage Dalar Dawnweaver considers Arugal a dangerous incompetent whose meddling ruined the Kirin Tor's defense against the Scourge. By gathering Darksoul Shackles alongside those torn from Moonrage Gluttons, Forsaken researchers extract the residual enchantments woven into the metal. Studying these crutches reveals the structural flaws in Arugal's spellcraft, providing the Forsaken with the arcane insight necessary to formulate a countermeasure against his lupine scourge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Darksoul Shackle?",a="It is an enchanted metal fetter worn by Moonrage Darksoul worgen in Silverpine Forest. It was crafted by Archmage Arugal to reinforce his flawed spellcraft and bind the beasts to his control.",al={"what are darksoul shackles","darksoul shackle item lore","what is this shackle"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Darksoul Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver, a Forsaken mage stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, requires them. He studies the enchantments inside the shackles to find a solution to Arugal's worgen outbreak.",al={"who needs darksoul shackles","who takes the shackles","dalar dawnweaver quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do these shackles come from?",a="They are recovered from the corpses of Moonrage Darksouls, aggressive worgen haunting the northern and eastern reaches of Silverpine Forest.",al={"who drops darksoul shackles","darksoul shackle mob","where to get darksoul shackle"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Arugal put shackles on the worgen?",a="According to Dalar Dawnweaver, Arugal was not a talented enough mage to command the beasts through sheer power alone. He relied on enchanted objects like these shackles to channel and sustain the volatile magic holding the pack together.",al={"why do worgen wear shackles","arugal shackle purpose"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, breaking Arugal's hold on Silverpine Forest is essential to protecting their southern borders and proving the superiority of Undercity's arcane scholarship over Dalaran's failures.",["class:Mage"]="Examining these shackles reveals how a desperate wizard used crude enchanted artifacts to shore up volatile summoning spells he could not properly control."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","darksoul shackle","moonrage darksoul","sepulcher","silverpine forest","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","quest:99","npc:arugal","item:glutton-shackle","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Darksoul Shackle","Arugal's Folly (2)"}}
E["item:deathstalker-report"] = {t="item",n="Deathstalker Report",z="silverpine",s="The Deathstalker Report is a written dispatch penned by Deathstalker Rane Yorick detailing military reconnaissance in Silverpine Forest. It contains critical tactical intelligence intended for High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher regarding local Scourge movements and the state of the Forsaken's forward scouts.",h="The Deathstalker Report is a written dispatch penned by Deathstalker Rane Yorick detailing military...",sec={{t="Frontline Intelligence",b="Reconnaissance in northern Silverpine Forest is a lethal duty, even for the undead. After finding themselves ambushed and pinned down by Scourge prowling the pine woods, Deathstalkers Rane Yorick and Quinn Yorick had to consolidate their findings into this hurried dispatch. The report summarizes unexpected levels of Scourge resistance threatening Forsaken territorial ambitions in the region. Because Quinn suffered grievous injuries during their mission, the document is entrusted to passing allies to ensure High Executor Hadrec receives word at the Sepulcher without delay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Deathstalker Report?",a="It is a field report assembled by Deathstalker Rane Yorick documenting the dangers, Scourge activities, and obstacles faced by Forsaken scouts operating within Silverpine Forest.",al={"what is this report","deathstalker report lore","what is deathstalker report"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote the report?",a="The report is written by Deathstalker Rane Yorick after tending to his injured partner, Deathstalker Quinn, following an encounter with the regional Scourge.",al={"who wrote deathstalker report","report author","who wrote it"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the report delivered to?",a="It is addressed and delivered to High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken commander stationed at the Sepulcher who oversees military operations throughout Silverpine Forest.",al={"where does report go","who gets the report","hadrec report"}},{q="Why is the report so urgently needed?",a="High Executor Hadrec had undercalculated the sheer volume of Scourge presence in Silverpine Forest. The report outlines these hostile forces, providing vital data needed to protect Forsaken occupation efforts.",al={"why is it important","why does hadrec need it","what info is inside"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The report highlights the ruthless efficiency and persistent danger facing the Deathstalkers, the intelligence-gathering arm that secures Lordaeron's frontiers for Sylvanas.",["class:Rogue"]="Carrying intelligence gathered by seasoned Deathstalkers offers a direct glimpse into the covert reconnaissance work that keeps the Forsaken military functional."},kw={"deathstalker report","hadrec","quinn","rane yorick","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:449","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:1886","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Deathstalker Report","The Deathstalkers' Report"}}
E["item:deliah-s-ring"] = {t="item",n="Deliah's Ring",z="silverpine",s="Deliah's Ring is an engraved piece of jewelry recovered from a corpse pile amassed by the Rot Hide gnolls in Silverpine Forest. Bearing the inscription 'For Deliah', the keepsake offers a grim trail tracing back to a plague victim stolen from Tirisfal's mass graves.",h="Deliah's Ring is an engraved piece of jewelry recovered from a corpse pile amassed by the Rot Hide gnolls in...",sec={{t="A Keepsake in the Mire",b="Discovered upon the pockmarked, relatively fresh hand of a corpse among gnoll mounds in Silverpine Forest, the ring is inscribed simply: 'For Deliah'. The discovery reveals that the local Rot Hide gnolls are not merely scavenging battlefields—they are actively raiding the mass graves of Tirisfal Glades and ferrying human and Forsaken corpses south to Fenris Isle for their own vile purposes.",sp=0},{t="Ties to Brill",b="When brought before the Forsaken authorities, High Executor Hadrec directs the artifact toward Brill, where Magistrate Sevren maintains records of recent deceased. Sevren confirms that Deliah lived in Brill before succumbing to the plague, where she was laid to rest before body-snatchers exhumed her remains. Tracing the ring uncovers the lingering grief of those she left behind, testing whether mortal devotion can survive the transition into undeath.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Deliah's Ring found?",a="The ring is discovered during investigations into the Rot Hide gnoll mounds in northern Silverpine Forest, resting on the hand of an unwrapped plague victim among the scavenged dead.",al={"where to find deliahs ring","deliah ring location","how do you get deliahs ring"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Deliah?",a="Deliah was a former resident of Brill who died of the plague. Her body was interred in the local mass graves before being stolen by Rot Hide gnolls and dragged into Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is deliah","deliah lore","deliah of brill"},it="people"},{q="Why did the Rot Hide gnolls have her body?",a="The Scourge-aligned Rot Hide gnolls have been pillaging the communal graves in Tirisfal Glades, stockpiling corpses and ferrying them toward their stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"why gnolls stealing bodies","rot hide corpse stealing","what are gnolls doing with corpses"},it="motive"},{q="What is the inscription on the ring?",a="The interior of the band is engraved with the words 'For Deliah', indicating it was a personal gift from a lover or husband prior to her death.",al={"ring engraving","what does the ring say","for deliah ring"}},{q="What is Deliah's Ring?",a="Deliah's Ring is an engraved piece of personal jewelry found on the hand of a deceased woman among the Rot Hide gnolls in Silverpine Forest. Inscribed simply with \"For Deliah,\" it is a rare, lingering token of affection and life from Lordaeron before the plague took hold.",al={"what is deliahs ring","deliah's ring lore","about deliahs ring"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why is Deliah's Ring wanted?",a="High Executor Hadrec values the ring as vital evidence that the Rot Hide gnolls are raiding mass plague graves in Tirisfal Glades for fresh corpses. Beyond that military clue, the ring serves to identify the dead woman through Brill's records, offering a chance to discover who once loved her and whether that mourner still exists.",al={"why keep deliahs ring","who wants deliahs ring","why turn in deliah's ring"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The ring illustrates the cold reality of Forsaken existence: mortal attachments often rot away alongside flesh, though a rare few still cling to the memory of who they loved in life."},kw={"brill","deliah","deliah's ring","engraved ring","fenris isle","hadrec","magistrate sevren","rot hide gnolls"},rel={"quest:439","quest:440","quest:441","quest:530","npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:brill"},src={"Deliah's Ring","Rot Hide Clues","The Engraved Ring"}}
E["item:essence-of-nightlash"] = {t="item",n="Essence of Nightlash",z="silverpine",s="The Essence of Nightlash is the lingering magical remnant collected from the defeated banshee Nightlash at the Dead Fields. It serves as irrefutable proof for High Executor Hadrec that the Scourge force bolstering the local rot hide gnolls has been broken.",h="The Essence of Nightlash is the lingering magical remnant collected from the defeated banshee Nightlash at...",sec={{t="The Banshee of the Dead Fields",b="At an abandoned farmstead in northern Silverpine known as the Dead Fields, packs of undead rot hide gnolls have entrenched themselves under Scourge command. Initial Forsaken assaults were repeatedly broken not by the feral gnolls, but by their spectral commander: the banshee Nightlash. Calling upon wailing magics, she reinforced the gnoll lines and routed the forces sent from the Sepulcher. Slaying her dissolves her incorporeal form into dust, leaving behind a crystalline, magical essence that represents her permanent dissolution.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Scourge Defeat",b="Because banshees leave behind no corporeal corpse, the Essence of Nightlash is the only physical evidence that the malevolent spirit has been destroyed. High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher requires this essence to verify that the Scourge's local foothold has collapsed, allowing the Forsaken to finally secure their northern perimeter and suppress the rot hide threat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Essence of Nightlash?",a="It is the crystallized dust left behind when the Scourge banshee Nightlash is defeated. Since spirits have no physical bodies, this magical residue serves as proof of her demise.",al={"essence of nightlash","nightlash dust","what is nightlash essence"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Nightlash?",a="Nightlash is a banshee allied with the Scourge who leads and reinforces the rot hide gnolls operating out of the Dead Fields in northern Silverpine.",al={"who is nightlash","nightlash lore","banshee nightlash"}},{q="Who wants this essence?",a="High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher asks Forsaken champions to retrieve it to prove that the banshee routing his frontline assaults has been neutralized.",al={"who needs nightlash essence","who turn in essence","high executor hadrec"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the gnolls working with a banshee?",a="The rot hide gnolls in the Dead Fields have succumbed to the undead plague, making them thralls to the Scourge. Nightlash was dispatched to oversee them and lend magical support against Forsaken patrols.",al={"gnolls and scourge","rot hide scourge","why gnolls with banshee"}},{q="Where does the Essence of Nightlash come from?",a="The essence comes from the banshee Nightlash herself. When you confront and destroy her at the Dead Fields, her spectral form collapses and her essence turns into dust, leaving behind the remnant you collect.",al={"essence of nightlash origin","how to get essence of nightlash","where does essence of nightlash drop"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken soldiers view eliminating banshees like Nightlash as vital work; as former victims of Scourge domination, destroying agents of the Lich King is central to securing Lordaeron for their own people.",["class:Mage"]="Arcanists and scholars often examine the residue of destroyed banshees to study how spectral undead tether necrotic magic to the physical world."},kw={"banshee","dead fields","dust","essence","hadrec","nightlash","rot hide","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:437","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:dead-field","subzone:sepulcher","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken","topic:gnoll"},src={"Essence of Nightlash","The Dead Fields (quest)"}}
E["item:glutton-shackle"] = {t="item",n="Glutton Shackle",z="silverpine",s="Glutton Shackles are enchanted restraints worn by Moonrage Glutton worgen in Silverpine Forest. Crafted by the mad archmage Arugal, these bands channel magic to bolster his otherwise flawed sorcery and sustain his cursed lupine creations.",h="Glutton Shackles are enchanted restraints worn by Moonrage Glutton worgen in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Crutch for Weak Sorcery",b="To the trained mages of the Forsaken, the feral worgen infesting Silverpine are not merely savage monstrosities—they are evidence of gross arcane ineptitude. Dalar Dawnweaver, an accomplished arcanist stationed at the Sepulcher, holds nothing but contempt for Archmage Arugal, deeming him an incompetent hack unworthy of the Kirin Tor. Dawnweaver discovered that Arugal relied on enchanted relics to compensate for his fragile spells. The Glutton Shackles, worn by the heavy Moonrage Gluttons wandering northern Silverpine, act as magical anchors that reinforce the curse binding the beasts.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for Forsaken Countermeasures",b="Because Arugal bound raw enchantments directly into these heavy iron bands, they retain residual magical energy even after their wearers are slain. Dawnweaver demands these shackles from Forsaken agents to study their construction and siphon their magical reserves. By analyzing the crude enchantments embedded in the metal, the Forsaken hope to unravel the mysteries of the worgen curse and orchestrate the downfall of the beastmaster entrenched in Shadowfang Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Glutton Shackle?",a="A Glutton Shackle is an enchanted iron restraint worn by Moonrage Glutton worgen in Silverpine Forest. Created by Archmage Arugal, these bands infuse their wearers with magical reinforcement to shore up his flawed spells.",al={"what are glutton shackles","glutton shackle lore","worgen cuffs"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Glutton Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver needs the shackles to analyze Arugal's crude enchantments and siphon their lingering magical energy. By understanding the items Arugal used to stabilize his beasts, the Forsaken can better counteract his magic.",al={"why collect shackles","dalar dawnweaver quest","shackles for sepulcher"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who makes these shackles?",a="They were enchanted by Archmage Arugal, a former wizard of Dalaran who summoned the worgen to fight the Scourge and eventually lost his mind, binding his creations to his will with magical trinkets.",al={"who made the shackles","arugal shackles","where did shackles come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the creatures wearing these shackles found?",a="Moonrage Gluttons roam the woods and abandoned farmsteads of central and northern Silverpine Forest, often lurking in packs alongside other corrupted Moonrage worgen.",al={"where do gluttons spawn","moonrage glutton location","silverpine worgen shackles"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages will appreciate Dalar Dawnweaver's biting critique of Arugal's shoddy technique, as using physical enchanted crutches to stabilize simple transmutation and summoning spells is seen as a sign of mediocre wizardry.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken agents view the collection of these shackles as an essential step toward neutralizing the worgen threat that encroaches directly upon the borders of the Sepulcher."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","glutton shackle","moonrage glutton","sepulcher","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"quest:99","item:darksoul-shackle","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:dalaran","quest:421"},src={"Glutton Shackle","Arugal's Folly (2)"}}
E["item:head-of-grimson"] = {t="item",n="Head of Grimson",z="silverpine",s="The Head of Grimson is the severed trophy taken from Grimson the Pale, the corrupted overseer of the Deep Elem Mine in Silverpine Forest. Brought to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher, it serves as physical proof that the mine's leadership has been eliminated. Securing the mine allows the Forsaken to seize valuable mineral wealth to fuel Varimathras's military campaigns.",h="The Head of Grimson is the severed trophy taken from Grimson the Pale, the corrupted overseer of the Deep...",sec={{t="Securing the Deep Elem Mine",b="While Dalar Dawnweaver studies Archmage Arugal's shadowy enchantments from the safety of the Sepulcher, Forsaken scouts known as Darkstalkers identified a strategic threat brewing in the southeastern hills. Arugal's dark magic had seeped into the Deep Elem Mine, corrupting its workers and driving its overseer, Grimson the Pale, into madness. To secure the subterranean riches for Varimathras's forces, Dawnweaver dispatched champions to cut down Grimson and return with his severed head as undeniable confirmation of the mine's liberation from rogue magics.",sp=0},{t="A Trophy for the Dreadlord",b="For the Forsaken, grim trophies of war carry pragmatic weight. Claiming the head of Grimson ensures that the subterranean workforce in the Deep Elem Mine is entirely broken, ending any lingering allegiance to Arugal's twisted reign. With Grimson eliminated, the rich mineral veins within the mine can be extracted and reforged into weapons and armor, sustaining the ongoing Forsaken advance across Silverpine Forest and the neighboring reaches of Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Grimson the Pale?",a="Grimson the Pale was the overseer of the Deep Elem Mine located in the southeastern hills of Silverpine Forest. Exposed to Archmage Arugal's spreading shadow magic, Grimson and his fellow miners fell under its dark sway, transforming the mine into a corrupted stronghold until the Forsaken intervened.",al={"who is grimson","grimson the pale lore","grimson background"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Grimson's head?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver needs concrete proof that the corrupted foreman has been permanently eliminated. Varimathras desires the Deep Elem Mine's mineral wealth for the Forsaken war effort, and killing Grimson breaks the resistance of the corrupted miners holding the tunnels.",al={"why dalar wants head","head of grimson purpose","why take head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Deep Elem Mine located?",a="The Deep Elem Mine is situated in the hills to the southeast of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. It serves as a vital mineral cache contested by the Forsaken and the corrupted remnants subjected to Arugal's magic.",al={"where is deep elem mine","grimson location","mine location silverpine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Varimathras play in this task?",a="Varimathras serves as the military overseer directing Forsaken expansion across Lordaeron from the Undercity. Securing the resources of the Deep Elem Mine directly serves his strategic goals, providing raw materials to fuel his growing war machine in Silverpine.",al={"varimathras role","why does varimathras want mine","varimathras silverpine"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Head of Grimson?",a="The Head of Grimson is the severed head of Grimson the Pale, taken as proof of his death. Once an ordinary overseer, Grimson was warped by the dark magical taint unleashed across Silverpine by Archmage Arugal. Claiming his head marks the end of his command over the Deep Elem Mine, securing undeniable evidence that the mine's corrupted leadership has fallen.",al={"head of grimson","grimson head","what is grimson's head"},it="item",add=true,nx={6}},{q="Where does the Head of Grimson come from?",a="This grim trophy comes directly from the Deep Elem Mine, located in the hills southeast of the Sepulcher. It is severed from the shoulders of Grimson the Pale, the mine's tainted foreman. Grimson succumbed to the wild magics leaking from Pyrewood and Shadowfang Keep, holding the mine until brought down on the orders of Dalar Dawnweaver.",al={"where to get head of grimson","who drops head of grimson","head of grimson origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Claiming the mine fulfills the strategic mandates of Undercity high command, proving the Forsaken's resolve to reclaim Lordaeron's vital infrastructure from maddened remnants.",["profession:Mining"]="Deep Elem Mine represents one of Silverpine's prime mineral claims, now cleared of its maddened overseer so raw ore can flow into Horde supply lines."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","deep elem mine","grimson the pale","head of grimson","sepulcher","silverpine forest","varimathras"},rel={"quest:99","subzone:deep-elem-mine","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","subzone:sepulcher","npc:varimathras","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","quest:421"},src={"Head of Grimson","Arugal's Folly (3)"}}
E["item:ivar-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Ivar's Head",z="silverpine",s="Ivar's Head is the gruesome proof of the destruction of the ravenous ghoul Ivar the Foul in Silverpine Forest. It is sought by the Deathstalker Rane Yorick to ensure safe recovery for his wounded brother Quinn.",h="Ivar's Head is the gruesome proof of the destruction of the ravenous ghoul Ivar the Foul in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Severed Threat",b="While scouting northern Silverpine Forest on the orders of High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick were ambushed at an abandoned farmstead by a feral ghoul known as Ivar the Foul. Though the brothers managed to fend off the fiend, Quinn was severely mauled in the confrontation. Stranded at the ruined farm while his brother recovered, Rane could not safely leave Quinn unattended to complete their mission. Severing Ivar's head provides definitive proof that the beast will never terrorize the estate again, granting Quinn the necessary time to recuperate under Rane's watchful eye.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Whose head is this?",a="The head belonged to Ivar the Foul, a savage ghoul haunting the abandoned farmstead known as the Ivar Patch in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is ivar","ivar head identity","what is ivar"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick want Ivar's head?",a="Rane requires physical proof that Ivar is destroyed. His brother Quinn was badly mauled by the creature and needs time to heal without fear of another ambush before they can report back to High Executor Hadrec.",al={"why rane wants head","ivar head turn in","why kill ivar"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where was Ivar the Foul found?",a="Ivar the Foul lurks inside the dilapidated barn at the Ivar Patch, watching and waiting for the wounded Deathstalkers to let their guard down.",al={"ivar location","where is ivar"},it="place"},{q="Where does Ivar's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken directly from the corpse of Ivar the Foul, a vicious ghoul lurking within the ruined barn at the Ivar Patch in Silverpine Forest. It is not an artifact or crafted item, but the physical trophy severed from an undead monster to guarantee he has truly been destroyed.",al={"origin of ivar's head","where did ivar's head come from","who made ivar's head"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken scouts, wild ghouls are mindless liabilities that disrupt military reconnaissance and threaten the nascent security of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Eliminating rogue Scourge remnants like Ivar protects traveling Horde couriers moving through northern Silverpine toward the Sepulcher."},kw={"deathstalkers","ivar patch","ivar the foul","ivar's head","quinn yorick","rane yorick","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:425","subzone:ivar-patch","quest:430","quest:428","quest:429","npc:high-executor-hadrec","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Ivar's Head","Ivar the Foul (quest)"}}
E["item:johaan-s-findings"] = {t="item",n="Johaan's Findings",z="silverpine",s="Johaan's Findings is a bundle of research documents penned by Apothecary Johaan in Brill. Entrusted to a courier heading south, these notes convey recent alchemical developments in Tirisfal Glades to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",h="Johaan's Findings is a bundle of research documents penned by Apothecary Johaan in Brill.",sec={{t="Apothecary Correspondence",b="The Royal Apothecary Society operates under relentless pressure from Lady Sylvanas Windrunner to engineer a New Plague capable of destroying both the living and the Scourge. Because researchers are scattered across Lordaeron's contested ruins, maintaining a flow of data between outposts is vital. Apothecary Johaan compiles his local testing notes in Brill and dispatches them southward to Apothecary Renferrel, who directs society efforts from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. These records represent one small piece of the Society's collective effort to hone their lethal brews.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Johaan's Findings?",a="It is a package of alchemical notes and research compiled by Apothecary Johaan in Brill. The papers detail his recent testing and experiments within Tirisfal Glades.",al={"johaans findings","what are johaans findings","johaan research papers"},it="identity"},{q="Who is supposed to receive this item?",a="The findings are addressed to Apothecary Renferrel, a senior member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Sepulcher in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"who gets johaans findings","where do i take johaans findings","renferrel delivery"},it="target"},{q="Why is this research being shared between apothecaries?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society relies on shared knowledge among its dispersed researchers to accelerate their work. Sylvanas Windrunner demands rapid development of the New Plague, making it essential that researchers in Silverpine stay updated on breakthroughs made back in Tirisfal.",al={"why share findings","purpose of johaans findings","royal apothecary society research"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wrote these documents?",a="Apothecary Johaan, an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society based near the gallows in Brill. He conducts experimental testing on local specimens to advance Forsaken alchemical goals.",al={"who is apothecary johaan","who wrote this","apothecary johaan"},it="origin"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="These findings reflect the singular, driving ambition of the Royal Apothecary Society: delivering the New Plague promised to the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="Carrying research southward marks a traveler's graduation from the familiar grounds of Tirisfal Glades into the darker conflicts of Silverpine Forest."},kw={"apothecary johaan","apothecary renferrel","brill","johaan","johaan's findings","new plague","royal apothecary society","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:445","npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:brill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Johaan's Findings","Delivery to Silverpine Forest"}}
E["item:podrig-s-order"] = {t="item",n="Podrig's Order",z="silverpine",s="Podrig's Order is a written military requisition penned by Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher. It requests a fresh shipment of weapons from Undercity merchant Gordon Wendham to keep Silverpine's Forsaken garrison properly armed.",h="Podrig's Order is a written military requisition penned by Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="Arming the Sepulcher",b="Silverpine Forest is a precarious frontier for the Forsaken, caught between encroaching Scourge, feral beasts, and other lurking threats. After an equipment inventory conducted by Deathguard Podrig on the orders of Executor Hadrec, the Sepulcher's stores were found mostly adequate but desperately low on replacement weapons. This official dispatch details the needed blades and arms to sustain the Deathguards holding the outpost.",sp=0},{t="Dispatch via Bat Handler",b="Because weapons cannot be forged easily amidst the damp crypts of Silverpine, the request is directed to Gordon Wendham, a weapon dealer located in the bustling Trade Quarter of the Undercity. To expedite the order, couriers carry the document directly to bat master Karos Razok, taking advantage of Forsaken flight paths to secure a swift resupply from the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written in Podrig's Order?",a="It is an official requisition listing replacement weaponry needed by the Deathguards stationed at the Sepulcher after routine field losses.",al={"what does the order say","contents of podrig's order","podrig order details"}},{q="Who wrote Podrig's Order?",a="It was drafted by Deathguard Podrig under the instruction of Executor Hadrec, following an inventory check of the Sepulcher's armory.",al={"who wrote it","author of podrig order"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives the order?",a="It is meant for Gordon Wendham, a weapon dealer conducting business in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity.",al={"who gets the order","where does podrig order go","recipient of podrig order"},it="target"},{q="Why does the Sepulcher need new weapons?",a="Constant skirmishes against the Scourge and other hostile forces in Silverpine Forest frequently result in broken or lost equipment among the defending Deathguards.",al={"why need weapons","sepulcher weapon shortage"},it="motive"},{q="What is Podrig's Order?",a="Podrig's Order is an official Forsaken requisition document written to secure fresh armaments for the outpost at the Sepulcher. Penned by Podrig on behalf of Executor Hadrec, the scroll lists replacement weapons needed by the garrison's Deathguards to survive their ongoing clashes against the Scourge and other terrors lurking in Silverpine Forest.",al={"what is podrigs order","podrig order item","podrig requisition"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Gordon Wendham need Podrig's Order?",a="As a weapons vendor in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, Gordon Wendham requires the formal requisition to verify and fulfill the garrison's supply request. Without this verified manifest, the Sepulcher cannot receive the necessary shipment of blades and gear to resupply its front-line Deathguards.",al={"why does gordon wendham want the order","why take podrigs order to undercity","why is podrig order needed"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The requisition highlights the logistical lifeline between the Undercity and outer outposts like the Sepulcher, ensuring the Dark Lady's soldiers remain properly armed against the Scourge.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Forged weapons are vital out on the front lines, where ongoing combat constantly drains garrison supplies."},kw={"gordon wendham","hadrec","karos razok","podrig","podrig's order","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"quest:6321","quest:6323","subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok","npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","zone:silverpine"},src={"Podrig's Order","Supplying the Sepulcher","Ride to the Undercity (Classic)"}}
E["item:pyrewood-shackle"] = {t="item",n="Pyrewood Shackle",z="silverpine",s="Pyrewood Shackles are enchanted restraints worn by the beleaguered inhabitants of Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest. Imbued with the strange magic of Archmage Arugal, these bands are linked to the eerie curse that transforms ordinary townsfolk into ravenous worgen once night falls.",h="Pyrewood Shackles are enchanted restraints worn by the beleaguered inhabitants of Pyrewood Village in...",sec={{t="Arugal's Binding Magic",b="The cursed village of Pyrewood holds an unsettling secret: by day, its residents carry on ordinary lives appearing as typical humans, but the setting sun twists them into feral Moonrage worgen. Archmage Arugal bound these villagers in enchanted shackles as part of his twisted experiments with worgen sorcery. Dalar Dawnweaver, an arcane researcher stationed at the Sepulcher for the Forsaken, studies these shackles to decode the enchantments driving this dual existence. By gathering and analyzing the lingering energy on the bands, Dawnweaver seeks a deeper understanding of Arugal's magic in hopes of unraveling the mad archmage's hold over the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Pyrewood Shackles used for?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher requests these shackles to study their enchantments. By siphoning their magic, he hopes to unravel Archmage Arugal's spells and find a way to dismantle the archmage's influence in Silverpine Forest.",al={"pyrewood shackles use","why gather shackles","dalar dawnweaver shackles"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Who carries these shackles?",a="The shackles are carried by the cursed residents of Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest, worn during their daytime human guise and their nighttime transformation into Moonrage worgen.",al={"who drops pyrewood shackles","shackle source","where to find pyrewood shackles"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the villagers transform at night?",a="Archmage Arugal subjected Pyrewood's populace to reckless magical experiments and enchantments. The shackles maintain an enchantment that allows them to appear as ordinary humans during daylight, only to reveal their feral worgen forms when darkness falls.",al={"why pyrewood turns into worgen","pyrewood village curse","pyrewood werewolf secret"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage residing at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He actively studies the arcane anomalies left behind by Archmage Arugal, focusing on dissecting and breaking the archmage's twisted curses.",al={"dalar dawnweaver","who is dalar"},it="people"},{q="What is a Pyrewood Shackle?",a="A Pyrewood Shackle is an enchanted fetter bound to the unfortunate residents of Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest. Imbued with the strange, reckless sorcery of the mad mage Archmage Arugal, these shackles play a direct role in binding the townsfolk to his will and masking the dark curse that afflicts them.",al={"pyrewood shackle","what are pyrewood shackles","pyrewood shackles"},it="identity",add=true,nx={6}},{q="Where does a Pyrewood Shackle come from, and who made it?",a="These enchanted shackles were forged and placed upon the villagers by Archmage Arugal, the rogue Dalaran wizard who took residence in Shadowfang Keep. Arugal cast the shackles on Pyrewood's peasants as part of his twisted enchantments, keeping them under his sway while hiding their lupine transformation beneath a daylight illusion of ordinary human life.",al={"who made pyrewood shackles","pyrewood shackle origin","where do shackles come from"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Pyrewood Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver, an ambitious Forsaken mage conducting research at the Sepulcher, seeks these enchanted shackles to study Arugal's magic. By siphoning their residual energy, Dalar hopes to unravel the bizarre enchantment causing the villagers to appear human by day and turn into ravenous Moonrage worgen after dusk, seeking ultimately to dismantle Arugal's spells.",al={"why gather pyrewood shackles","who needs pyrewood shackles","pyrewood shackle purpose"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken scholars at the Sepulcher view Arugal's rampant sorcery as a major threat to their borders, making the collection of these enchanted bindings critical to neutralizing Shadowfang Keep's influence.",["class:Mage"]="Mages studying Arugal's handiwork will recognize the reckless application of transmutation and binding magic woven into ordinary steel."},kw={"arugal","dawnweaver","moonrage","pyrewood","sepulcher","shackle","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"quest:99","subzone:pyrewood-village","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:worgen","topic:human"},src={"Pyrewood Shackle","Arugal's Folly (4)"}}
E["item:quinn-s-potion"] = {t="item",n="Quinn's Potion",z="silverpine",s="Quinn's Potion is a restorative draught concocted by Apothecary Renferrel in the Sepulcher. It is brewed to stabilize and revitalize the wounded Deathstalker Quinn Yorick following a disastrous scouting patrol in Silverpine Forest.",h="Quinn's Potion is a restorative draught concocted by Apothecary Renferrel in the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="Renferrel's Cure",b="After Deathstalker Quinn Yorick was severely battered and incapacitated near the Ivar Patch, word reached the Royal Apothecary Society at the Sepulcher. Apothecary Renferrel hastily compounded this specialized draught to facilitate Quinn's recovery. While Renferrel rarely lets minor field casualties distract him from his grander, more sinister research for Lady Sylvanas, he provided the restorative to get the injured scout back on his feet and capable of travel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Quinn's Potion used for?",a="The potion is formulated to aid in the recovery of Deathstalker Quinn Yorick, who lies injured in the northern woods of Silverpine Forest. Drinking it restores enough of his vitality to allow him to travel again.",al={"quinn potion purpose","what does quinn potion do","why brew quinn potion"},it="purpose"},{q="Who brewed this potion?",a="Apothecary Renferrel, an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in the crypts of the Sepulcher, concocted the draught.",al={"who made quinn's potion","who brewed it","renferrel potion"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the potion need to be delivered?",a="It must be carried north of the Sepulcher to Quinn Yorick, who is sheltering near the farmstead known as the Ivar Patch.",al={"where do i take the potion","quinn location","quinn yorick spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was Quinn Yorick in need of a potion?",a="Quinn was part of a Deathstalker patrol scouting the region that suffered brutal casualties from local beast attacks and feral worgen, leaving him incapacitated and stranded at the Ivar Patch.",al={"why is quinn hurt","what happened to quinn yorick","quinn injured"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Quinn's Potion?",a="It is a restorative concoction brewed by Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher. Formulated specifically to aid the injured scout Quinn Yorick, the draught provides the strength he needs to recover from his wounds and regain enough mobility to travel.",al={"quinns potion","what is this potion","what is quinn's draught"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society rarely wastes effort on simple field remedies unless it directly preserves Forsaken scouts vital to securing Silverpine's borders."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","deathstalker","ivar patch","quinn yorick","quinn's potion","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"quest:430","npc:quinn-yorick","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:ivar-patch","subzone:sepulcher","quest:428","quest:429","quest:425"},src={"Quinn's Potion","Return to Quinn"}}
E["item:remedy-of-arugal"] = {t="item",n="Remedy of Arugal",z="silverpine",s="The Remedy of Arugal is an incantation penned by the mage Arugal during his early experiments with worgen magic. Left behind in a dilapidated farmhouse in Silverpine Forest, the spell is sought by Dalar Dawnweaver to unravel the sorcerer's dark work.",h="The Remedy of Arugal is an incantation penned by the mage Arugal during his early experiments with worgen...",sec={{t="A Mage's Leftovers",b="Before seizing Shadowfang Keep, Archmage Arugal took refuge at an abandoned wheat farm north of the river bridge in Silverpine Forest. There, amidst forgotten farm tools and rotting floorboards, he documented his strange arts in a set of dusty spellbooks. The scroll titled the Remedy of Arugal is among these notes, outlining early methods and magical formulations he devised while dabbling in the dangerous transmutations that cursed the local populace.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Scrutiny",b="Dalar Dawnweaver, an accomplished Forsaken spellcaster operating from the Sepulcher, holds little respect for Arugal's pedigree, dismissing the former Dalaran wizard's intellect as fragile and transparent. Even so, Dawnweaver recognizes the urgent need to understand the exact mechanics behind the worgen curse. By recovering the Remedy of Arugal, Forsaken agents provide Dawnweaver with the foundational arcana required to counter Arugal's spreading menace and secure Silverpine for Lady Sylvanas.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Remedy of Arugal?",a="It is a magical formula written down by the renegade mage Arugal. Rather than a curative potion, it is a written spell containing the arcane techniques he used when he first started experimenting with worgen magic in Silverpine Forest.",al={"what is remedy of arugal","arugal remedy item","remedy spell"},it="identity"},{q="Where was the Remedy left behind?",a="Arugal left it within a set of dusty spellbooks on the upper floor of an abandoned wheat farm, located just north of the bridge that crosses the river in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to find remedy of arugal","remedy of arugal location","farm spellbook"},it="place"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want this spell?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver seeks to analyze the specific magic Arugal employed so that the Forsaken can develop counters against it, hoping to turn the sorcerer's own methods against him to secure the region.",al={"why does dalar want the remedy","dalar dawnweaver remedy"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who guards the spellbooks at the farm?",a="The farm is infested with Arugal's lupine thralls. When someone attempts to disturb the dusty spellbooks on the second floor, a Moonrage Darkrunner leaps from the shadows to defend its master's belongings.",al={"what attacks at the farm","spellbook ambush"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Remedy of Arugal come from, and who made it?",a="The Remedy of Arugal is an incantation penned by Archmage Arugal himself during his early days in Silverpine Forest. After his schemes began to unfurl, he resided briefly at a wheat farm north of the main river bridge, leaving behind dusty spellbooks containing his research.",al={"who made remedy of arugal","remedy of arugal origin","where did remedy of arugal come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages will share Dalar Dawnweaver's professional disdain for Arugal's clumsy, reckless dabbling, yet recognize the danger inherent in unchecked summoning arcana.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing this spell is an early, vital step in pushing back against the feral worgen threatening the borders of Silverpine Forest."},kw={"arugal","arugal's folly","dalar dawnweaver","dusty spellbooks","moonrage","remedy of arugal","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:99","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","quest:1886","quest:421"},src={"Remedy of Arugal","Arugal's Folly"}}
E["item:rot-hide-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Rot Hide Ichor",z="silverpine",s="Rot Hide Ichor is a foul bodily fluid harvested from the undead Rot Hide gnolls infesting Fenris Isle in Lordamere Lake. Apothecary Renferrel collects samples of the substance at the Sepulcher to uncover the origin of the gnolls' corruption and devise a strategy against them.",h="Rot Hide Ichor is a foul bodily fluid harvested from the undead Rot Hide gnolls infesting Fenris Isle in...",sec={{t="A Plague in the Blood",b="The Rot Hide gnolls of Fenris Isle are not ordinary wild beasts; they are visibly decomposed and twisted by unnatural blight. Rather than normal blood, their veins pump a noxious ichor that sustains their animated flesh. The Royal Apothecary Society suspects that this fluid holds the secret to how the pack was corrupted and who commands them from within the ruined keep of Fenris Isle.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Research",b="Apothecary Renferrel gathers vials of this ichor to analyze its properties at the Sepulcher. By isolating the chemical and magical components fueling the gnolls, the Forsaken hope to pinpoint vulnerabilities before committing troops to a full-scale assault across Lordamere Lake.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Rot Hide Ichor come from?",a="It is gathered from the bodies of the Rot Hide gnolls dwelling across Fenris Isle, located in Lordamere Lake east of Silverpine Forest's mainland.",al={"where to get rot hide ichor","how to find rot hide ichor","gnoll ichor location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want this ichor?",a="Renferrel seeks to dissect the strange fluid to discover what corrupted the gnolls and identify any physical or alchemical weaknesses the Forsaken can exploit before attacking the island.",al={"why does renferrel need ichor","renferrel quest reason","purpose of rot hide ichor"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the Rot Hide gnolls Scourge?",a="They are undead gnolls warped by plague, but the Forsaken are actively investigating exactly who or what created them and commands their presence on Fenris Isle.",al={"are rot hides scourge","who controls rot hides","what are rot hide gnolls"},it="identity"},{q="Do all gnolls have this ichor?",a="No. The fluid is unique to the Rot Hide pack, whose flesh and blood have been corrupted by foul necromantic blights.",al={"do all gnolls drop ichor","normal gnoll blood"}},{q="What is Rot Hide Ichor?",a="Rot Hide Ichor is a strange, unnatural fluid that courses through the bodies of the Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle. It is not ordinary blood; the Royal Apothecary Society believes this tainted substance is directly responsible for the gnolls' twisted, undead-like nature and heightened resilience.",al={"what is rot hide ichor","rot hide fluid","what is the ichor"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, studying the ichor is vital military intelligence to secure Silverpine's eastern flank and advance the Royal Apothecary Society's mastery over plague science."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","fenris isle","lordamere lake","rot hide gnolls","rot hide ichor","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:443","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:fenris-isle","quest:442","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:decrepit-ferry","topic:gnoll","zone:silverpine"},src={"Rot Hide Ichor","Rot Hide Ichor (quest)"}}
E["item:rune-inscribed-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Rune-Inscribed Pendant",z="silverpine",s="The Rune-Inscribed Pendant is a magical trinket recovered from Dalaran supply shipments destined for Ambermill. Prized by the Kirin Tor, these pendants serve as conduits for channeling potent arcane energies.",h="The Rune-Inscribed Pendant is a magical trinket recovered from Dalaran supply shipments destined for...",sec={{t="Kirin Tor Relic",b="Discovered among crates of cartographic supplies bound for the Dalaran enclave at Ambermill, this pendant bears intricate arcane inscriptions. High-ranking wizards of the Kirin Tor frequently employ such artifacts to focus and amplify their spellcasting. The presence of numerous channeled pendants moving into the region immediately draws the suspicion of the Forsaken at the Sepulcher, signaling an impending project of immense magical power.",sp=0},{t="A Clue to Ambermill's Plans",b="When brought to the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister recognizes the threat posed by the Dalaran wizards' fortified position, but passes the relic to Dalar Dawnweaver for deeper scrutiny. Dawnweaver identifies the pendant as a key component of the mages' operations, deducing that the Kirin Tor is stockpiling arcane focus tools to fuel substantial defensive or offensive workings shielded behind Ambermill's borders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Pendant used for?",a="Wizards of the Kirin Tor use the pendant to channel and direct significant flows of magical energy. It serves as an arcane focus for complex spellcraft rather than simple decoration.",al={"what does the pendant do","pendant purpose","rune pendant use"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did this pendant come from?",a="It is intercepted from supply shipments bound for Ambermill in Silverpine Forest, where Kirin Tor remnants have heavily fortified themselves.",al={"where do i find the pendant","pendant origin","where was it found"},it="origin"},{q="Who analyzes the pendant at the Sepulcher?",a="After Shadow Priest Allister briefly inspects it alongside captured maps, he sends it to Dalar Dawnweaver, an arcane specialist at the Sepulcher who recognizes Kirin Tor handiwork.",al={"who studies the pendant","who wants the pendant","dalar pendant"},it="target"},{q="Why are the Forsaken concerned about it?",a="The shipment of large quantities of channeling pendants suggests the Kirin Tor at Ambermill are preparing a massive magical undertaking, threatening the Forsaken grip on Silverpine Forest.",al={"why do forsaken care","ambermill threat","why is the pendant dangerous"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Pendant?",a="It is an arcane artifact crafted and utilized by the powerful magi of Dalaran. Frequently used by the Kirin Tor to focus and channel tremendous magical energies, such pendants are conduits of potent arcane power rather than simple ornaments.",al={"what is rune inscribed pendant","rune pendant identity","what is this dalaran pendant"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Mages readily recognize Kirin Tor craftsmanship; the runes carved into the pendant are designed to stabilize volatile currents when channeling high-order spells.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken guarding Silverpine Forest, intercepted Dalaran focuses like this pendant provide vital intelligence on human resistance gathering behind Ambermill's walls."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran","kirin tor","pendant","rune-inscribed pendant","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:478","quest:481","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine"},src={"Rune-Inscribed Pendant","Maps and Runes","Dalar's Analysis"}}
E["item:thule-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Thule's Head",z="silverpine",s="Thule's Head is the grisly proof demanded by the Forsaken to confirm the demise of Thule Ravenclaw, commander of the Scourge forces on Fenris Isle. Bringing this macabre trophy back to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher solidifies the Forsaken's hold on Silverpine Forest.",h="Thule's Head is the grisly proof demanded by the Forsaken to confirm the demise of Thule Ravenclaw, commander...",sec={{t="Trophy of Fenris Isle",b="Fenris Isle serves as the primary bastion of the Lich King's Scourge within Silverpine Forest. From deep inside Fenris Keep, the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw directs his legions of rot hides and undead minions, directly threatening Forsaken outposts like the Sepulcher. High Executor Hadrec requires absolute certainty that this dark commander has fallen, refusing to accept any testimony short of Thule's severed head. The violent release of dark magic upon Ravenclaw's death was felt across the woods, but his head remains the physical proof the Hand requires to declare Fenris Isle broken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants Thule's Head?",a="High Executor Hadrec, commander of Forsaken military operations stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, demands Thule's Head to confirm the Scourge leader's elimination.",al={"who needs thules head","who turned in thule head to","who takes thule head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful necromancer commanding the Scourge presence on Fenris Isle. From the heart of Fenris Keep, he orchestrates attacks against the Forsaken and wields sinister enchantments like the Hex of the Ravenclaw.",al={"thule lore","who is thule","thule ravenclaw backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Forsaken demand his head specifically?",a="The Forsaken cannot afford lingering Scourge threats in Silverpine. Because necromancers are notorious for deceit and dark resurrections, High Executor Hadrec accepts nothing less than physical, irrefutable proof of Thule's total destruction.",al={"why thule head","why do they want his head"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when Thule Ravenclaw is slain?",a="Upon Thule's defeat, a violent burst of necrotic energy radiates across the region, potent enough that Forsaken scholars and apothecaries back at the Sepulcher can sense the magical shockwave from afar.",al={"what happens after thule dies","energy released thule"},sp=1},{q="Where does Thule's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken directly from the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw within the halls of Fenris Keep. Thule led the Scourge forces that seized Fenris Isle in northern Silverpine Forest, transforming the stronghold into a bastion of the undead until you cut him down.",al={"thules head origin","where do you get thules head","source of thules head"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, severing Thule's head is both a military victory and personal vengeance against the Lich King's grip on Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Eliminating Thule Ravenclaw secures the eastern borders of Silverpine Forest, shielding newly gained Horde territories from Scourge incursions."},kw={"fenris","hadrec","necromancer","ravenclaw","scourge","sepulcher","thule"},rel={"quest:442","quest:446","subzone:fenris-isle","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Thule's Head","Assault on Fenris Isle"}}
E["npc:apothecary-renferrel"] = {t="npc",n="Apothecary Renferrel",z="silverpine",s="Apothecary Renferrel is a prominent member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Tasked with advancing the Forsaken's alchemical endeavors, he coordinates extensive field research into the region's corrupted wildlife and undead threats. Travelers through Silverpine frequently assist him with gathering volatile reagents and investigating dangerous Scourge remnants.",h="Apothecary Renferrel is a prominent member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Sepulcher in...",sec={{t="The Sepulcher's Alchemist",b="Operating out of the Sepulcher, Renferrel serves as one of the Royal Apothecary Society's chief field researchers in Silverpine Forest. While Undercity houses the grand laboratories and high leadership of the society, Renferrel handles the practical, muddy work of securing native biological specimens, refining potent concoctions, and analyzing the grim ecology of Lordaeron's western border.",sp=0},{t="Investigating Rot Hide and Scourge",b="Renferrel directs much of his energy toward the Rot Hide gnolls and rogue undead infesting the region. Through blood and tissue samples, he seeks to understand the lingering touch of the plague and the necromantic forces binding local monsters. His investigations lead him into direct opposition with Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful Scourge necromancer operating near the ruins of Fenris Isle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society based in the Sepulcher, the main Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest. He studies local beasts, plague variations, and enemy forces to brew concoctions and secure the region for Queen Sylvanas.",al={"renferrel","who is renferrel","apothecary renferrel lore"},it="identity"},{q="What does Renferrel research in Silverpine?",a="He focuses on developing new plagues and venomous mixtures, known broadly as a 'Recipe for Death'. He tasks adventurers with collecting grizzly bear hearts, Rot Hide gnoll ichor, and other biological components to test and refine lethal concoctions.",al={"renferrel research","renferrel experiments","recipe for death"},it="wants"},{q="What is his connection to the Rot Hide gnolls?",a="Renferrel is fascinated by the infected, necrotic state of Silverpine's Rot Hide gnolls. By analyzing their corrupted ichor, he uncovers the necromantic hand behind their transformation, tracing their masters back to rogue Scourge forces.",al={"rot hide ichor","rot hide origins","gnolls silverpine"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Renferrel target Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Renferrel's investigation into the Rot Hide gnolls reveals that Thule Ravenclaw, a dangerous necromancer aligned with the Scourge at Fenris Isle, created them. Renferrel sends adventurers to destroy Thule and eliminate the threat to Silverpine.",al={"thule ravenclaw quest","who is thule ravenclaw","fenris keep necromancer"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Where does Renferrel send adventurers after Silverpine?",a="Once his initial research and the local threats are addressed, Renferrel directs seasoned travelers southeast to Hillsbrad Foothills, connecting the Sepulcher's frontier efforts with broader Forsaken operations in Lordaeron.",al={"after sepulcher","hillsbrad delivery","journey to hillsbrad"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is the scientific and alchemical branch of the Forsaken, founded under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Headquartered in Undercity, its researchers work tirelessly to develop new poisons, resist natural decay, and craft a plague capable of eradicating the Scourge.",al={"royal apothecary society","ras","forsaken apothecaries"}},{q="Whose side is Apothecary Renferrel on?",a="Apothecary Renferrel serves the Forsaken and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner as a sworn member of the Royal Apothecary Society. Operating under the broader banner of the Horde, his loyalty lies with Undercity's alchemical orders, dedicating his efforts to advancing the Forsaken's survival and dominance against common enemies like the Scourge and the living.",al={"renferrel faction","who does renferrel serve","is apothecary renferrel horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Apothecary Renferrel here in Silverpine Forest?",a="Stationed at the Sepulcher, Renferrel carries out vital alchemical field research for the Royal Apothecary Society. Silverpine Forest provides him access to feral beasts, dangerous Scourge activity, and tainted local threats like the Rot Hide gnolls—all vital subjects for harvesting potent ingredients and brewing new toxins.",al={"why is renferrel in the sepulcher","renferrel location why","why is apothecary renferrel here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Renferrel represents the pragmatic, ruthless survival mindset of the Forsaken, weaponizing Lordaeron's native flora and fauna to build a secure future for the freed undead.",["faction:Horde"]="While orcs and tauren may balk at the gruesome nature of his biological experiments, Renferrel's intelligence gathering against the Scourge helps keep Horde territories safe from northern incursions."},kw={"apothecary","recipe for death","renferrel","rot hide","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","silverpine","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:forsaken","quest:446","quest:447","quest:443","quest:493"},src={"Apothecary Renferrel"}}
E["npc:clarice-foster"] = {t="npc",n="Clarice Foster",z="silverpine",s="Clarice Foster is a Forsaken woman residing deep beneath the bluffs of Mulgore within the Pools of Vision. Far from the plagued glades of Lordaeron, she spends her days in contemplation among the tauren seers and mystics.",h="Clarice Foster is a Forsaken woman residing deep beneath the bluffs of Mulgore within the Pools of Vision.",sec={{t="A Forsaken in the Pools of Vision",b="While most Forsaken remain in the northern lands of Lordaeron rebuilding their kingdom under the Undercity, Clarice Foster has traveled to the heart of the tauren lands in Kalimdor. Sheltered within the cavernous Pools of Vision beneath the mesa of Thunder Bluff, she dwells alongside Forsaken apothecaries and tauren shamans who study the spiritual and elemental mysteries of the earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Clarice Foster?",a="Clarice Foster is a Forsaken woman located in the subterranean Pools of Vision below Thunder Bluff. She is one of the few undead envoys and visitors dwelling among the tauren of Mulgore.",al={"who is clarice","clarice foster npc","clarice foster backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Clarice Foster?",a="She is located in the Pools of Vision, a cave complex situated beneath the Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"clarice foster location","where is clarice foster","find clarice foster"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does she offer?",a="She provides the quest 'Until Death Do Us Part', dispatching travelers on business connecting her quiet post in Kalimdor with the wider affairs of the Forsaken.",al={"clarice foster quests","until death do us part quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Clarice Foster on?",a="Clarice Foster is aligned with the Forsaken and the broader Horde. Though her duties keep her far from Lordaeron within the subterranean Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff, she remains loyal to Queen Sylvanas and the Forsaken cause.",al={"clarice foster faction","clarice foster allegiance","who does clarice foster serve"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Clarice Foster represents Forsaken ties to their tauren allies in Kalimdor, resting far from the blight-stained soil of Tirisfal and Silverpine.",["race:Tauren"]="Welcomed into the sacred Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise, Clarice Foster shows the tauren's willingness to host the unconventional newcomers of the Horde."},kw={"clarice foster","forsaken","pools of vision","spirit rise","thunder bluff","until death do us part"},rel={"subzone:pools-of-vision","zone:thunderbluff","quest:264","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},src={"Clarice Foster"}}
E["npc:dalar-dawnweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Dalar Dawnweaver",z="silverpine",s="Dalar Dawnweaver is a former archmage of Dalaran who now serves the Forsaken at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Slain during the Scourge's destruction of the magi's city and later freed from the Lich King's control, he turns his magical intellect toward dissecting regional threats. From the shadows of the tomb, he directs efforts to understand Dalaran's lingering presence and undo the madness of Archmage Arugal.",h="Dalar Dawnweaver is a former archmage of Dalaran who now serves the Forsaken at the Sepulcher in Silverpine...",sec={{t="A Fallen Archmage",b="In life, Dalar Dawnweaver held high rank among the Kirin Tor, walking the halls of the Violet Citadel when Dalaran was a pinnacle of arcane mastery. His mortal life ended when the Scourge sacked the city to pave the way for Archimonde's summoning. Reanimated into the mindless thrall of the Lich King, Dalar broke free alongside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner when the Scourge's grip faltered. Now stationed at the Sepulcher, he retains the piercing intellect of an archmage, turned entirely toward safeguarding the Forsaken realm.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on Ambermill and Shadowfang",b="Silverpine Forest is caught between multiple perils, and Dalar serves as the Sepulcher's arcane strategist. To the south, Dalaran wizards occupy Ambermill under a protective dome, meddling in matters Dalar seeks to uncover and disrupt. Even closer looms Shadowfang Keep and the feral worgen loosed upon the woods. Dalar possesses intimate knowledge of his former colleague, Archmage Arugal, and meticulously orchestrates campaigns to neutralize Arugal's beastly creations before they overrun the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage found at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. In life, he was an archmage of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. After dying during the Third War and being raised by the Scourge, he broke free of the Lich King's control to serve the Dark Lady.",al={"who is dalar","dalar dawnweaver lore","dalar background"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to him during the Third War?",a="Dalar was present in Dalaran when Arthas Menethil and the Scourge invaded to recover the Book of Medivh. Slain during the assault as Kel'Thuzad summoned Archimonde into Azeroth, Dalar was raised into undeath as a servant of the Scourge until Sylvanas liberated him.",al={"how did dalar die","dalar death","dalar third war"},it="history"},{q="Why is Dalar stationed at the Sepulcher?",a="He serves as the local arcane authority for the Forsaken in Silverpine Forest. His historical familiarity with both the Kirin Tor forces occupying Ambermill and his former peer, Archmage Arugal, makes him ideally suited to counter those threats.",al={"why is dalar in sepulcher","dalar role in silverpine"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Dalar's connection to Archmage Arugal?",a="Both were mages of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran before its fall. Dalar recognizes the tragic descent and lethal danger of Arugal's summoning experiments in Shadowfang Keep, tasking adventurers with gathering relics of Arugal's folly and ultimately demanding the mad mage's death.",al={"dalar and arugal","did dalar know arugal"},it="ties"},{q="What does Dalar want with Dalaran's remnants?",a="Dalar keeps a watchful eye on his former homeland and the surviving Kirin Tor forces stationed at Ambermill. He directs agents to intercept their communications and analyze their intentions to ensure they cannot threaten the Forsaken in Silverpine.",al={"dalar and dalaran","dalar ambermill"},it="wants"},{q="Is Dalar aligned with the Kirin Tor?",a="No. While he was once an archmage among them, his loyalty now lies with the Forsaken and the Horde. He actively opposes the surviving Kirin Tor forces operating within Silverpine Forest.",al={"is dalar kirin tor","is dalar loyal to dalaran"},it="side"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages will find in Dalar a dark mirror of Dalaran's former grandeur, demonstrating how Kirin Tor training can be weaponized in service to the Dark Lady.",["race:Undead"]="Dalar exemplifies the reclaimed agency of the Forsaken, turning the very knowledge he possessed in life against Dalaran remnants and rogue wizards who threaten their sovereignty.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed at the Sepulcher, Dalar secures the Horde's western frontier by coordinating strikes against the worgen of Shadowfang Keep and hostile Kirin Tor enclaves."},kw={"archmage","arugal","dalar","dalaran","dawnweaver","forsaken","kirin tor","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","npc:arugal","quest:99","quest:1014","quest:481","quest:482","topic:forsaken"},src={"Dalar Dawnweaver"}}
E["npc:darius-crowley"] = {t="npc",n="Darius Crowley",z="silverpine",s="Lord Darius Crowley is a fiery Gilnean nobleman who staunchly championed the Grand Alliance and opposed King Genn Greymane's isolationist policy. After the construction of the Greymane Wall severed his northern holdings and abandoned the outside world, Crowley led the Northgate Rebellion, an armed revolt that ultimately landed him in Stoneward Prison for high treason.",h="Lord Darius Crowley is a fiery Gilnean nobleman who staunchly championed the Grand Alliance and opposed King...",sec={{t="A Friend of the Alliance",b="During the Second War, Lord Darius Crowley was one of Gilneas's most charismatic and popular young nobles. When King Genn Greymane journeyed to Lordaeron to hear Anduin Lothar speak on Stormwind's destruction, Crowley urged his monarch to aid their fellow human nations against the Old Horde. His sympathy for the Alliance never wavered, even as Greymane grew resentful of the internment camp expenses and taxes required to rebuild the south. When the Third War broke out and Greymane chose seclusion, Crowley defied royal orders by dispatching the Gilneas Brigade across the Great Sea alongside Lady Jaina Proudmoore's expedition to Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="The Northgate Rebellion",b="King Greymane's decision to construct the massive Greymane Wall cut straight through Crowley's ancestral lands, abandoning holdings like Ambermill and Pyrewood Village to the wilderness beyond. Viewing the wall as both an insult and an act of tyrannical cowardice, Crowley raised an armed faction known as the Northgate rebels to depose the king. The ensuing civil war tore through Gilneas until the rebels made an assault on Gilneas City itself, bombarding the capital with artillery. Royalist forces rallied and shattered the insurrection, and Crowley was captured and locked away in Stoneward Prison, branded a traitor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Darius Crowley?",a="Lord Darius Crowley is a prominent Gilnean lord who fiercely advocated for Gilneas to remain part of the Grand Alliance. He opposed King Genn Greymane's isolationism, funded an expedition to Kalimdor against the king's wishes, and eventually led an armed civil war to overthrow the crown.",al={"darius crowley lore","who is crowley","lord crowley"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Darius Crowley right now?",a="Crowley is imprisoned deep within Stoneward Prison in Gilneas City. Following the defeat of his rebel forces in the Northgate Rebellion, the Gilnean crown convicted him of high treason and had him placed under heavy lock and key.",al={"where is crowley","is crowley alive","crowley location"},it="why_here"},{q="Why did Crowley rebel against King Greymane?",a="Crowley opposed Greymane's decision to withdraw Gilneas from the Alliance and erect the Greymane Wall. The construction cut right through Crowley's northern holdings, stranding settlements such as Ambermill and Pyrewood outside the kingdom's protection. Viewing this as tyrannical abandonment, Crowley took up arms.",al={"why did crowley rebel","northgate rebellion cause","crowley vs greymane"},it="motive"},{q="What lands did Crowley hold outside the Greymane Wall?",a="Before the Greymane Wall sealed Gilneas off from Silverpine Forest, Crowley owned and administered the settlements of Ambermill and Pyrewood Village, along with the surrounding territory in the north.",al={"crowley lands","pyrewood lord","ambermill crowley"},it="place"},{q="Whose side is Darius Crowley on?",a="Crowley has long stood for the Grand Alliance and the unity of the human kingdoms. When King Genn Greymane chose isolation and retreated behind the Greymane Wall, Crowley bitterly opposed abandoning Lordaeron and their allies, even dispatching the Gilneas Brigade to aid Lady Jaina Proudmoore across the sea. Within Gilneas, he heads the Northgate faction against Greymane's royalists.",al={"crowley alliance or horde","whose side is crowley on","darius crowley allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Darius Crowley want?",a="Crowley fought to end what he considered King Genn Greymane's blind tyranny and misguided isolation. He sought an open Gilneas that honored its treaties and stood shoulder-to-shoulder with the wider Alliance, rather than cowering behind stone while neighboring human realms fell. Above all, he fought to restore Gilneas to the world stage and overturn Greymane's rule.",al={"what does crowley want","crowley goal","what is darius crowley trying to do"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Darius Crowley tied to?",a="He is the father of Lorna Crowley and was once a close confidant and advisor to King Genn Greymane before politics shattered their bond. Across Gilneas, he commands the deep loyalty of the Northgate rebels and the people of northern territories like Pyrewood Village and Ambermill, while royalist lords like Vincent Godfrey despise him as a traitor.",al={"who is crowley allied with","darius crowley daughter","crowley connections"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why is Darius Crowley famous?",a="Crowley is renowned as a charismatic, passionate nobleman who defied his own king to defend his people and ideals. Celebrated by commoners and soldiers for his courage during the Second War and his defiance against isolationism, he is equally notorious among royalists as the ruthless leader of the Northgate Rebellion who turned cannons upon Gilneas City itself.",al={"why is crowley famous","darius crowley reputation","is crowley feared"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Crowley remained one of the few Gilnean nobles committed to the Grand Alliance, defying his king to send troops with Jaina Proudmoore to Kalimdor.",["race:Human"]="For humans outside the closed gates of the Greymane Wall, Crowley is remembered as a rare Gilnean leader who refused to abandon his neighbors during the dark days of the Third War."},kw={"ambermill","crowley","darius crowley","gilneas","greymane wall","northgate","pyrewood","rebellion","stoneward"},rel={"subzone:greymane-wall","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:ambermill","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:alliance","zone:silverpine","topic:third-war","topic:second-war"},src={"Darius Crowley"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-faerleia"] = {t="npc",n="Deathstalker Faerleia",z="silverpine",s="Deathstalker Faerleia is an operative of the Forsaken intelligence agency stationed deep within enemy territory inside Pyrewood Village. Operating out of the settlement's town hall, she orchestrates covert strikes against the local Gilnean leadership.",h="Deathstalker Faerleia is an operative of the Forsaken intelligence agency stationed deep within enemy...",sec={{t="Behind Enemy Lines",b="As an agent of the Deathstalkers—the covert intelligence and assassin branch of the Undercity—Faerleia is tasked with infiltrating Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest. The isolated human enclave harbors dark secrets, including a curse that transforms its populace under the night sky. Stationed within the upper levels of the town hall, Faerleia coordinates operations to disrupt the settlement from the inside, calling on Horde operatives to eliminate the influential members of the Pyrewood Council.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Faerleia?",a="She is an operative of the Deathstalkers, the stealth and intelligence division of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken. She has slipped into Pyrewood Village to wage a covert war against its leadership.",al={"faerleia","who is faerleia","deathstalker faerleia"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Deathstalker Faerleia be found?",a="Faerleia is tucked away inside the town hall of Pyrewood Village, located in southern Silverpine Forest just north of the Greymane Wall.",al={"where is faerleia","faerleia location","find faerleia"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What mission does she give?",a="She directs adventurers in the Pyrewood Ambush, an operation to assassinate the councilmen governing Pyrewood Village to weaken the enclave's resistance against the Forsaken.",al={"faerleia quest","pyrewood ambush quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the Deathstalkers targeting Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood remains an active human settlement affiliated with Gilneas right on the border of Forsaken territory. Weakening its leadership helps secure Silverpine Forest from hostile threats.",al={"why attack pyrewood","deathstalkers in pyrewood"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Deathstalker Faerleia on?",a="Faerleia is an operative of the Deathstalkers, the intelligence and assassin order serving Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. Her loyalty lies with the Undercity and the Horde, advancing their hold over Silverpine Forest against hostile enclaves.",al={"faerleia faction","who does faerleia serve","faerleia loyalty"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Deathstalker Faerleia want?",a="She seeks the destruction of Pyrewood Village's leadership. Deep within hostile territory, Faerleia coordinates an ambush against the Pyrewood Council to break the village's organized resistance and eliminate the local threat.",al={"what does faerleia want","faerleia goal","faerleia objective"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Deathstalker Faerleia in Pyrewood Village?",a="Faerleia has slipped past Pyrewood's defenders into the town hall itself. Positioned directly in the seat of power, she lies in wait to stage a decisive strike against the village leaders from within their own walls.",al={"why is faerleia here","why is faerleia in pyrewood","faerleia silverpine town hall"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Deathstalker Faerleia tied to?",a="Faerleia answers to the Deathstalkers of the Forsaken, answering up the chain of command to Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. In the field, she depends on trusted Horde scouts and adventurers bold enough to infiltrate the cursed settlement to carry out her ambush.",al={"faerleia ties","faerleia connections","who is faerleia working with"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Faerleia exemplifies the Deathstalkers' reliance on infiltration and cold calculation to dismantle enemies of the Dark Lady without committing an entire army.",["class:Rogue"]="For rogues serving the Forsaken, Faerleia represents the pinnacle of Deathstalker field craft: slipping unnoticed straight into the enemy's seat of power to orchestrate ambushes."},kw={"ambush","council","deathstalker","faerleia","forsaken","pyrewood","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:pyrewood-village","quest:452","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Deathstalker Faerleia"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-rane-yorick"] = {t="npc",n="Deathstalker Rane Yorick",z="silverpine",s="Deathstalker Rane Yorick is an operative of the Forsaken intelligence guild stationed deep in Silverpine Forest. Together with her brother Quinn, she was sent to scout the farms of northern Silverpine and report to High Executor Hadrec.",h="Deathstalker Rane Yorick is an operative of the Forsaken intelligence guild stationed deep in Silverpine...",sec={{t="Eyes in the Woods",b="The Deathstalkers serve as Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's eyes, ears, and blades across Lordaeron. Operating out of shadows and hidden posts, agents like Rane Yorick monitor the wilderness for threats that could disrupt Forsaken dominion. When sent to scout northern Silverpine Forest, Rane and her brother Quinn found themselves hemmed in by surrounding feral dangers, turning an undercover reconnaissance mission into a battle for survival.",sp=0},{t="Trapped at Ivar Patch",b="Holed up inside a derelict farmhouse at the Ivar Patch, Rane Yorick finds her mission compromised. The ghoul Ivar the Foul has badly mauled her brother Quinn, and worgs roam the fields between her and the safety of the Sepulcher. Rather than abandon her assignment, she relies on passing Horde travelers to gather worg hearts for a healing potion, slay Ivar, and deliver her report back to command.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Rane Yorick?",a="She is an operative of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken rogue order of assassins and intelligence gatherers. She is currently stationed at a dilapidated farmhouse at the Ivar Patch in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is rane yorick","rane yorick lore","who is deathstalker yorick"},it="identity"},{q="What are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the clandestine rogue guild of the Forsaken, answering to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. They carry out covert scouting, espionage, and targeted assassinations across Lordaeron.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker faction","who are the deathstalkers"}},{q="Why is she trapped in a farmhouse?",a="Rane and her brother Quinn were sent to scout the farms of northern Silverpine Forest, but the ghoul Ivar the Foul attacked them at the Ivar Patch and badly mauled Quinn, forcing them to hole up in the farmhouse while he heals.",al={"why is rane trapped","ivar patch farmhouse","why is she hiding"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is her brother?",a="Her brother is Quinn Yorick, a fellow Deathstalker on the same reconnaissance mission, who was badly mauled by the ghoul Ivar the Foul at the Ivar Patch.",al={"rane yorick brother","who is erland","deathstalker erland"},it="ties"},{q="What threats are they tracking in Silverpine?",a="Their mission was to scout the farms of northern Silverpine for threats to the Forsaken occupation. They found a far heavier Scourge presence than expected, along with prowling worgs and the ghoul Ivar the Foul.",al={"what are they scouting","what is rane investigating"},it="threat"},{q="Where does she report her findings?",a="She reports to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher, who oversees the Forsaken occupation of Silverpine Forest.",al={"where do reports go","who is rane's superior"}},{q="Whose side is Deathstalker Rane Yorick on?",a="Deathstalker Rane Yorick is fully loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady. As a member of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's covert espionage and assassination order, she carries out dangerous reconnaissance missions across Lordaeron to protect their fledgling realm from lurking enemies.",al={"rane yorick faction","who does rane yorick serve","is rane yorick forsaken"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Deathstalker Rane Yorick want?",a="Rane wants to complete her scouting mission and ensure her findings make it back to Forsaken command. With herself and her companion cornered and beleaguered in Silverpine, she desperately needs reliable allies to assist them, neutralize nearby perils, and convey her intelligence safely.",al={"what does rane yorick need","rane yorick motive","why does rane yorick want help"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For Forsaken rogues, Rane Yorick exemplifies the perilous fieldwork expected of the Deathstalkers, maintaining stealth and collecting intelligence under constant enemy pressure.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken champions encounter Rane as a frontline scout keeping the untamed frontier of Silverpine Forest from falling back into hostile hands.",["faction:Horde"]="Her intelligence operations help ensure Horde supply routes running through Silverpine remain clear of worgen and local ambushes."},kw={"deathstalker","erland","forsaken","ivar patch","rane","rogue","scout","silverpine","yorick"},rel={"quest:428","quest:435","quest:449","subzone:ivar-patch","quest:425","topic:worgen","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Deathstalker Rane Yorick"}}
E["npc:elder-obsidian"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Obsidian",z="silverpine",s="Elder Obsidian is an ancestral earthen spirit who manifests at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest during the annual Lunar Festival. Appearing among the graves claimed by the Forsaken, he offers the wisdom and blessings of the ancient world to travelers honoring the festival.",h="Elder Obsidian is an ancestral earthen spirit who manifests at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest during the...",sec={{t="A Spirit at the Sepulcher",b="Standing amid the somber tombs of the Sepulcher, Elder Obsidian provides a striking contrast to Silverpine Forest's gloomy expanse. As an ethereal earthen elder, his spirit manifests during the Lunar Festival to celebrate the ancient heritage of Azeroth. While the surrounding crypts are held by the Forsaken and menaced by feral worgen, Obsidian greets wayfarers of all allegiances in peace, bestowing Coin of Ancestry and ancient blessings upon those who take the time to seek out his wisdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Obsidian?",a="Elder Obsidian is an ancient earthen ghost who appears in Silverpine Forest. He surfaces exclusively during the Lunar Festival, greeting travelers who honor the world's ancestral heritage.",al={"elder obsidian lore","who is obsidian","sepulcher elder"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Elder Obsidian be found?",a="He can be found resting within the graveyard grounds of the Sepulcher, a Forsaken-controlled hamlet situated along the road in central Silverpine Forest.",al={"elder obsidian location","where is obsidian","find elder obsidian"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does an earthen elder appear in Silverpine Forest?",a="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of ancient elders manifest in lands across Azeroth to share their ancestral wisdom. Obsidian's spiritual presence transcends local territorial conflicts, allowing him to commune quietly amidst the ancient graves.",al={"why is obsidian in silverpine","earthen in silverpine"},it="why_here"},{q="Can Alliance adventurers speak with Elder Obsidian?",a="Yes. Festival elders remain neutral toward all travelers regardless of faction. However, because he rests in the Sepulcher, Alliance adventurers must carefully navigate the hostile Forsaken guards stationed nearby to reach him.",al={"can alliance visit elder obsidian","elder obsidian alliance friendly"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Obsidian on?",a="Elder Obsidian stands apart from the mortal conflicts between the Alliance and Horde. As an ancient earthen spirit returning for the Lunar Festival, he offers his wisdom and ancestral blessing to any adventurer who comes to honor the elders, regardless of allegiance, even though he manifests near the Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher.",al={"is elder obsidian alliance or horde","elder obsidian faction","elder obsidian side"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Elder Obsidian want?",a="Elder Obsidian wishes to be remembered and honored by the mortals of Azeroth. During the celebration of the Lunar Festival, he welcomes travelers who seek out his ancient presence, bestowing his blessing and a token of ancestral luck upon those who pay their respects to the past.",al={"what does elder obsidian need","elder obsidian goal","why visit elder obsidian"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves curious about their Titan-forged lineage, speaking with an earthen spirit like Elder Obsidian offers a rare glimpse into the primordial past of their stone-hewn ancestors.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance pilgrims seeking Elder Obsidian must tread carefully, as his chosen resting place lies in the heart of the Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","earthen","elder obsidian","lunar festival","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"quest:8645","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},src={"Elder Obsidian"}}
E["npc:high-executor-hadrec"] = {t="npc",n="High Executor Hadrec",z="silverpine",s="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander of the Forsaken garrison stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. From this central crypt, he oversees defense against regional threats including the gnolls of the Rot Hide clan and investigates the disappearance of scouts across the zone. He serves as the primary officer directing Horde operations throughout Silverpine.",h="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander of the Forsaken garrison stationed at the Sepulcher in...",sec={{t="Commander at the Sepulcher",b="Stationed within the gloom of the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec directs Forsaken military operations across Silverpine Forest. While Tirisfal Glades is firmly secured by the Dark Lady's forces, Silverpine remains fraught with peril, bordered by hostile Dalaran mages, feral worgen, and encroaching gnolls. Hadrec bears the grim responsibility of consolidating Forsaken territory and stamping out anything that challenges Undercity authority south of the capital.",sp=0},{t="The Rot Hide Scourge",b="Much of Hadrec's immediate concern revolves around the Rot Hide gnolls and Fenris Isle. These undead-tainted beasts have infested the Dead Fields and the shores of Lake Lordamere, posing an unpredictable and vicious threat to Forsaken patrols. Hadrec dispatches agents to scour the decrepit ferries and rotting farmsteads for clues, determine what empowers the beasts, and prepare an outright strike against their island stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Eye on Shadowfang",b="Beyond the gnoll infestation, Hadrec closely monitors intelligence gathered by the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's secretive rogue intelligence arm. When covert operatives disappear near the eerie spires of Shadowfang Keep, Hadrec tasks adventurers with discovering their fate, ensuring the Dark Lady remains informed of the shadowy archmage Arugal and his cursed worgen.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="Hadrec is a Forsaken military officer holding the rank of High Executor. He commands the garrison based at the Sepulcher, making him the supreme Forsaken authority over operations in Silverpine Forest.",al={"hadrec lore","who is hadrec","sepulcher commander"},it="identity"},{q="Where can High Executor Hadrec be found?",a="He is located inside the Sepulcher, the Forsaken settlement situated in central Silverpine Forest along the main north-south road.",al={"hadrec location","where is hadrec","find hadrec"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats does Hadrec direct players against?",a="Hadrec directs soldiers and adventurers against the Rot Hide gnolls that plague the Dead Fields and Fenris Isle. He also oversees missions to locate missing Deathstalker spies and uncover what is unfolding inside Shadowfang Keep.",al={"hadrec quests","what does hadrec do","silverpine missions"},it="threat"},{q="What does a High Executor do in Forsaken military structure?",a="A High Executor is a high-ranking field commander in the Forsaken military, entrusted with full strategic oversight of an entire regional outpost or front line under the authority of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"forsaken high executor","high executor rank","hadrec rank"},it="power"},{q="Why is Hadrec interested in Fenris Isle?",a="Fenris Isle has become the primary den of the Rot Hide gnolls. To secure Lake Lordamere and the surrounding waterways for Forsaken supply lines, Hadrec coordinates reconnaissance and an eventual assault to break the gnoll leadership.",al={"fenris isle hadrec","why assault fenris isle","rot hide fenris"},it="target"},{q="What is Hadrec's connection to Shadowfang Keep?",a="Hadrec coordinates with the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken espionage order. When scouts sent toward Shadowfang Keep fail to report back, Hadrec commissions trusted agents to investigate the keep and uncover what happened to them.",al={"shadowfang keep hadrec","hadrec arugal","deathstalkers in shadowfang"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is High Executor Hadrec on?",a="High Executor Hadrec serves the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner, as part of the Horde. From his post at the Sepulcher, he commands Forsaken military operations across Silverpine Forest, acting directly in the interests of the Undercity.",al={"hadrec faction","who does hadrec serve","hadrec horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does High Executor Hadrec want?",a="Hadrec aims to secure Silverpine Forest for the Forsaken and protect the Undercity's southern flank. He coordinates efforts to gather intelligence on enemy movements, eradicate the Rot Hide gnoll scourge infesting the region, and eliminate rival threats lurking across the forest from Fenris Isle to the outskirts of Shadowfang Keep.",al={"what is hadrec's goal","hadrec motives","hadrec silverpine goals"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is High Executor Hadrec here at the Sepulcher?",a="Hadrec is stationed at the Sepulcher because it serves as the Forsaken's central military and operational stronghold in Silverpine Forest. As High Executor, he oversees regional operations, coordinates field reports from the Deathstalkers, and dispatches champions to neutralize encroaching threats to ensure Forsaken dominion over the territory.",al={"why is hadrec at sepulcher","hadrec location silverpine","why is hadrec in silverpine"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec tied to?",a="Hadrec works in close concert with the Forsaken's covert intelligence wing, the Deathstalkers, receiving field reports and sending reinforcements to uncover hidden perils. He also collaborates with local specialists like Apothecary Renferrel to study regional threats such as the Rot Hide gnolls.",al={"hadrec allies","hadrec connections","who does hadrec work with"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken traveling south from Deathknell, Hadrec represents the voice of the Undercity's high command, turning newborn undead into organized defenders of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Forsaken arriving from Kalimdor report to Hadrec to aid in stabilizing Silverpine, learning firsthand how tenuous the Horde's foothold in northern Lordaeron remains.",["class:Rogue"]="Hadrec relies heavily on the Deathstalkers for intelligence, frequently employing stealthy operatives to recover missing comrades and gather enemy ichor and documents."},kw={"deathstalker","fenris isle","hadrec","high executor","rot hide","sepulcher","shadowfang","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:442","quest:1098","quest:449","quest:437","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:forsaken"},src={"High Executor Hadrec"}}
E["npc:karos-razok"] = {t="npc",n="Karos Razok",z="silverpine",s="Karos Razok is the Forsaken bat handler stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He oversees the roost of undead fliers that connect this contested frontier outpost directly to the Undercity and other Horde strongholds.",h="Karos Razok is the Forsaken bat handler stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Sepulcher's Wings",b="Perched on the wooden platform above the crypts of the Sepulcher, Karos Razok tends to the skeletal bats vital for Forsaken communications. With Silverpine Forest infested by Moonrage worgen, rogue Dalaran magi, and the human remnants of Ambermill, overland travel along the northern road is treacherous. Razok ensures that messengers, fresh recruits, and vital supplies can cross above the haunted canopy, keeping the front line linked straight back to the capital in Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok is the Forsaken flight master stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He manages the roost of trained vampiric bats used by Horde adventurers and messengers to travel across Lordaeron.",al={"karos razok role","who is the flight master in the sepulcher","sepulcher bat handler"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Karos Razok send travelers?",a="In classic travel networks, Razok primarily links the Sepulcher directly to the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades and to Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, facilitating rapid transit across northern Lordaeron.",al={"sepulcher flight paths","where does the sepulcher bat fly","flight routes from sepulcher"},gp=true},{q="What creatures does Karos handle?",a="He tends to large, skeletal flight bats. These undead beasts are hardy, tireless fliers adapted to Lordaeron's blighted skies and are favored by the Forsaken for their silence and endurance.",al={"what mounts does razok have","forsaken flight beasts","what are the flying mounts at sepulcher"}},{q="Why is a flight master important at the Sepulcher?",a="The roads of Silverpine are choked with hostile forces, from Pyrewood's worgen curse to human wizards at Ambermill. Razok provides an aerial lifeline that allows the Forsaken to supply this forward base without suffering ambushes on the highway.",al={"why is sepulcher bat master needed","sepulcher travel importance"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Karos Razok on?",a="Karos Razok serves the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed in Silverpine Forest, he pledges his allegiance to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Undercity, aiding Forsaken couriers, scouts, and adventurers traveling across the region.",al={"karos razok faction","who does karos razok serve","karos razok horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Karos Razok want?",a="Karos simply wants to keep the skies open and aerial transit running smoothly for the Forsaken. Managing the roost at the Sepulcher ensures that supplies, messages, and reinforcements can flow reliably between Silverpine and other Horde bastions.",al={"karos razok goal","what does karos razok do","karos razok motives"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Karos Razok represents your lifeline back to the Undercity, ensuring that frontline efforts in Silverpine remain firmly tethered to Lady Sylvanas's capital.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers pushing south toward Hillsbrad Foothills, Razok's bat roost is an indispensable waypoint on the western edge of Lordaeron."},kw={"bat handler","flight master","karos razok","sepulcher","silverpine forest","undercity"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:forsaken","quest:6323","quest:6321","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Karos Razok"}}
E["npc:lorna-crowley"] = {t="npc",n="Lorna Crowley",z="silverpine",s="Lorna Crowley is the daughter of Lord Darius Crowley, a leading nobleman of Gilneas. Isolated behind the towering Greymane Wall, she remains entwined with the shifting internal politics and conflicts of the sealed human kingdom.",h="Lorna Crowley is the daughter of Lord Darius Crowley, a leading nobleman of Gilneas.",sec={{t="Daughter of the Rebellion",b="Behind the colossal stone ramparts of the Greymane Wall, the kingdom of Gilneas cut itself off from the rest of Lordaeron years ago. Lorna Crowley is the daughter of Lord Darius Crowley, a prominent nobleman who strongly resisted the kingdom's isolationist decree and the wall's construction. Growing up amidst deep political unrest and the Northgate Rebellion, Lorna shares her father's fierce spirit and martial pride while remaining tucked away from the wider events shaping the continent outside.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lorna Crowley?",a="Lorna Crowley is a Gilnean noblewoman and the daughter of Lord Darius Crowley. She is known for her strong will and sharp mind, shaped by the political friction and insular struggles inside Gilneas.",al={"lorna crowley","who is lorna","darius crowley daughter"},it="identity"},{q="Can players meet Lorna Crowley right now?",a="No. Lorna remains sealed behind the massive Greymane Wall within the closed kingdom of Gilneas, which keeps its gates shut tight against all outsiders.",al={"where is lorna crowley","can you find lorna","is lorna in game"},it="why_here"},{q="What is her father's role in Gilneas?",a="Lord Darius Crowley is one of the kingdom's foremost noblemen. He opposed King Genn Greymane's decision to wall off the realm, eventually leading the Northgate Rebellion against the crown.",al={"who is darius crowley","darius crowley","crowley gilneas"},it="ties"},{q="What is happening in Gilneas behind the wall?",a="Gilneas remains in self-imposed isolation, cut off from the Alliance and the surrounding lands since the aftermath of the Second War. Its internal conflicts and daily life stay entirely hidden behind its massive barricades.",al={"what is happening in gilneas","greymane wall status","gilneas situation"},it="place"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lorna Crowley and her family belong to the lost kingdom of Gilneas, which severed ties with the Alliance of Lordaeron to lock its gates behind the Greymane Wall."},kw={"darius crowley","gilneas","greymane wall","lorna crowley","silverpine"},rel={"npc:darius-crowley","subzone:greymane-wall","zone:silverpine","topic:alliance"},src={"Lorna Crowley"}}
E["npc:quinn-yorick"] = {t="npc",n="Quinn Yorick",z="silverpine",s="Quinn Yorick is a wounded Forsaken scout sheltering on the upper floor of a ruined farmhouse in the Ivar Patch. Having barely survived an encounter with the feral worgen known as Ivar the Foul, he now relies on passing allies to help secure his survival.",h="Quinn Yorick is a wounded Forsaken scout sheltering on the upper floor of a ruined farmhouse in the Ivar...",sec={{t="A Precarious Refuge",b="Tucked away inside an abandoned home at the Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick lies gravely injured upstairs. His condition is the result of a vicious clash with Ivar the Foul, one of the savage worgen haunting the northern stretches of Silverpine Forest. Unable to finish his mission or safely retreat alone, Quinn remains in hiding, waiting for travelers working for the Forsaken to aid his plight and deliver retribution to the beast that nearly tore him apart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Quinn Yorick located?",a="Quinn Yorick can be found hiding on the upper floor of a broken farmhouse in the Ivar Patch, located in Silverpine Forest north of the Sepulcher.",al={"quinn yorick location","where is quinn","quinn yorick house"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who injured Quinn Yorick?",a="He was severely wounded by Ivar the Foul, a powerful and vicious worgen prowling the nearby farmland.",al={"who attacked quinn","what happened to quinn yorick","quinn injured"},it="conflict"},{q="What role does Quinn serve for Horde adventurers?",a="Quinn serves as the turn-in point for Forsaken scouts and allies sent to assist him in the field, seeking vengeance against Ivar the Foul.",al={"quinn yorick quest","quinn quest giver"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Quinn Yorick?",a="Quinn Yorick is a Forsaken operative sheltering upstairs in a decrepit farmhouse within the Ivar Patch. Severely wounded during an encounter with the feral leader Ivar the Foul, he hides among the shadows of Silverpine Forest, relying on travelers of the Horde to assist him while he recovers from his injuries.",al={"who is quinn","quinn yorick lore","who quinn yorick"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Quinn Yorick on?",a="Quinn is loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, and by extension the Horde. He welcomes Horde champions who wander into the isolated farmstead, seeking their aid against the feral threats lurking just outside his refuge.",al={"quinn yorick faction","is quinn yorick horde","quinn yorick allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Quinn Yorick here?",a="Quinn came to the area now overrun by worgen, only to be ambushed and grievously battered by Ivar the Foul. Unable to easily escape or press forward on his own, he holed up in the second floor of the abandoned farmhouse to survive.",al={"why is quinn yorick at ivar patch","quinn yorick purpose here","why quinn upstairs"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Quinn Yorick want?",a="Stuck nursing grave wounds, Quinn wants allies to avenge him and deal with the menace surrounding his hideout. He depends on capable adventurers to settle the score with Ivar the Foul and report back once the threat has been handled.",al={"what does quinn want","quinn yorick goal","quinn yorick objectives"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Quinn's predicament highlights the ever-present danger the feral worgen pose to Forsaken forces attempting to secure northern Silverpine."},kw={"forsaken scout","ivar patch","ivar the foul","quinn yorick","silverpine forest","worgen"},rel={"subzone:ivar-patch","quest:425","quest:430","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Quinn Yorick"}}
E["npc:shadow-priest-allister"] = {t="npc",n="Shadow Priest Allister",z="silverpine",s="Shadow Priest Allister is a Forsaken priest stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Overseeing intelligence and tactical efforts in the region, he coordinates operations to monitor Dalaran's wizards and secure the borders of Lordaeron for the Dark Lady.",h="Shadow Priest Allister is a Forsaken priest stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Watcher at the Sepulcher",b="Operating out of the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister directs Forsaken reconnaissance throughout Silverpine Forest. From this central crypt settlement, he tracks nearby threats ranging from renegade humans and beastly incursions to the arcane machinations unfolding near Dalaran's shimmering dome.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on Ambermill and Dalaran",b="Allister's chief concern lies with the surviving mages of Dalaran, particularly those occupying Ambermill and probing across the borders. Unwilling to let the Kirin Tor entrench themselves in Forsaken lands, he dispatches agents to intercept Dalaran messengers, decipher arcane runes, and determine the wizards' long-term ambitions.",sp=0},{t="Heretical Musings",b="Beyond his duties as a field strategist, Allister is a cynical philosopher of the shadow. He is the author of 'Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You'—a scathing treatise criticizing traditional holy doctrine. The text explores the harsh realities of undeath and how the Holy Light fails those discarded by life, a work that has somehow circulated as far afield as the ruins of Dire Maul in Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shadow Priest Allister?",a="He is a Forsaken shadow priest stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest who coordinates surveillance and strikes against nearby threats, particularly Dalaran forces.",al={"allister","shadow priest allister","who is allister silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Shadow Priest Allister?",a="He resides in the Sepulcher, the primary Forsaken settlement located along the main road running through Silverpine Forest.",al={"allister location","where is shadow priest allister","find allister"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Allister focused on Dalaran and Ambermill?",a="The Kirin Tor mages stationed at Ambermill pose a constant threat to Forsaken territory. Allister seeks to decrypt their communications, uncover their intentions, and keep their influence contained.",al={"allister dalaran","why attack ambermill","dalaran threat silverpine"},it="wants"},{q="What book did Allister write?",a="Allister authored 'Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You', an irreverent and critical critique of the Holy Light that found its way across the sea to the ancient libraries of Dire Maul.",al={"allister book","holy bologna","what the light wont tell you"}},{q="What quests does Allister offer?",a="He offers several intelligence-gathering missions around Silverpine Forest, including Border Crossings, Maps and Runes, Ambermill Investigations, and tasks confronting Dalaran agents.",al={"allister quests","sepulcher shadow priest quests"},gp=true},{q="Why does Allister practice Shadow magic instead of the Holy Light?",a="Like many Forsaken priests who felt abandoned by the Holy Light upon their deaths, Allister turned to the shadows, finding power and resolve in a discipline that embraces their undead existence.",al={"why shadow priest","forsaken shadow magic allister"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Shadow Priest Allister on?",a="Allister is utterly loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady. Stationed in the crypts of the Sepulcher, he turns his dark arts and calculating mind entirely toward securing Lordaeron for the undead and neutralizing any regional threats that challenge their fragile new domain.",al={"allister faction","who does shadow priest allister serve","is allister forsaken"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Shadow Priest Allister here in Silverpine Forest?",a="Operating from the Sepulcher, Allister keeps a watchful eye on hostile enclaves lingering along the southern borders. Between the surviving Dalaran wizards entrenched in Ambermill and strange magics stirring nearby, his role is to direct Forsaken operatives to probe enemy defenses and uncover their true intentions.",al={"why is allister at the sepulcher","allister silverpine purpose","why is shadow priest allister here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Allister exemplifies the Forsaken's ruthless pragmatism, turning his back on former holy dogmas to safeguard his people against living enemies.",["class:Priest"]="As the author of 'Holy Bologna', Allister represents the Forsaken perspective on the Cult of Forgotten Shadow and their disillusionment with the Light.",["faction:Horde"]="Allister works to secure Silverpine Forest, ensuring Horde allies have safe passage between Tirisfal Glades and lands to the south."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalaran","forsaken","holy bologna","sepulcher","shadow priest","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:ambermill","quest:479","quest:482","subzone:dalaran","subzone:dire-maul","topic:forsaken"},src={"Shadow Priest Allister"}}
E["quest:100"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="silverpine",s="This ritualistic step marks the culmination of the shaman's ordeal at the Brazier of Everfount along the coast of Silverpine Forest. Having shattered the corrupt spirits threatening the spring with a burst of elemental radiance, the shaman stands before an apparition of pure water to receive its communion.",h="This ritualistic step marks the culmination of the shaman's ordeal at the Brazier of Everfount along the...",sec={{t="A Burst of Cleansing Light",b="Upon reciting the final incantation at the Brazier of Everfount, an explosion of light scours the area of surrounding corruption. The hissed protests of tainted water drops evaporating over elemental flame fade, leaving the immediate shore silent as malevolent minor spirits disperse.",sp=0},{t="The Water's Gratitude",b="In the wake of the spirits' destruction, a Minor Manifestation of Water materializes beside the brazier. Grateful for the ritual intervention, the spirit recognizes the growing burden placed upon the Horde's shamans: though the local taint has ebbed, life in the decaying lands of Silverpine continues to wane, requiring vigilance to preserve.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happens when the brazier ritual finishes?",a="Completing the incantation at the Brazier of Everfount releases an explosion of brilliant light. This destroys the surrounding corrupted spirits and purifies the immediate elemental flow.",al={"brazier ritual light","everfount explosion"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is the Minor Manifestation of Water?",a="It is a minor elemental entity of pure water that manifests after the corrupted elementals near the Brazier of Everfount are destroyed.",al={"water spirit silverpine","manifestation of water"},it="identity"},{q="What does the water spirit say about Silverpine?",a="The spirit expresses thanks to the shamans, noting that while this specific corruption has ebbed, life across the land continues to wane and requires constant stewardship to safeguard.",al={"water spirit warning","silverpine corruption"},it="place"},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The ritual takes place at the Brazier of Everfount, situated along the coastline of Silverpine Forest.",al={"brazier location","call of water location"},it="place"},{q="Why must shamans intervene in Silverpine?",a="As part of their elemental trials to earn the Water Totem, shamans must prove their commitment to balance by defending distant, embattled natural waters from blight and lingering corruption.",al={"why shamans here","shaman duty silverpine"},it="motive"},{q="What comes next in the trials?",a="After conferring with the Minor Manifestation of Water, the shaman receives elemental remains or guidance to complete their journey and forge their Water Totem.",al={"next step call of water","after water manifestation"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This communion directly tests a shaman's resolve to heal suffering waters far beyond their native homes, earning communion with the spirit of water itself.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's spiritual leaders must cleanse corrupted waterways even within Forsaken-controlled territories like Silverpine to maintain elemental harmony."},kw={"brazier of everfount","call of water","elemental","minor manifestation of water","shaman trial","silverpine forest","water totem"},rel={"npc:minor-manifestation-of-water","zone:silverpine","quest:63","topic:light"},m={start="Brazier of Everfount",["end"]="Minor Manifestation of Water",level="23",faction="Horde",id=100},src={"Call of Water (8)"}}
E["quest:1103"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="silverpine",s="This quest offers a second chance for shamans completing their spiritual trials along the coast of Silverpine Forest. If a shaman's spirit-sight fades before communing with the purified manifestation of water, Tiev Mordune stands by to rekindle the communion. By providing another Water Sapta, the petitioner can witness the ritual anew and finish their communion.",h="This quest offers a second chance for shamans completing their spiritual trials along the coast of Silverpine...",sec={{t="A Helping Hand in the Mist",b="The path to mastering water is fraught with delicate spiritual timings. Shamans drink a potent draught known as a Water Sapta to perceive the spirits lingering around the elemental shrines. Should the draught's magic lapse before the shaman speaks with the Minor Manifestation of Water, they find themselves locked outside the spirit realm, unable to complete their trial. Fortunately, fellow shaman Tiev Mordune lingers on the fog-shrouded shores of Silverpine Forest to assist those whose visions ended too soon.",sp=0},{t="Renewing the Ritual",b="Tiev Mordune, having already conquered the corrupt water spirit lurking off the coast, waits with his gathered ritual remnants. He requires proof of readiness in the form of a fresh Water Sapta from Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. Once presented with the sapta, Tiev casts his gathered bracers and droplets into the shrine's brazier, summoning forth the pure manifestation once more so his fellow shaman can speak with it and seal their elemental bond.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tiev Mordune?",a="Tiev Mordune is a fellow Horde shaman stationed on the coast of Silverpine Forest. He has completed the battle against the local corrupt elemental and remains by the shore to help other initiates who lose their spiritual vision before finishing their communion.",al={"tiev mordune","who is tiev","tiev silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I need a Water Sapta for this quest?",a="A Water Sapta allows a shaman's mind to cross the threshold into the spirit world. Tiev requires a fresh draught from Islen Waterseer to ensure you have the vision needed to perceive the elemental once he summons it again.",al={"why need sapta","water sapta tiev","where to get sapta"},it="item"},{q="What happens if I missed speaking to the water spirit?",a="If the spirit draught wears off or the Minor Manifestation of Water vanishes before you can speak with it, you cannot finish the trial on your own. Tiev Mordune steps in to re-ignite the brazier using his own gathered trophies so you can commune with the spirit.",al={"missed the water spirit","failed water manifestation","manifestation despawned"},gp=true},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The trial takes place along the western coast of Silverpine Forest, near an elemental shrine facing the Great Sea.",al={"where is water shrine","silverpine water shrine location"},it="place"},{q="Who sent shamans on this pilgrimage?",a="Islen Waterseer, a tauren shaman dwelling by a fishing hut on the eastern coast of the Barrens, guides initiates through their Call of Water trials and brews the necessary saptas.",al={"who gave the call of water","islen waterstrider"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Minor Manifestation of Water?",a="It is a purified elemental spirit summoned at the shrine after the corruption poisoning the local waters has been cleansed. Communing with it marks the successful completion of this leg of a shaman's elemental trials.",al={"what is the water spirit","minor manifestation"},it="target"},{q="Why is Tiev Mordune helping other shamans here?",a="Tiev Mordune is a fellow shaman who has already conquered the corrupt water spirit and prepared his offerings. Having seen other pilgrims lose their chance when the spirit realm faded too quickly, he chose to delay his own ritual so he could assist any brother or sister who stumbled during the trial. By offering his ritual parts and knowledge of sapta magic, he ensures no worthy shaman is left behind on their path to understanding.",al={"why does tiev help","tiev mordune motive","why is tiev waiting"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This rite represents the camaraderie among shamans walking the grueling path to earn their Water Totem, ensuring no initiate is stranded by a fading trance.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's shamanic traditions rely heavily on mutual aid and respect for natural spirits, extending even into the haunted lands of Lordaeron."},kw={"call of water","islen waterstrider","minor manifestation of water","shaman","silverpine forest","tiev mordune","water sapta"},rel={"quest:63","quest:972","npc:minor-manifestation-of-water","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Tiev Mordune",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1103,ri={"Water Sapta"}},src={"Call of Water (Silverpine)"}}
E["quest:264"] = {t="quest",n="Until Death Do Us Part",z="silverpine",s="Until Death Do Us Part is a bitter, personal quest that leads to the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Clarice Foster, a Forsaken dwelling in the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff, sends adventurers to discard her keepsake pendant upon the tomb of her late husband, Yuriv. The task reveals the painful human fractures caused by zealotry and war as the plague claimed Lordaeron.",h="Until Death Do Us Part is a bitter, personal quest that leads to the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Bitter Keepsake",b="Clarice Foster carries no fondness for the memories of her mortal marriage. While Lordaeron crumbled, her husband Yuriv abandoned her and their children to march off on a crusade against the rising undead threat, declaring that serving the Holy Light was paramount. In the end, his devotion saved neither his family nor himself. Now raised into undeath while Yuriv rots beneath a defaced stone, Clarice seeks only to cast away the last tangible reminder of his broken promises.",sp=0},{t="The Neglected Grave",b="Yuriv's tomb rests in the graveyard surrounding the Sepulcher, marred by gashes, strewn with rubbish, and overtaken by weeds. Placing Clarice's pendant onto the sculpted relief of his hands brings no grand magic or spiritual closure, only a dulling of the gem and a cold, silent gust of wind over the tombs. It serves as a stark testament to the lingering resentments of Lordaeron's fallen people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Yuriv?",a="Yuriv was Clarice Foster's mortal husband. He left her and their children behind during life to fight against the Scourge in the name of the Holy Light, prioritizing his crusade over his family.",al={"who is yuriv","yuriv lore","clarice husband"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Clarice hate her late husband so much?",a="Clarice spent night after night waiting for Yuriv while he placed his religious duties first. In the end, his crusade failed to protect them, leaving him dead in a neglected grave while she was cursed to rise as the very undead monster he fought against.",al={"why is clarice mad","clarice foster backstory"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you return the pendant?",a="When placed upon the stone hands of Yuriv's carved relief, the pendant's gemstone noticeably dulls. A stiff, cool breeze sweeps over the Sepulcher, leaving the defaced tomb in cold, quiet abandonment.",al={"pendant on grave","ending of until death do us part"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Yuriv's tomb located?",a="Yuriv's tombstone is found within the cemetery grounds of the Sepulcher, the Forsaken stronghold in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is yuriv tomb","yuriv grave location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Yuriv's grave so damaged?",a="The grave has been gashed, littered with garbage, and overgrown with weeds. The Forsaken living at the Sepulcher hold no sympathy or reverence for a crusader who died opposing their kind.",al={"why is grave defaced","tomb abused"}},{q="Did Clarice's children survive?",a="Clarice mentions that Yuriv abandoned his children along with her, but their ultimate fate remains unstated. Given the total devastation of Lordaeron, it is likely they met a tragic end.",al={"what happened to the kids","clarice children"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Clarice's plight embodies the hypocrisy of the living: holy warriors left their families to perish in holy fervor, leaving their transformed survivors to bear the burden of memory.",["class:Priest"]="The quest paints a grim picture of faith, highlighting how devotion to the Light can tear families apart and breed lasting bitterness in those left behind.",["faction:Horde"]="Aiding Clarice provides Horde champions insight into the personal tragedies and enduring spite that bind the Forsaken together in Silverpine Forest."},kw={"clarice foster","crusade","forsaken","pendant","sepulcher","silverpine","tomb","yuriv"},rel={"npc:clarice-foster","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:light"},m={start="Clarice Foster",["end"]="Yuriv's Tombstone",faction="Horde",id=264},src={"Until Death Do Us Part"}}
E["quest:3221"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Renferrel",z="silverpine",s="Speak with Renferrel is a brief errand within the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. High Executor Hadrec directs you back to the Royal Apothecary Society's local researcher to discuss findings regarding tainted wolf hearts.",h="Speak with Renferrel is a brief errand within the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Summons from the Society",b="After assisting the Deathstalkers across Silverpine Forest, High Executor Hadrec passes along an urgent message from Apothecary Renferrel. Renferrel has spent time analyzing the discolored wolf hearts gathered from the local wildlife and requires your presence immediately.",sp=0},{t="Alchemical Curiosities",b="Apothecary Renferrel serves the Royal Apothecary Society from his laboratory inside the crypt at the Sepulcher. His ongoing work explores how dark magic and disease are altering the beasts of Silverpine, bridging frontline military recon with chemical research.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Apothecary Renferrel located?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is located inside the Sepulcher's crypt in central Silverpine Forest, standing near his alchemy equipment just steps away from High Executor Hadrec.",al={"renferrel location","where is renferrel","find renferrel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want to speak with me?",a="Renferrel has been analyzing discolored wolf hearts gathered from local Silverpine wolves and discovered peculiarities in their corruption that require further investigation and communication with the Undercity.",al={"why does renferrel want me","renferrel wolf hearts"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends you to Renferrel?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken military commander at the Sepulcher, delivers Renferrel's summons to you once you report back from aiding his Deathstalkers.",al={"who gives speak with renferrel","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What follows this conversation?",a="Speaking with Renferrel leads directly into tasks that help connect the Sepulcher's regional alchemical research with senior figures like Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.",al={"next quest after speak with renferrel","renferrel follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec send you to Renferrel?",a="High Executor Hadrec is simply passing along a formal summons on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society. While you were scouting the Silverpine front lines for the Deathstalkers, Apothecary Renferrel requested your return to discuss the wolf hearts you previously gathered for his alchemical research. Hadrec ensures that vital business between the military post and the Society continues smoothly.",al={"hadrec motive","why does hadrec want me to speak with renferrel","why send me to apothecary renferrel"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society works closely with military command at the Sepulcher, ensuring every biological anomaly in Silverpine is studied to benefit the Dark Lady's goals.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde establishes footholds across Lordaeron, understanding the corruption affecting local beasts is vital to securing the wilderness."},kw={"hadrec","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","silverpine","wolf hearts"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","quest:449","quest:1359","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="12",faction="Horde",id=3221},src={"Speak with Renferrel"}}
E["quest:421"] = {t="quest",n="Prove Your Worth",z="silverpine",s="Prove Your Worth is an introductory Horde quest offered by Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. To assist the Forsaken campaign against southern human and dwarven territories, adventurers are tasked with thinning the feral worgen prowling near the roadside. It marks the opening step in unraveling the arcane fallout wrought by Archmage Arugal.",h="Prove Your Worth is an introductory Horde quest offered by Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher in Silverpine...",sec={{t="Securing the Southern Corridor",b="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her dreadlord lieutenant, Varimathras, have set their sights on securing the regions south of Tirisfal Glades, including human and dwarven enclaves. However, the path through Silverpine Forest remains fraught with danger. Instead of an open staging ground, the Forsaken find their supply lines and forward bases threatened by feral Moonrage worgen that roam the pine-choked hills.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Blight",b="The presence of these beasts is no natural occurrence. Dalar Dawnweaver points the finger directly at Arugal, a disgraced former mage of Dalaran who unleashed otherworldly worgen upon the region during the Scourge invasion. Arugal has since claimed Shadowfang Keep, letting his feral creations overrun the forest. Before Dalar will entrust soldiers with deeper investigations into Arugal's sorcery, recruits must demonstrate their martial prowess by culling the nearest Moonrage Whitescalps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage stationed at the Sepulcher. He oversees efforts to counter the magical threats in Silverpine Forest, focusing primarily on neutralizing Archmage Arugal and his feral worgen pack.",al={"dalar dawnweaver","who gives prove your worth","sepulcher questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Moonrage Whitescalps located?",a="The Whitescalps prowl just off the main roadway down the hill from the Sepulcher, infesting the woods and ruined homesteads of central Silverpine Forest.",al={"where are whitescalps","moonrage whitescalps location","whitescalp farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde care about worgen in Silverpine?",a="Silverpine Forest is a vital strategic corridor linking the Undercity to the southern lands. Lady Sylvanas and Varimathras require safe transit to project power southward, making the aggressive worgen packs an intolerable hazard.",al={"why kill worgen","forsaken worgen problem","why clear silverpine"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Arugal's connection to these creatures?",a="Archmage Arugal summoned the extradimensional worgen to fight the Scourge while serving Dalaran. The summoned beasts turned wild, driving Arugal mad with guilt before he retreated to Shadowfang Keep to foster the curse.",al={"how did worgen get here","arugal worgen connection","who summoned worgen"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after proving your worth to Dalar?",a="Once you prove your combat capability by slaying the Whitescalps, Dalar Dawnweaver enlists you directly into his campaign to dismantle Arugal's influence through the multi-part quest chain titled Arugal's Folly.",al={"next quest","what follows prove your worth","arugal's folly start"},it="next_step"},{q="Is the Alliance involved in this quest?",a="No. Prove Your Worth is exclusively a Horde quest given at the Forsaken outpost of the Sepulcher.",al={"can alliance do prove your worth","alliance silverpine"},it="side"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want this done?",a="Lady Sylvanas tasked Varimathras with conquering the human and dwarven territories to the south, making Silverpine Forest an essential strategic corridor for the Forsaken. However, the mage Arugal's reckless conjurations have overrun the woods with feral worgen. Before Dalar can commit to a campaign against Arugal's curse and secure the region, he needs capable fighters who can clear the surrounding wilderness and handle the feral beasts.",al={"dalar dawnweaver motive","why prove your worth","why does dalar want whitescalps killed"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are Moonrage Whitescalps?",a="Moonrage Whitescalps are feral worgen roaming the hills and woods near the Sepulcher. Once human villagers and defenders of Silverpine, they fell victim to Archmage Arugal's summoned curse, transforming into vicious, predatory beasts that threaten Forsaken expansion and control across the forest.",al={"moonrage whitescalps","who are the whitescalps","what are we killing"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, clearing Silverpine is essential to securing the Undercity's borders and eliminating threats left behind by Dalaran's failures.",["class:Mage"]="Dalar Dawnweaver's mission serves as a stark warning to spellcasters about the catastrophic risks of reckless conjuration magic, epitomized by Arugal.",["faction:Horde"]="Taming the wilds of Silverpine ensures the Horde retains an unimpeded military highway toward southern Lordaeron."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","moonrage whitescalps","prove your worth","sepulcher","shadowfang keep","silverpine forest","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","quest:99","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","npc:arugal","zone:shadowfang","npc:varimathras","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="10",faction="Horde",id=421},src={"Prove Your Worth (Classic)"}}
E["quest:422"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="Assigned by Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher, this quest tasks Forsaken agents with securing Arugal's earliest spellbooks from a nearby farmstead. Uncovering the magic behind the worgen curse is vital for the Forsaken to turn it against the mad mage and secure Silverpine Forest. Recovering the Remedy of Arugal marks the first step in unraveling the threat looming from Shadowfang Keep.",h="Assigned by Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher, this quest tasks Forsaken agents with securing Arugal's...",sec={{t="A Mage's Derision",b="Dalar Dawnweaver, an ambitious Forsaken mage residing in the crypts of the Sepulcher, holds no respect for Archmage Arugal. To Dawnweaver, Arugal was an unremarkable practitioner whose inclusion in the Kirin Tor was baffling and whose magical understanding seemed amateurish. However, the monstrous beasts now roaming Silverpine cannot be ignored. To break Arugal's hold on the region, Dawnweaver intends to deconstruct the spells that unleashed the worgen upon Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Remnants on the Farmstead",b="Before seizing Shadowfang Keep, Arugal resided at a secluded wheat farm just north of the river bridge. Deathstalker scouts spotted discarded spellbooks preserved on the upper floor of the farmhouse, though lingering beasts prevented them from recovering the texts. Sifting through the dusty grimoires yields the incantation known as the Remedy of Arugal, revealing crucial insights into the unnatural curse spreading across Silverpine Forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Dedicated to Sylvanas Windrunner, he seeks to dissect and counteract the magical practices of Archmage Arugal to claim the territory for the Forsaken.",al={"dalar dawnweaver","who gives arugal's folly","sepulcher mage"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Remedy of Arugal?",a="It is a specific spell transcribed in Arugal's discarded books, dating back to when he lived on the farm north of the bridge. Dalar Dawnweaver requires this incantation to analyze the arcane foundations of Arugal's work.",al={"remedy of arugal","arugal's remedy","what is the book"},it="item"},{q="Where are Arugal's old spellbooks located?",a="The dusty spellbooks are kept on the upper floor of an abandoned farmhouse at the wheat farm situated just north of the bridge crossing in northern Silverpine.",al={"where are the books","dusty spellbooks location","farmhouse books"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dawnweaver look down on Arugal?",a="Dawnweaver views Arugal as an inferior wizard whose understanding of the arcane was superficial and transparent. He finds it baffling that the Kirin Tor ever accepted Arugal into their ranks in Dalaran.",al={"why dawnweaver hate arugal","dawnweaver opinion on arugal"}},{q="Why is this task important to the Forsaken?",a="The worgen created by Arugal slaughter Forsaken forces and threaten their grip on Silverpine Forest. By analyzing his spells, the Forsaken hope to neutralize the threat and secure the region for the Dark Lady.",al={"forsaken interest in arugal","why do forsaken care about arugal"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you touch the dusty spellbooks?",a="Disturbing the grimoires alerts a Moonrage worgen lurking within the farmhouse, which immediately attacks anyone attempting to meddle with Arugal's left-behind research.",al={"spellbook trap","moonrage darkrunner attack"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For Forsaken mages, studying Arugal's work offers a sharp lesson in how disastrously dangerous magic can become when wielded without discipline or proper foresight.",["race:Undead"]="Silverpine is the western shield of the Undercity. Reclaiming it from feral worgen is essential to securing the Dark Lady's borders.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's presence in Silverpine is contested by feral beasts; neutralizing Arugal is critical to establishing stable supply lines out of Lordaeron."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","dusty spellbooks","kirin tor","remedy of arugal","sepulcher","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","quest:421","quest:99","topic:forsaken","quest:1886"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="11",faction="Horde",id=422,ri={"Remedy of Arugal"}},src={"Arugal's Folly"}}
E["quest:423"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="This task sends Forsaken agents to collect enchanted shackles from Moonrage worgen roaming Silverpine Forest. Dalar Dawnweaver, analyzing Arugal's notes, aims to unravel how the renegade mage artificially reinforced his unstable magic. Studying these bindings brings the Forsaken closer to dismantling the worgen threat plaguing the region.",h="This task sends Forsaken agents to collect enchanted shackles from Moonrage worgen roaming Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Hack's Shortcut",b="Upon inspecting Arugal's recovered research, Dalar Dawnweaver expresses utter contempt for his former peer. According to Dalar, Arugal was never fit to serve Dalaran, let alone handle high sorcery during the kingdom's direst hour. To compensate for his mediocre talent, Arugal relied on enchanted relics and hardware to bolster and bind his summoned worgen beasts. Dalar requires physical samples of these items to dissect the magical tether holding the monsters together.",sp=0},{t="The Moonrage Bindings",b="The cursed inhabitants of Silverpine, transformed into Moonrage worgen, wander the woods carrying physical manifestations of Arugal's binding enchantments. Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls stalk the regions to the north and east of the Sepulcher. Prized for the residual arcane energy woven into their metal, their heavy shackles serve as crucial specimens for Dawnweaver's counter-research against Shadowfang Keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want worgen shackles?",a="Dalar determined that Arugal used enchanted items to compensate for weak magical talent. By examining the enchanted shackles worn by Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls, Dalar hopes to extract their magical energy and uncover how Arugal commands his beasts.",al={"why collect shackles","purpose of worgen shackles","dalar dawnweaver plan"},it="motive"},{q="Who was Arugal before he went mad in Silverpine?",a="Arugal was a mage of Dalaran. According to Dalar Dawnweaver, Arugal was considered a mediocre talent within the Kirin Tor, but during the Third War he turned to forbidden extra-planar summoning to unleash the worgen against the Scourge.",al={"arugal backstory","who is arugal","arugal dalaran"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls found?",a="These savage worgen roam the wilds north and east of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, prowling near old ruins and forested trails.",al={"where to find gluttons","darksoul location","worgen locations silverpine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken so concerned with Arugal?",a="Arugal's worgen overrun Silverpine Forest, directly threatening the Sepulcher and the Forsaken's territorial control south of Tirisfal Glades. Neutralizing his magic is critical to securing the northern kingdom.",al={"forsaken worgen threat","why fight arugal"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Dalar Dawnweaver think of Dalaran?",a="Dalar holds bitter disdain for his former peers in Dalaran, viewing them as fools for trusting Arugal with responsibilities he was not competent enough to handle.",al={"dalar dalaran opinion","dalar on kirin tor"},it="history"},{q="Is Arugal working with the Scourge?",a="No. Arugal originally summoned the worgen to fight the Scourge to defend Dalaran. However, the beasts turned wild and drove him mad, leading him to claim Shadowfang Keep as his personal domain.",al={"arugal scourge alliance","is arugal scourge"},it="side"},{q="What are the Glutton and Darksoul Shackles used for?",a="These enchanted metal bands are forged by Archmage Arugal to reinforce his otherwise weak spellcraft and anchor his command over the worgen. Because Arugal lacked the innate power to control the feral beasts summoned to Silverpine, he bound them with these magical fetters. Dalar Dawnweaver requires them to study their enchantments and extract their residual energies, hoping to unravel Arugal's crude magic and devise a way to neutralize the worgen threat.",al={"glutton shackle","darksoul shackle","arugal shackles use"},it="item",add=true},{q="What are Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls?",a="They are vicious worgen prowling the woods of northern and eastern Silverpine Forest. Once summoned into this world by Arugal to repel the Scourge, the monstrous beasts quickly slipped from his control and overran the local lands. Bound by enchanted shackles that channel Arugal's crude magic, these corrupted predators now stalk the forest, terrorizing both surviving locals and Forsaken scouts traveling through the region.",al={"moonrage worgen","who are moonrage gluttons","moonrage darksouls"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing Silverpine from feral worgen is essential to protecting the southern border of Tirisfal Glades and cementing Queen Sylvanas's domain.",["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages can appreciate Dalar's scathing professional critique: Arugal compensated for shoddy arcane fundamentals by channeling power through physical enchanted bindings.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the woods of Silverpine ensures safe transit along the high road connecting Tirisfal to regions further south."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran","darksoul","glutton","kirin tor","sepulcher","shackles","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","quest:99","npc:arugal","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:421","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="14",faction="Horde",id=423,ri={"Darksoul Shackle","Glutton Shackle"}},src={"Arugal's Folly (2)"}}
E["quest:424"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="Arugal's Folly is a key quest in the Sepulcher's ongoing campaign against the mad archmage's influence across Silverpine Forest. Dalar Dawnweaver tasks Horde adventurers with infiltrating Deep Elem Mine to execute the corrupted foreman, Grimson the Pale, securing vital mineral wealth for Varimathras's forces.",h="Arugal's Folly is a key quest in the Sepulcher's ongoing campaign against the mad archmage's influence across...",sec={{t="Securing the Depths",b="While unraveling the dark enchantments Archmage Arugal unleashed upon the forest, Dalar Dawnweaver receives urgent intelligence from the Forsaken Darkstalkers. The feral sorcery spreading from Shadowfang Keep has reached the Deep Elem Mine in the southeastern hills, turning the miners into savage wretches. The mine holds crucial ore needed to fuel Undercity's militarization, but its current occupants render it completely unusable.",sp=0},{t="The Severed Head",b="At the heart of the infested shafts lurks Grimson the Pale, the tainted foreman who directs the mad remnant within the subterranean tunnels. Dawnweaver orders an immediate decapitation strike: with Grimson slain and his head returned to the Sepulcher, the scattered mine workers will lose their coordination, allowing Forsaken laborers to claim the excavation for Lord Varimathras.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grimson the Pale?",a="Grimson the Pale is the foreman of Deep Elem Mine. Like many laborers and residents in southern Silverpine, he fell under the corrupting magical influence radiating from Archmage Arugal's experiments, becoming a twisted figure overseeing an infested subterranean den.",al={"grimson","who is grimson","deep elem foreman"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Deep Elem Mine located?",a="Deep Elem Mine lies in the craggy hills southeast of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Its tunnels cut deep into the hillside, teeming with cursed miners and ferals.",al={"deep elem mine location","where is deep elem","where to find grimson"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Varimathras care about a mining operation?",a="Varimathras oversees the strategic expansion of Forsaken power. High-yield resources like iron and stone from Deep Elem Mine are vital for arming troops and reinforcing fortresses throughout Lordaeron.",al={"why varimathras want mine","varimathras interest"}},{q="What happens after Grimson is slain?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver takes Grimson's head as proof of victory and turns his focus back to the primary threat, preparing to strike directly at the core of Arugal's encroaching presence.",al={"after arugals folly 3","what next","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What kind of magic corrupted the mine?",a="Archmage Arugal unleashed wild otherworldly magic and worgen curses across Silverpine. That tainted energy drifted into the subterranean workers of Deep Elem, driving them mad and mutating their minds.",al={"arugals magic in mine","what corrupted deep elem","mine curse"}},{q="Who are the Darkstalkers mentioned by Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="The Darkstalkers are the covert intelligence and scouting branch of the Forsaken military, operating out of outposts like the Sepulcher to monitor enemy troop movements and regional anomalies.",al={"darkstalkers","who are darkstalkers"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Grimson the Pale killed?",a="While Dalar studies Arugal's dark enchantments, he must also answer to Varimathras, who demands the Deep Elem Mine to fuel the Forsaken's military advance across Silverpine. Arugal's spreading magic tainted the mine and corrupted its foreman, Grimson the Pale. Slain, Grimson's hold over the site will break, securing a critical source of ore and metal for the Forsaken while keeping Dalar in good standing with the dreadlord.",al={"why kill grimson","dalar dawnweaver motive","why does dalar want the mine"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Head of Grimson for?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver requires Grimson's severed head as undeniable proof that the tainted foreman is dead. With Varimathras demanding swift results for his campaign, Dalar cannot afford any doubt that the Deep Elem Mine has been cleared of its corrupted overseer and is ready to be claimed.",al={"why take grimson's head","head of grimson purpose","grimson head quest"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every strategic holding captured from Arugal's mad thralls provides the Forsaken with raw metal to fortify their young nation against the living and the Scourge.",["profession:Mining"]="The rich subterranean veins of Deep Elem Mine are coveted across the hills, offering valuable ore once cleared of hostile tainted workers.",["class:Mage"]="Studying how Arugal's runaway conjurations and transmutations seeped into the mines offers a harrowing lesson in magical recklessness."},kw={"arugal's folly","dalar dawnweaver","deep elem mine","grimson the pale","sepulcher","silverpine forest","varimathras"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","subzone:deep-elem-mine","npc:arugal","npc:varimathras","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:421"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="15",faction="Horde",id=424,ri={"Head of Grimson"}},src={"Arugal's Folly (3)"}}
E["quest:425"] = {t="quest",n="Ivar the Foul",z="silverpine",s="Ivar the Foul is a quest in Silverpine Forest that marks the culmination of the reconnaissance mission undertaken by Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick. Trapped at the farmstead known as the Ivar Patch, Rane asks Horde travelers to eliminate the savage ghoul Ivar the Foul so Quinn can recover from his mauling and complete their report to High Executor Hadrec.",h="Ivar the Foul is a quest in Silverpine Forest that marks the culmination of the reconnaissance mission...",sec={{t="A Mission Derailed",b="Siblings Rane and Quinn Yorick were deployed by the Deathstalkers to conduct reconnaissance across Silverpine Forest on behalf of High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher. Their reconnaissance grinded to a sudden, violent halt when moving through a farmstead in the northern forest, where they were ambushed by the vicious ghoul known as Ivar the Foul.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Barn",b="Though the scouts managed to escape with their unlives, Quinn was severely mauled in the confrontation. Even after receiving an alchemical remedy concocted from forest beasts, Quinn remains too frail to march. Knowing Ivar prowls the nearby barn waiting for Rane's guard to falter, Rane calls upon Horde adventurers to storm the barn, sever Ivar's head, and permanently secure the homestead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ivar the Foul?",a="Ivar the Foul is a dangerous Scourge ghoul lingering in the northern reaches of Silverpine Forest. He took over a farmstead now known as the Ivar Patch, ambushing passersby and savaging Forsaken scouts.",al={"who is ivar","ivar the foul lore","what is ivar the foul"},it="target"},{q="Where can Ivar the Foul be found?",a="Ivar lurks inside the dilapidated barn at the Ivar Patch, situated just north of the ruined farmhouse where Rane and Quinn Yorick have taken shelter.",al={"ivar location","where is ivar","ivar the foul barn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are Rane and Quinn Yorick?",a="Rane and Quinn Yorick are Forsaken siblings, a sister and brother, and Deathstalkers. They were dispatched by High Executor Hadrec to map and survey enemy activity within Silverpine Forest before being ambushed by Ivar.",al={"who is rane yorick","yorick brothers","who is quinn yorick"},it="people"},{q="Why does Rane ask an adventurer to kill Ivar?",a="Quinn was grievously mauled during their initial encounter and is still convalescing. Rane must stay by her brother's side to guard him against sudden Scourge attacks, making it impossible for her to hunt down the ghoul herself.",al={"why kill ivar","why doesn't rane fight"},it="motive"},{q="Who receives the report on Ivar's death?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the military commander seated at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, receives the scouts' official reconnaissance logs, in which Rane promises to commend the adventurer's assistance.",al={"who is hadrec","who sent the yoricks"}},{q="What happens after Ivar is slain?",a="Slaying Ivar the Foul concludes the Deathstalkers' ordeal at the Ivar Patch. With the immediate threat removed, Quinn has the time needed to heal before the siblings finish their survey of the forest.",al={"what next after ivar","quest after ivar"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Ivar's Head for?",a="Bringing severed heads back to your commander or patron is standard protocol in Lordaeron's wild frontier. Rane Yorick demands Ivar's head as indisputable proof that the vicious ghoul has been permanently destroyed. With Quinn incapacitated and vulnerable in their makeshift shelter, Rane cannot afford to take anyone's word on faith: only the creature's decapitated head guarantees his brother has the time he needs to recover safely.",al={"ivar head","why ivar head","what is ivars head for"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Rane Yorick need an adventurer to kill Ivar?",a="Rane cannot leave his brother's side. The ghoul savagely mauled Quinn during their initial scout, leaving him bedridden and reliant on healing draughts to mend his broken frame. With Ivar lurking in the nearby barn waiting for Rane's vigilance to slip, abandoning Quinn even briefly would leave him completely defenseless against a second strike. Far from Undercity reinforcements or The Sepulcher's patrols, an outside mercenary is their only lifeline.",al={"why rane cant kill ivar","why me ivar the foul","why not kill ivar himself"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The mission emphasizes the perilous duty of the Deathstalkers, demonstrating how lone Forsaken scouts must rely on wandering champions when cornered behind enemy lines.",["faction:Horde"]="By clearing Scourge remnants like Ivar, Horde forces protect vital supply lines and strategic ground for the Forsaken war effort in Lordaeron.",["class:Rogue"]="Assisting the Deathstalkers showcases the dangers of stealth reconnaissance when caught unawares by ravenous Scourge horrors."},kw={"deathstalkers","ghoul","hadrec","ivar","ivar patch","ivar the foul","quinn yorick","rane yorick","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:430","quest:429","quest:428","subzone:ivar-patch","zone:silverpine","npc:high-executor-hadrec","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Rane Yorick",level="12",faction="Horde",id=425,ri={"Ivar's Head"}},src={"Ivar the Foul (quest)"}}
E["quest:428"] = {t="quest",n="Lost Deathstalkers",z="silverpine",s="Lost Deathstalkers is a reconnaissance mission assigned by High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher. Two Forsaken scouts, Rane and Quinn Yorick, went missing weeks ago while surveying the haunted farmsteads of northern Silverpine Forest. Tracking them down reveals not only their fate, but the encroaching perils that threaten the Forsaken hold on the region.",h="Lost Deathstalkers is a reconnaissance mission assigned by High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Silence from the North",b="The Deathstalkers serve as the eyes, ears, and hidden daggers of Lady Sylvanas and the Forsaken. When operatives go silent, command takes notice. High Executor Hadrec deployed the scouts Rane and Quinn Yorick into northern Silverpine Forest weeks ago to monitor the abandoned farms and watch for enemy movements. Having received no courier or report since their departure, Hadrec fears the duo met a grim end at the hands of the Scourge or worse.",sp=0},{t="The Northern Peril",b="Northern Silverpine is rife with danger, situated between the ruined estates of Lordaeron and the shadowed borders of Tirisfal Glades. Wandering undead, prowling beasts, and feral worgen make unescorted travel perilous even for seasoned rogues. Tracking the Yoricks requires searching the dilapidated northern farmsteads where their reconnaissance first began, hoping to recover whatever intelligence they gathered before danger overwhelmed them.",sp=0},{t="Trapped in the Shadows",b="Upon following their trail, Rane and Quinn Yorick are revealed to be alive, though barely clinging to freedom. They escaped an attack by the ghoul Ivar the Foul, but Quinn was badly mauled, and the Deathstalkers now find themselves cornered at the farm while the ghoul lurks nearby. Rescuing them pulls the Forsaken deeper into dealing with the feral threats prowling just beyond the road.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are Rane and Quinn Yorick?",a="Rane and Quinn Yorick are two Forsaken scouts belonging to the Deathstalkers, the intelligence and assassination wing of the Forsaken. They were dispatched north into Silverpine Forest to surveil local farmsteads before disappearing.",al={"who are the yoricks","who are the lost deathstalkers","rane and quinn lore"},it="people"},{q="Why is High Executor Hadrec concerned about them?",a="Hadrec oversees Forsaken military operations from the Sepulcher. Losing communication with two key reconnaissance operatives leaves the Forsaken blind to hostile activity along their northern borders, especially with the Scourge lingering nearby.",al={"why hadrec care","who sent the yoricks","hadrec lost scouts"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the Yoricks disappear?",a="They vanished while scouting northern Silverpine Forest. Their reconnaissance route focused on the scattered, decaying farmsteads situated north of the Sepulcher.",al={"where are the deathstalkers","yorick location","where to find rane and quinn"},it="place"},{q="What threats do the Deathstalkers face in northern Silverpine?",a="Northern Silverpine is plagued by roaming Scourge remnants, aggressive predators, and unnatural worgen prowling the woods, any of which pose lethal hazards to isolated scouts.",al={"what happened to them","silverpine dangers","why did they go missing"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after finding the missing Deathstalkers?",a="Finding Rane Yorick opens up the immediate task of helping the battered scouts recover through the quest Wild Hearts, which leads to confronting local threats like Ivar the Foul.",al={"what is the next quest","after lost deathstalkers","quest chain after yorick"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers as an organization?",a="The Deathstalkers are the premier espionage, scouting, and assassination guild of the Forsaken, serving as the secretive vanguard of the Dark Lady across Lordaeron.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker order","forsaken assassins"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken operatives know that every missing agent represents a potential breach in their fragile defense of Silverpine. Securing your own kin keeps the Sepulcher safe from sudden assault.",["class:Rogue"]="The Yoricks are fellow operatives of the shadows. Seeing experienced Deathstalkers pinned down serves as a sharp reminder that stealth alone cannot guarantee survival against the northern horrors.",["faction:Horde"]="Holding Silverpine Forest ensures a safe corridor between Undercity and the southern reaches of Lordaeron, making reconnaissance missions like this critical to Horde security."},kw={"deathstalkers","hadrec","quinn yorick","rane yorick","reconnaissance","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:quinn-yorick","quest:429","quest:430","quest:425","quest:1886","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Rane Yorick",level="12",faction="Horde",id=428},src={"Lost Deathstalkers"}}
E["quest:429"] = {t="quest",n="Wild Hearts",z="silverpine",s="Wild Hearts is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest tasked by Rane Yorick. To save her brother Quinn from wounds inflicted by the ghoul Ivar the Foul, you must harvest discolored worg hearts and deliver them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher for an alchemical remedy.",h="Wild Hearts is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest tasked by Rane Yorick.",sec={{t="A Brother's Desperation",b="Following the disastrous mission that left the Deathstalkers pinned down at a farm in northern Silverpine, Rane Yorick finds herself attending to her severely wounded brother, Quinn. The feral ghoul Ivar the Foul left Quinn mangled and failing to recover. Knowing conventional rest will not restore an undead body torn by such savagery, Rane looks to the macabre arts of the Royal Apothecary Society to stitch her brother back together.",sp=0},{t="Alchemy of the Scourge-Tainted Wilds",b="Silverpine's wolves have not escaped the dark corruption plaguing northern Lordaeron. The local worgs carry corrupted, discolored hearts that contain uniquely potent essences. While vile to ordinary eyes, the Royal Apothecaries have learned to distill these blighted organs into concoctions capable of revitalizing withered Forsaken flesh.",sp=0},{t="Renferrel's Cold Duty",b="Stationed within the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel views the incident with frustration rather than sympathy. Tasked directly by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner with pressing research, Renferrel resents the Royal Apothecary Society being treated as field medics for blundering scouts. Nevertheless, he accepts the gruesome ingredients and prepares the draught to keep the Dark Lady's agents operational.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Quinn Yorick need worg hearts to heal?",a="Forsaken physiology does not heal like the living. After sustaining grievous wounds from the ghoul Ivar the Foul, Quinn requires specialized alchemical aid. The Royal Apothecary Society utilizes the tainted, discolored hearts of Silverpine worgs to brew restorative tonics tailored for undead tissue.",al={"why worg hearts","quinn healing","healing potion recipe"},it="item"},{q="Where can the discolored worg hearts be found?",a="The worgs roam throughout the woods of central Silverpine Forest, particularly in the untamed stretches between the road where the Yorick siblings are stranded and Malden's Orchard to the east.",al={"where are the worgs","worg locations silverpine","worg heart farming"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Ivar the Foul?",a="Ivar the Foul is a dangerous ghoul lurking at the farm where the Yoricks took shelter. He attacked Rane and Quinn Yorick as they scouted through, and though both escaped, he left Quinn badly mauled.",al={"who is ivar","ivar the foul lore","ghoul ivar"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Apothecary Renferrel annoyed by the task?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is stationed at the Sepulcher on direct orders from Sylvanas Windrunner to advance critical plague research. He considers Deathstalkers failing their scouting missions an embarrassment and an unnecessary distraction from his grander alchemical experiments.",al={"why is renferrel mad","renferrel dialogue","renferrel's attitude"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after giving the hearts to Renferrel?",a="Once Renferrel processes the discolored hearts, he sends you back to Rane and Quinn Yorick with the restorative potion so Quinn can recover sufficiently to seek vengeance.",al={"next quest after wild hearts","what to do with the potion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers need help from an adventurer?",a="Rane Yorick cannot leave her brother's side due to the severity of Quinn's injuries and the danger of further ambushes from roaming Scourge and beasts. She relies on passing Horde travelers to harvest the organs and deliver the plea to the Sepulcher.",al={"why can't rane get the hearts","deathstalker failure"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick need you to gather worg hearts?",a="Rane Yorick is desperate to save his brother, Quinn, who was gravely injured in a disastrous skirmish against the powerful ghoul Ivar the Foul. Knowing ordinary rest will not suffice to mend Quinn's damaged undead frame, Rane seeks an apothecary's concoction made from local worg hearts to restore him before he succumbs to his wounds.",al={"why does rane want worg hearts","rane yorick motive","why help quinn yorick"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The quest highlights the pragmatic ruthlessness of the Forsaken; even in brotherhood, survival hinges on scavenged organs and cold alchemical science rather than divine grace.",["class:Rogue"]="Seeing seasoned Deathstalkers brought low by a feral ghoul serves as a grim warning about the stealth and lethality required to survive the Lordaeron wilderness."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","discolored worg heart","ivar the foul","maldens orchard","quinn yorick","rane yorick","sepulcher","silverpine forest","wild hearts"},rel={"quest:428","quest:430","quest:425","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:malden-s-orchard","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Rane Yorick",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="11",faction="Horde",id=429,ri={"Discolored Worg Heart"}},src={"Wild Hearts"}}
E["quest:430"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Quinn",z="silverpine",s="Return to Quinn is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest where an adventurer delivers a restorative draught concocted by Apothecary Renferrel to the wounded Deathstalker Quinn Yorick. Trapped and weakened at the Ivar Patch north of the Sepulcher, Quinn requires the draught before he can contemplate returning to duty.",h="Return to Quinn is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest where an adventurer delivers a restorative draught...",sec={{t="A Bitter Draught",b="Following the harvesting of wild beast hearts for the Royal Apothecary Society, Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher brews a restorative potion formulated to aid Quinn Yorick. Renferrel has little time for sentimentality or bedside manners, quickly handing off the mixture to return to his own clandestine alchemical research, leaving the adventurer to run the courier run back into the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Respite at the Ivar Patch",b="Quinn Yorick hides beside his sister, Deathstalker Rane Yorick, amid the ruined farmstead known as the Ivar Patch. Severely hurt by the ghoul Ivar the Foul and unable to march through hostile territory, Quinn drinks the draught immediately upon arrival. While the concoction restores his strength enough to eventually travel, the surrounding territory remains fraught with danger, particularly under the watchful malice of the ghoul lurking nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Quinn Yorick located?",a="Quinn Yorick is sheltered at the Ivar Patch, an abandoned farmstead located just north of the Sepulcher along the western bluffs of Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is quinn","quinn yorick location","ivar patch location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who made the potion for Quinn?",a="Apothecary Renferrel, an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in the crypts of the Sepulcher, brewed the potion using wild beast hearts collected from the forest.",al={"who brewed the potion","apothecary renferrel potion"},it="origin"},{q="Why was Quinn unable to move on his own?",a="Quinn was ambushed and badly mauled by the ghoul Ivar the Foul while scouting the area with his sister, leaving him incapacitated and dependent on his sister Rane and medicinal aid to recover.",al={"why is quinn stuck","quinn yorick injured"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after giving Quinn the potion?",a="Drinking the concoction restores Quinn's strength, paving the way to strike back against Ivar the Foul, the dangerous ghoul threatening their position.",al={"what next after return to quinn","next quest after quinn"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Quinn's sister?",a="Quinn's sister is Deathstalker Rane Yorick, who stayed by his side at the Ivar Patch to protect him and coordinate their survival.",al={"quinn yorick sister","quinn sister"},it="ties"},{q="Does Apothecary Renferrel care about Quinn's fate?",a="Renferrel shows minimal personal concern, viewing the concoction purely as an errand before dismissing the adventurer so he can resume his own secretive research for the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"does renferrel care","renferrel attitude"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel send you back to Quinn instead of going himself?",a="Apothecary Renferrel views Quinn Yorick's plight as little more than an inconvenience that interrupts his true research for the Royal Apothecary Society. Having concocted the restorative draught from the wolf hearts you supplied, Renferrel is eager to return immediately to his alchemical experiments and considers courier work beneath him. Entrusting the delivery to an adventurer lets him resume his studies without wasting further time.",al={"why send me","why renounce quinn delivery","renferrel why me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The mission illustrates the practical utility of the Royal Apothecary Society, providing vital restorative mixtures to keep the Dark Lady's scouts operational in hostile terrain.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing scouts stranded behind enemy lines is crucial for cementing the Horde's foothold across Silverpine Forest against feral worgen packs.",["class:Rogue"]="Assisting fellow operatives of the Deathstalkers highlights the perilous reality of reconnaissance work when caught unawares by pack predators."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","deathstalker erland","deathstalkers","ivar patch","quinn yorick","quinn's potion","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:429","quest:425","quest:428","npc:quinn-yorick","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:ivar-patch","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Quinn Yorick",level="11",faction="Horde",id=430},src={"Return to Quinn"}}
E["quest:435"] = {t="quest",n="Escorting Erland",z="silverpine",s="Trapped indoors by aggressive prowling predators, Deathstalker Erland requires an escort through Silverpine Forest to regroup with his partner. Assisting him safely across the wilderness delivers him directly to Deathstalker Rane Yorick.",h="Trapped indoors by aggressive prowling predators, Deathstalker Erland requires an escort through Silverpine...",sec={{t="Cornered by Wolves",b="Even seasoned scouts of the Forsaken occasionally find themselves outmatched by the unforgiving ecology of Silverpine Forest. Deathstalker Erland finds himself cornered inside a dilapidated shelter, surrounded by starved wolves eager to pick at what little flesh remains on his withered frame. Alone, breaking through their pack is suicide.",sp=0},{t="A Treacherous Crossing",b="Erland's objective lies near the Ivar Patch, where his partner Deathstalker Rane Yorick maintains watch. The route cuts directly through predatory wolf territory. Once guided through the prowlers, Erland sprints the final stretch to reach the safety of Rane Yorick's outpost, where the scouts can consolidate their intelligence for the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the wolves hunting an undead scout?",a="As Erland dryly observes, the beasts in Silverpine must be desperate with hunger if they view a desiccated Forsaken corpse as a viable meal. The feral wildlife of the forest is notoriously aggressive to anything moving through their territory.",al={"why wolves attack undead","why eat undead","erland wolves"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Deathstalker Erland reporting to?",a="Erland is reporting to Deathstalker Rane Yorick, his scouting partner stationed in a nearby farmhouse near the Ivar Patch. Together, they monitor threats in the woods for the Forsaken.",al={"who is rane yorick","who does erland report to","erland partner"},it="people"},{q="Where does the escort lead?",a="Erland moves from his refuge out through the wilderness toward the Ivar Patch, ultimately running inside a farmhouse and heading upstairs to join Deathstalker Rane Yorick.",al={"escort destination","where does erland go","erland route"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Erland is rescued?",a="Once Erland is safely reunited with Rane Yorick, the two scouts prepare their findings. Rane Yorick subsequently entrusts you with carrying their compiled dispatch back to the Sepulcher in the quest 'The Deathstalkers' Report'.",al={"what next after escorting erland","the deathstalkers report quest","what follows erland escort"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are there other threats encountered during the escort?",a="The primary danger comes from the packs of wolves patrolling the open ground between Erland's starting location and the farm near the Ivar Patch.",al={"escort enemies","what attacks erland","what is on the road"},it="threat"},{q="What role do Deathstalkers play in Silverpine?",a="Deathstalkers serve as the elite rogues, scouts, and assassins of the Forsaken. In Silverpine Forest, they are deployed ahead of main garrisons to track Scourge stragglers, Worgen incursions, feral beasts, and Alliance movements.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker role","deathstalker lore"},it="people"},{q="Why does Deathstalker Erland want an escort?",a="Erland is trapped inside his shelter by a pack of ravenous Silverpine wolves prowling right outside the doorway. Cut off from his fellow scout, Rane Yorick, he cannot deliver his scouting observations or fulfill his mission for the Forsaken while cornered alone. To break through the surrounding beasts and reach safety, he desperately requires your armed protection.",al={"why does erland need an escort","erland escort why","why does deathstalker erland need help"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Erland need your help rather than other Deathstalkers?",a="Deathstalkers operate as isolated reconnaissance agents in hostile frontier territory rather than marching in large battalions. Erland and Rane Yorick are stationed far from the safety of Undercity reinforcements, leaving Erland pinned down with no guards or fellow agents nearby to relieve him. You are the only capable ally within reach to break the siege.",al={"why erland need me","why can't guards help erland","why does erland ask me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken Deathstalkers rely heavily on teamwork and stealth; finding an operative pinned down by simple beasts highlights just how dangerous Silverpine's wilds can be for the newly risen.",["faction:Horde"]="Aiding isolated Deathstalkers secures crucial forward reconnaissance for Horde forces pushing outward from the Sepulcher."},kw={"deathstalker erland","deathstalkers report","ivar patch","rane yorick","silverpine forest","wolves"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-rane-yorick","quest:449","subzone:ivar-patch","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Deathstalker Erland",["end"]="Rane Yorick",level="11",faction="Horde",id=435,ri={"Deathstalker Shortsword"}},src={"Escorting Erland"}}
E["quest:437"] = {t="quest",n="The Dead Fields",z="silverpine",s="The Dead Fields is an assault mission issued by High Executor Hadrec from the Sepulcher. Forsaken scouts discovered that the Rot Hide gnolls infesting an abandoned northern farmstead are led and shielded by the Scourge banshee Nightlash, whose destruction is critical to securing Silverpine Forest.",h="The Dead Fields is an assault mission issued by High Executor Hadrec from the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Plague upon the Fields",b="North of the Sepulcher lies an abandoned farmstead known as the Dead Fields. Once ordinary farmland, the grounds are now choked by Rot Hide gnolls—pestilent, plagued scavengers that infest the Silverpine countryside. High Executor Hadrec previously sent small raiding parties to dislodge them, but every offensive stalled under unnatural magical resistance.",sp=0},{t="The Banshee's Grasp",b="The Rot Hides are not acting merely on feral instinct; they are reinforced by the Scourge. A banshee named Nightlash oversees the area, using dark sorcery to scatter Forsaken skirmishers whenever the gnolls face ruin. Hadrec dispatches Horde champions to cut down the gnolls until Nightlash is lured out, demanding her spectral essence as proof of her demise.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dead Fields located?",a="The Dead Fields are situated north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. It is an overgrown, decaying farmstead heavily overrun by Rot Hide gnolls.",al={"dead fields location","where is dead field","where to find dead fields"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Nightlash?",a="Nightlash is a Scourge banshee who commands and shields the Rot Hide gnolls at the Dead Fields, using dark magic to drive off previous Forsaken assault parties.",al={"who is nightlash","nightlash lore","banshee nightlash"},it="target"},{q="Why are gnolls working with a banshee?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls of Silverpine Forest are tainted by the plague of undeath. The Scourge uses figures like Nightlash to direct these rabid creatures as vanguard foot soldiers against the Forsaken.",al={"why rot hides with scourge","gnoll scourge connection","rot hide gnolls lore"},it="conflict"},{q="How do you draw out Nightlash?",a="Nightlash remains hidden until the gnolls under her protection are slaughtered in large numbers. Slaying enough Rot Hides forces her to manifest in the middle of the field to defend her domain.",al={"how to spawn nightlash","where is nightlash","nightlash not there"},gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest The Dead Fields?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken military commander stationed at the Sepulcher, issues the quest as part of his campaign to secure the region.",al={"who gives the dead fields","dead fields quest giver","hadrec quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happens after Nightlash is destroyed?",a="Bringing Nightlash's essence to High Executor Hadrec proves the Scourge has lost a vital presence in northern Silverpine, leading Hadrec to turn your attention toward the Decrepit Ferry to the west.",al={"dead fields followup","what comes after dead fields"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want Nightlash destroyed?",a="The rot hide gnolls have entrenched themselves at an old farm known as the Dead Fields, threatening Forsaken operations across Silverpine Forest. Previous assaults sent by High Executor Hadrec failed because the banshee Nightlash intervened, using her dark sorcery to turn the tide and rout his forces. Until Nightlash is eliminated, Hadrec cannot break the rot hide encampment or secure the region for the Dark Lady.",al={"why kill nightlash","hadrec motive dead fields","why attack dead fields"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Essence of Nightlash used for?",a="Upon her defeat, Nightlash dissolves into lingering dust. You collect this residue not as a magical ingredient, but as indisputable physical proof for High Executor Hadrec that the banshee has truly been destroyed and can no longer reinforce the rot hides.",al={"essence of nightlash purpose","why collect nightlash essence","essence of nightlash"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, destroying Nightlash is a personal strike against the Scourge and a grim reminder of the spectral torment Sylvanas and her banshees broke away from.",["faction:Horde"]="Breaking the Scourge hold over northern Silverpine Forest helps safeguard the travel corridor linking the Undercity to the southern territories of Lordaeron."},kw={"banshee","dead fields","hadrec","nightlash","rot hide","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:dead-field","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","topic:scourge","topic:gnoll","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",level="14",faction="Horde",id=437,ri={"Essence of Nightlash"}},src={"The Dead Fields (quest)"}}
E["quest:438"] = {t="quest",n="The Decrepit Ferry",z="silverpine",s="High Executor Hadrec directs Forsaken champions east of The Sepulcher to investigate the Decrepit Ferry. The lakeside dock has been swarmed by Scourge and rot hides, raising alarms about the enemy's expanding footprint along the shores of Lordamere Lake.",h="High Executor Hadrec directs Forsaken champions east of The Sepulcher to investigate the Decrepit Ferry.",sec={{t="Eyes Across the Lake",b="Following the suppression of Scourge presence in the Dead Fields, High Executor Hadrec turned his strategic gaze toward the eastern waterways of Silverpine Forest. The Decrepit Ferry, once a mundane transit crossing linking mainland Lordaeron to the island estates of Lordamere Lake, had quietly evolved into an active hive of undead activity. Hadrec dispatched scouts to discern what drew the Lich King's servants to these rotted piers.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Cargo",b="Reaching the ferry reveals more than just aimless rot hides patrolling the marshy banks. Tucked along the dock sits a waterlogged skiff laden with carefully wrapped, preserved corpses. Looking across the mist of Lordamere Lake, an opposing set of docks on Fenris Isle comes into view, exposing a macabre supply line feeding bodies straight toward the island keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to the Decrepit Ferry?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken military commander stationed at The Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, gives the assignment after you assist with clearing the Dead Fields.",al={"who gives the decrepit ferry quest","hadrec quest ferry","quest giver decrepit ferry"},gp=true},{q="Where is the Decrepit Ferry located?",a="The ferry sits east of The Sepulcher along the western bank of Lordamere Lake, where the inland creeks flow into the open water.",al={"decrepit ferry location","where is the ferry silverpine","how to find decrepit ferry"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures occupy the Decrepit Ferry?",a="The area is overrun by Scourge undead, primarily rot hide gnolls and reanimated skeletons patrolling the shoreline and surrounding docks.",al={"mobs at decrepit ferry","what enemies are at the ferry","decrepit ferry monsters"},it="threat"},{q="What do you discover at the ferry?",a="You find a corpse-laden boat pulled halfway out of the water, containing wrapped bodies positioned to be shipped across the water toward Fenris Isle.",al={"what is at the ferry","ferry turn in object","what is in the boat"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does the Scourge care about the ferry?",a="The ferry serves as a staging and transit point across Lordamere Lake, allowing the Scourge to ferry fresh corpses directly to their stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"why are scourge at decrepit ferry","ferry scourge purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What quest follows The Decrepit Ferry?",a="Examining the corpse-laden boat immediately leads into the quest Rot Hide Clues, prompting you to investigate the gnoll operations and the link to Fenris Isle.",al={"next quest after decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want you to investigate the Decrepit Ferry?",a="The Forsaken keep a precarious hold over Silverpine Forest, and the sudden emergence of a new Scourge hive so close to the Sepulcher threatens their security. High Executor Hadrec cannot ignore an organized enemy concentration directly east of his base. He needs to uncover what purpose brings the rot hides and undead to the shore of Lordamere Lake before they mount an assault against the Forsaken.",al={"hadrec motive decrepit ferry","why send to decrepit ferry","why investigate decrepit ferry"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent against at the Decrepit Ferry?",a="The Decrepit Ferry has been overtaken by the Scourge, specifically packs of rot hide gnolls and walking dead. They are not merely wandering; they actively patrol the ruined docks, securing the site to load wrapped corpses aboard boats bound across Lordamere Lake for Fenris Isle.",al={"decrepit ferry enemies","who controls decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry targets"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, any foothold the Scourge establishes in Silverpine is a direct existential threat to the borders of Tirisfal and the Undercity.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the perimeter around Lordamere Lake ensures Horde supply lines through Silverpine remain protected from northern Scourge incursions."},kw={"corpse laden boat","decrepit ferry","fenris isle","high executor hadrec","lordamere lake","rot hide","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:decrepit-ferry","npc:high-executor-hadrec","quest:439","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:sepulcher","topic:scourge","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Corpse Laden Boat",level="16",faction="Horde",id=438},src={"The Decrepit Ferry (quest)"}}
E["quest:439"] = {t="quest",n="Rot Hide Clues",z="silverpine",s="Investigating a barge loaded with corpses on Lordamere Lake reveals an engraved ring on a recently deceased woman's hand. Reporting the grim discovery to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher exposes a disturbing operation: Rot Hide gnolls are robbing Tirisfal's mass graves and shipping bodies to Fenris Isle.",h="Investigating a barge loaded with corpses on Lordamere Lake reveals an engraved ring on a recently deceased...",sec={{t="A Gruesome Cargo",b="While examining an abandoned, corpse-laden ferry on the shores of Lake Lordamere, Forsaken scouts discover that not all the dead are ancient remains. Protruding from the pile of carrion is the unwrapped, plague-marked hand of a recently slain woman wearing a simple band inscribed with the words 'For Deliah'. The boat itself points to coordinated logistics rather than senseless scavenger feeding.",sp=0},{t="Raiders of the Graves",b="When Deliah's ring is delivered to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher, the Forsaken commander quickly pieces the clues together. A body so newly buried could only originate from the vast mass graves across the border in Tirisfal Glades. The Rot Hide gnolls infesting Silverpine are not merely prowling the woods; they are methodically exhuming human corpses and shipping them across the water to Fenris Isle for sinister, unknown purposes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Corpse Laden Boat?",a="It is an old ferry moored along the shores of Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest. Rot Hide gnolls have been utilizing it as transport to haul exhumed human corpses across the water to their stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"corpse boat","decrepit ferry boat","lake boat"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Deliah?",a="Deliah was a human victim of the plague whose body was recently interred in the mass graves of Tirisfal Glades. Her corpse was stolen by Rot Hide gnolls, leaving only her engraved ring behind as a clue for investigators.",al={"deliah lore","who is deliah","for deliah ring"},it="history"},{q="Why are gnolls gathering dead bodies?",a="The Rot Hides are undead gnolls serving the Scourge. Rather than eating the bodies, they rob the mass graves of Tirisfal and ship the corpses to the Scourge stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"why do gnolls want corpses","rot hide corpses","fenris isle dead bodies"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander of the Forsaken stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He oversees defense against regional threats, including the feral Rot Hide gnolls, Dalaran wizards, and the Worgen.",al={"hadrec","sepulcher commander","executor hadrec"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where did the corpses on the boat come from?",a="According to High Executor Hadrec, the fresh state of the bodies indicates they were dug up from the mass graves in nearby Tirisfal Glades, where victims of the Scourge and plague were hastily buried.",al={"boat corpses origin","tirisfal graves boat"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after reporting this clue to Hadrec?",a="Hadrec dispatches agents to counter the Rot Hide threat directly on Fenris Isle and retrieve samples of the putrid ichor they are refining, while also prompting an investigation into who Deliah was and returning her ring.",al={"after rot hide clues","deliah ring follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The desecration of Tirisfal's mass graves hits close to home for the Forsaken, whose own fallen kin and unrisen brethren are being ferried off as raw material for gnoll alchemical horrors.",["faction:Horde"]="Hadrec coordinates Horde operations out of the Sepulcher to secure Silverpine against growing monster encampments like the Rot Hide pack occupying Fenris Isle."},kw={"corpse laden boat","deliah","deliah's ring","fenris isle","hadrec","rot hide clues","rot hide gnolls","sepulcher"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","quest:440","quest:443","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:gnoll","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Corpse Laden Boat",["end"]="High Executor Hadrec",level="16",faction="Horde",id=439},src={"Rot Hide Clues"}}
E["quest:440"] = {t="quest",n="The Engraved Ring",z="silverpine",s="High Executor Hadrec sends an adventurer to Brill carrying a recovered wedding band inscribed to a woman named Deliah. Magistrate Sevren consults town records to investigate her identity and determine where the ring originated.",h="High Executor Hadrec sends an adventurer to Brill carrying a recovered wedding band inscribed to a woman...",sec={{t="A Keepsake in Silverpine",b="While investigating the Rot Hide gnolls infesting the northern edges of Silverpine Forest, scouts uncovered an engraved ring bearing the name Deliah. Rather than discard the trinket, High Executor Hadrec directs you to take it back across the border to Brill. As Magistrate Sevren maintains the civic records and burial registers of the Tirisfal region, he is the most likely official to identify who she was—even if Hadrec remains deeply cynical about whether anyone among the Forsaken still cares.",sp=0},{t="Stolen from the Soil",b="Upon receiving the ring in Brill, Magistrate Sevren confirms that Deliah was indeed a resident who died and was interred within the town's mass grave. Finding her jewelry among the Rot Hides in Silverpine reveals a sinister desecration: the plague-warped gnolls have been raiding mass graves and spiriting corpses southward for Scourge experiments, leaving Sevren eager to see the gnolls wiped out.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Deliah?",a="Deliah was a former resident of Brill who died in recent years and was interred in the town's mass grave before her remains were disturbed by scavengers.",al={"who is deliah","deliah lore","deliah ring"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Why was Deliah's ring found in Silverpine Forest?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls raided the mass graves in Brill, exhuming fresh corpses—including Deliah's—and transporting them south into Silverpine to serve the Scourge.",al={"why do gnolls have the ring","rot hide ring","how did ring get to silverpine"},sp=1,it="why_here"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec doubt the ring matters?",a="Hadrec notes that undeath often strips away mortal attachments. He assumes Deliah's lover is either dead or, if risen as Forsaken, entirely indifferent to mortal vows and memories.",al={"hadrec dialogue","why hadrec cynical","forsaken feelings"},it="motive"},{q="What role does Magistrate Sevren play in this quest?",a="As the magistrate of Brill, Sevren maintains the local municipal records and registers of the dead, allowing him to confirm Deliah's identity and burial site.",al={"sevren brill","magistrate sevren role","who is sevren"},it="purpose"},{q="Are the Rot Hide gnolls allied with the Scourge?",a="Yes. The Rot Hide gnolls of Silverpine Forest were infected by the Scourge plague, operating under dark influences and collecting corpses for necromantic purposes.",al={"are rot hides scourge","gnoll scourge","silverpine gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Magistrate Sevren directs you toward Raleigh, Deliah's husband, who now dwells in the Undercity, leading to the follow-up quest 'Raleigh and the Undercity'.",al={"what next after engraved ring","next quest","deliah continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Deliah's ring is a quiet reminder of the fragile threads connecting their living pasts to their grim, cold present in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Stopping the Rot Hide gnolls from desecrating Horde-controlled graves in Tirisfal is a matter of territorial security as much as retribution."},kw={"brill","deliah","deliah's ring","gnolls","high executor hadrec","magistrate sevren","mass grave","rot hide","silverpine","the engraved ring"},rel={"npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:high-executor-hadrec","quest:439","quest:441","quest:530","subzone:brill","zone:silverpine","topic:gnoll"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="16",faction="Horde",id=440},src={"The Engraved Ring"}}
E["quest:442"] = {t="quest",n="Assault on Fenris Isle",z="silverpine",s="Assault on Fenris Isle is the climactic military directive issued by High Executor Hadrec to eradicate the Scourge stronghold in Silverpine Forest. To break the Lich King's grip upon Lake Lordamere, Forsaken agents are sent to storm Fenris Keep and take the head of the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw.",h="Assault on Fenris Isle is the climactic military directive issued by High Executor Hadrec to eradicate the...",sec={{t="Purging Lake Lordamere",b="For weeks, Fenris Isle has stood as a poisonous blister in the heart of Lake Lordamere. While the Forsaken secured the western roads and established their presence at the Sepulcher, the Scourge entrenched themselves inside Fenris Keep. Commanded by the powerful necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, this island outpost threatened not only Silverpine Forest but the southern waterways leading toward the Undercity itself. High Executor Hadrec recognizes that the Forsaken will never truly hold Silverpine while a servant of the Lich King conducts vile experiments right off their eastern shores.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Thule Ravenclaw",b="Storming Fenris Keep requires carving a path through hordes of rot hide gnolls and shambling undead before confronting Thule Ravenclaw in his stronghold. Thule wields foul necromantic curses, empowering his own strikes by leeching his attackers' vitality through dark magic. Upon his defeat, Thule's severed head is severed as undeniable proof of his demise. The necromantic disruption unleashed by his fall is so violent that Apothecary Renferrel detects the magical shockwaves all the way at the Sepulcher.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want Thule Ravenclaw dead?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is the master necromancer leading the Scourge on Fenris Isle. Leaving such an entrenched Scourge force unchecked threatens the Forsaken stronghold at the Sepulcher and endangers the waterways across Lake Lordamere. Hadrec demands his head to verify that the Scourge's regional command is definitively shattered.",al={"why kill thule","hadrec motives","fenris isle threat"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Thule Ravenclaw located?",a="Thule Ravenclaw resides deep inside the ruined castle on Fenris Isle, located in the middle of Lake Lordamere east of Silverpine Forest. He holds court in the lower communal hall of the keep, guarded by his undead retainers and twisted minions.",al={"thule ravenclaw location","where is thule","find thule"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when Thule Ravenclaw dies?",a="When Thule is destroyed, the sheer volume of dark necromantic energy released echoes across the region. Back at the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel detects the shockwave of unraveling magic, and High Executor Hadrec commends the strike as a massive strategic triumph for the Forsaken.",al={"thule death reaction","what happens after thule dies"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who controls Fenris Isle before this assault?",a="Fenris Isle is under the direct occupation of the Scourge. Thule Ravenclaw uses the island castle as a staging ground, commanding both reanimated undead and blight-twisted rot hide gnolls to terrorize the waters of Lake Lordamere.",al={"who holds fenris isle","fenris isle faction","is fenris isle scourge"},it="residents"},{q="Why was Bethor's Potion important for this mission?",a="Thule casts Hex of the Ravenclaw, a debilitating curse that diminishes his opponents' strength while magnifying his own power. Bethor Iceshard prepared an alchemical potion during the preceding operations specifically to neutralize this necrotic curse.",al={"hex of the ravenclaw cure","bethor potion thule","counter thule hex"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What is the strategic significance of Fenris Isle to the Forsaken?",a="Fenris Isle sits in Lake Lordamere, bordering both Silverpine and the Hillsbrad foothills. Securing or neutralizing it removes an active enemy outpost capable of launching attacks into Silverpine, clearing a major Scourge presence from the borders of Lordaeron.",al={"why fenris isle matters","fenris isle importance"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Thule's Head for?",a="High Executor Hadrec demands Thule's Head as undeniable proof that the necromancer has finally been destroyed. Fenris Isle is a fortified Scourge stronghold, and Hadrec will not commit to claiming victory in Silverpine until he sees physical evidence that their leader's grip on the region is broken.",al={"thules head use","why take thules head","proof of thules death"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful Scourge necromancer commanding the undead forces entrenched on Fenris Isle. From the keep in the middle of Lake Lordamere, he directs the Scourge's operations throughout Silverpine Forest, posing an immediate threat to the Forsaken presence at the Sepulcher.",al={"who is thule","thule ravenclaw lore","why is thule on fenris isle"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, eliminating Thule Ravenclaw is personal retribution. Crushing Scourge outposts proves their rebellion against the Lich King's will is absolute.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms relies heavily on the Forsaken stabilizing Silverpine and Tirisfal against rival powers and the wandering Scourge.",["class:Mage"]="Bethor Iceshard and Apothecary Renferrel closely monitor the magical fallout of Thule's demise, fascinated by the violent dispersal of his necrotic weaves."},kw={"fenris isle","hadrec","lake lordamere","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:446","subzone:fenris-isle","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","quest:448","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",level="20",faction="Horde",id=442,ri={"Thule's Head"}},src={"Assault on Fenris Isle"}}
E["quest:443"] = {t="quest",n="Rot Hide Ichor",z="silverpine",s="Rot Hide Ichor is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest assigned by High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher. Seeking to understand the unnatural Rot Hide gnolls infesting Fenris Isle before launching an assault, Forsaken leadership tasks adventurers with extracting the foul, mysterious fluid circulating through the creatures' veins for study.",h="Rot Hide Ichor is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest assigned by High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="Unnatural Biology",b="The Rot Hide gnolls of Silverpine Forest are far from typical wild humanoids. Decaying, aggressive, and reeking of blight, they occupy strategic positions like Fenris Isle across Lordamere Lake. High Executor Hadrec recognizes that their unnatural resilience stems from whatever strange fluid flows within them, requiring hard specimens before committing soldiers to a costly assault.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Analysis",b="The Royal Apothecary Society maintains an active presence in the Sepulcher, and Apothecary Renferrel specializes in biological and chemical anomalies. By bringing samples of this putrid rot hide ichor to Renferrel, the Forsaken hope to uncover the gnolls' origins, identify who is engineering them, and pinpoint vulnerabilities to exploit in battle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rot Hide ichor?",a="It is an unnatural, putrid fluid that courses through the bodies of the Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle. Rather than normal blood, this foul concoction sustains their undead-like, rotting state and gives them abnormal resilience.",al={"what is the ichor","rot hide fluid","gnoll ichor"},it="item"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want samples of the ichor?",a="Hadrec plans an assault on Fenris Isle, but military wisdom dictates understanding the enemy first. By obtaining fluid samples for Apothecary Renferrel to examine, the Forsaken hope to deduce who created the Rot Hides and find a biological weakness to exploit.",al={"why collect ichor","hadrec's goal","why hadrec wants ichor"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Rot Hide gnolls located?",a="They inhabit Fenris Isle, located east across Lordamere Lake from the Decrepit Ferry in Silverpine Forest. The island's shoreline, camps, and surrounding ruined grounds are overrun by various Rot Hide breeds, including brutes and plague weavers.",al={"where do i find rot hides","rot hide gnoll location","fenris gnolls"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Renferrel is a researcher for the Royal Apothecary Society stationed outside the crypt at the Sepulcher. He studies local blights, plagues, and strange biological hazards throughout Silverpine Forest on behalf of the Forsaken.",al={"who is renferrel","apothecary renferrel role"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after Renferrel receives the ichor?",a="Once Renferrel receives the samples, he sets about analyzing the fluid's chemical makeup to trace the origin of the Rot Hides, leading into the quest Rot Hide Origins.",al={"next quest after rot hide ichor","rot hide ichor follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about gnolls?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls hold Fenris Isle, a vital stronghold in Lordamere Lake bordering Forsaken territory. Furthermore, their rotting condition and use of plague-like abilities suggest outside tampering, posing a potential direct threat to Undercity's security.",al={"why forsaken fight gnolls","gnoll threat silverpine"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle?",a="The Rot Hides are an aggressive tribe of gnolls inhabiting Fenris Isle on Lordamere Lake. Unlike ordinary gnolls, they are visibly corrupted and rotting, bearing unnatural plagues and filth. The Forsaken consider them a dangerous blight right on the border of Silverpine Forest, prompting High Executor Hadrec to prepare an offensive against their stronghold.",al={"who are the rot hides","fenris isle gnolls","what are rot hide gnolls"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, understanding biological horrors and engineered diseases is both a science and a survival instinct. Dissecting the Rot Hides' fluid allows the Royal Apothecary Society to determine whether this infection threatens their own claims in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Fenris Isle sits on the eastern edge of Silverpine Forest, serving as a tactical danger zone if left unmonitored by the Horde forces securing the surrounding lands."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","fenris isle","high executor hadrec","lordamere lake","rot hide gnolls","rot hide ichor","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:439","quest:444","quest:442","npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="17",faction="Horde",id=443,ri={"Rot Hide Ichor"}},src={"Rot Hide Ichor (quest)"}}
E["quest:445"] = {t="quest",n="Delivery to Silverpine Forest",z="silverpine",s="This errand serves as a vital courier mission linking the Royal Apothecary Society's research in Brill with their ongoing efforts in Silverpine Forest. Tasked by Apothecary Johaan, you carry valuable findings to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher to aid the development of the Dark Lady's New Plague.",h="This errand serves as a vital courier mission linking the Royal Apothecary Society's research in Brill with...",sec={{t="A Society Bound by Purpose",b="The Royal Apothecary Society operates under the direct command of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, tasked with concocting a New Plague capable of wiping out both the living and the Scourge. Isolated laboratories across Forsaken territory cannot work in a vacuum; survival and progress demand constant communication. In Brill, Apothecary Johaan has gathered experimental results that must be circulated to other researchers in the field without delay.",sp=0},{t="Outpost in the South",b="Silverpine Forest represents the next frontier of Forsaken expansion and research. Based out of the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel oversees biochemical testing amidst regional threats like the Moonrage worgen, rogue humans, and lingering Scourge. By receiving Johaan's notes from Tirisfal Glades, Renferrel integrates new alchemical findings into his own local experiments, further advancing the Society's grand design.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Apothecary Johaan sending these documents?",a="Members of the Royal Apothecary Society are expected to share their discoveries to accelerate the creation of the New Plague. Johaan needs his latest findings from Tirisfal Glades brought south so other researchers can build upon his work.",al={"why courier findings","johaan notes","why send research"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Sepulcher located?",a="The Sepulcher is the primary Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest. It lies south of the border with Tirisfal Glades and southwest of the Undercity, along the main road that winds through the woods.",al={"where is sepulcher","finding renferrel","sepulcher location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Renferrel is a prominent member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Sepulcher. He directs field testing and studies exotic ingredients found throughout Silverpine Forest, reporting back to the Society's high leadership in the Undercity.",al={"renferrel role","who is renferrel","renferrel silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="What is the New Plague mentioned by Johaan?",a="The New Plague is a bespoke alchemical contagion being engineered by the Royal Apothecary Society under orders from Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. It is designed to eradicate both living enemies and the undead minions of the Lich King.",al={"new plague","sylvanas plague","what plague"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Necropolis Renferrel mentions?",a="Upon receiving the findings, Renferrel mentions needing to send samples to 'the Necropolis', referencing the central scientific installations and leadership of the Royal Apothecary Society deep within the Undercity.",al={"necropolis renferrel","renferrel samples","samples to necropolis"},it="place"},{q="Why use an adventurer instead of official messengers?",a="Forsaken couriers face dangerous roads teeming with feral worgen, aggressive wildlife, and hostile human survivors. Entrusting research to an able-bodied adventurer ensures the delicate alchemical notes reach the Sepulcher intact while enlisting another hand for regional work.",al={"why me courier","why adventurer messenger"},it="why_me"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Delivering this research represents direct service to Lady Sylvanas and the survival of the Forsaken, helping fulfill the Royal Apothecary Society's central ambition.",["faction:Horde"]="While Forsaken alchemical research often raises eyebrows among other Horde allies, safe passage and courier work along the Silverpine road keep the northern territories secured."},kw={"brill","delivery to silverpine forest","johaan","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:brill","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="10",faction="Horde",id=445},src={"Delivery to Silverpine Forest"}}
E["quest:446"] = {t="quest",n="Thule Ravenclaw",z="silverpine",s="Following the discovery of strange Rot Hide ichor in Silverpine Forest, Bethor Iceshard identifies the foul substance as the handiwork of his traitorous former colleague, Thule Ravenclaw. To aid the Forsaken in repelling the Rot Hide gnolls, Bethor prepares a specialized scroll containing counter-incantations for Apothecary Renferrel.",h="Following the discovery of strange Rot Hide ichor in Silverpine Forest, Bethor Iceshard identifies the foul...",sec={{t="A Colleague Turned Traitor",b="When a courier delivers the sampled Rot Hide ichor to Bethor Iceshard atop the Mage Quarter in the Undercity, the veteran sorcerer immediately recognizes its signature arcane resonance. The distillation belongs to Thule Ravenclaw, once a bright and promising young mage alongside Bethor before the Third War. Driven by ambitions of dark power, Thule deserted his peers to swear allegiance to the Scourge and the Lich King, abandoning his humanity long before Lordaeron fell.",sp=0},{t="The Master of Fenris Isle",b="Bethor is troubled to learn that Ravenclaw not only survived the war, but has entrenched himself inside Fenris Keep upon Fenris Isle in Lake Lordamere. From there, Thule commands the Rot Hide gnolls, infusing them with foul magic and sending them forth to harass Forsaken borders. Drawing upon his intimate knowledge of his former peer's magical repertoire, Bethor scribes a specialized scroll designed to neutralize Thule's signature curses and wards.",sp=1},{t="Alchemical Countermeasures",b="Entrusted with Bethor's scroll, the courier returns to the Sepulcher to present it to Apothecary Renferrel of the Royal Apothecary Society. Fascinated by the potent magical incantations laid out by the Undercity mage, Renferrel begins combining high sorcery with the society's alchemical brews. The resulting concoction is crafted specifically to shatter Ravenclaw's hexes, clearing the path for an assault on Fenris Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw was once a promising young Dalaran-trained human mage who studied alongside Bethor Iceshard. When the Lich King began spreading corruption throughout Lordaeron, Thule betrayed his brethren to serve the Scourge, eventually rising to command the Rot Hide gnolls from Fenris Isle.",al={"thule lore","who is thule","thule ravenclaw backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard know Thule's magic?",a="Bethor and Thule were colleagues and fellow spellcasters before the fall of Lordaeron. Because they studied the arcane arts together, Bethor is intimately familiar with Thule's favored spellcraft, magical theory, and hexes.",al={"bethor and thule","how does bethor know thule","bethor iceshard connection"},it="ties"},{q="What is Bethor's Scroll used for?",a="Bethor's Scroll contains intricate counter-incantations specifically crafted to unravel Thule's spells. Apothecary Renferrel uses these incantations to brew an alchemical potion that shields Forsaken champions against Ravenclaw's hexes.",al={"bethors scroll","scroll purpose","what does the scroll do"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Rot Hide gnolls a threat in Silverpine?",a="Unlike ordinary wild beasts, the Rot Hide gnolls are coordinated and empowered by Thule Ravenclaw using Scourge necromancy. From their stronghold on Fenris Isle, they stage organized incursions against Forsaken settlements and patrols across Silverpine Forest.",al={"rot hide gnolls","why fight gnolls","fenris isle gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest begins with Bethor Iceshard in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity and concludes with Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"thule ravenclaw turn in","where to turn in thule ravenclaw","scroll delivery location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Renferrel receives the scroll?",a="With the counter-potion developed, Renferrel sends you to report to High Executor Hadrec ahead of an all-out assault on Fenris Isle to eliminate Thule Ravenclaw and reclaim the island.",al={"what happens next","after thule ravenclaw quest","fenris isle attack"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the scroll delivered to Renferrel?",a="Upon inspecting the ichor, Bethor was shocked to discover that his former colleague, Thule Ravenclaw, not only survived the war but betrayed his kin to serve the Scourge and lead the Rot Hide gnolls against the Forsaken. Bethor knows Thule's magical repertoire intimately. By sending this enchanted scroll to Apothecary Renferrel, he provides the arcane incantations required to brew a potion capable of neutralizing Thule's foul hexes.",al={"why deliver bethor's scroll","bethor iceshard motive","why send scroll to renferrel"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The conflict between Bethor and Thule highlights the tragic divide among Lordaeron's former magi, contrasting those who fell to necromancy with those who retained their arcane discipline into undeath.",["race:Undead"]="Neutralizing Thule Ravenclaw is vital for the Forsaken, as his control of Fenris Isle threatens both the Sepulcher and the western approaches to the Capital City.",["faction:Horde"]="Rooting out Scourge remnants in Lordaeron secures the Horde's solitary foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","fenris isle","rot hide","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:444","quest:448","quest:442","npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Bethor Iceshard",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="16",faction="Horde",id=446},src={"Thule Ravenclaw (quest)"}}
E["quest:448"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Hadrec",z="silverpine",s="Report to Hadrec is a Horde military dispatch directing champions within the Sepulcher to consult Silverpine's field commander. Following Apothecary Renferrel and Bethor Iceshard's investigation into the Scourge presence in Lake Lordamere, High Executor Hadrec coordinates the martial preparations required to storm Fenris Isle. It marks the transition from magical reconnaissance to direct tactical warfare.",h="Report to Hadrec is a Horde military dispatch directing champions within the Sepulcher to consult...",sec={{t="Escalation in Silverpine",b="While Apothecary Renferrel and the mage Bethor Iceshard spent considerable effort divining the threat posed by the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, scholarly study alone cannot dislodge a rising Scourge stronghold. With Ravenclaw actively binding the restless dead across Fenris Isle, Renferrel recognized that the problem had grown far beyond alchemical or arcane solutions. Halting this burgeoning infection required the hard steel and disciplined forces of the Forsaken military, shifting the matter from the apothecaries' tables straight to the commander's desk.",sp=0},{t="The High Executor's Arsenal",b="Stationed in the crypts of the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec directs all strategic operations across Silverpine Forest on behalf of the Dark Lady. When Bethor's grim warnings regarding Ravenclaw reached him, Hadrec acted without hesitation, knowing that an entrenched necromancer on Lordamere's western shore poses a lethal risk to Undercity's flanks. To ensure the strike on the island fortress succeeds, Hadrec opens the local garrison's armory, outfitting vanguard combatants before sending them directly into the fray.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec is the commanding officer of the Forsaken military forces stationed at the Sepulcher. He oversees frontline defense and offensive operations throughout Silverpine Forest, answering directly to Undercity leadership.",al={"hadrec","who is hadrec","sepulcher commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel send you to Hadrec?",a="Apothecary Renferrel and Bethor Iceshard discovered that Thule Ravenclaw has amassed a dangerous Scourge force on Fenris Isle. Because eliminating an entrenched necromancer requires military power and proper equipment rather than mere alchemy, Renferrel directs you to the garrison's commander.",al={"why report to hadrec","renferrel hadrec connection"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Sepulcher located?",a="The Sepulcher is a fortified Forsaken settlement and tomb complex situated in central Silverpine Forest, serving as the main Horde hub and staging ground for operations in the region.",al={"where is sepulcher","sepulcher location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful Scourge necromancer who seized Fenris Keep on Fenris Isle in Lake Lordamere, raising the dead to establish an active beachhead right off Silverpine's eastern shore.",al={"thule ravenclaw","thule lore"},it="target"},{q="What happens after reporting to Hadrec?",a="Hadrec grants you supplies from the Sepulcher's armory and orders an immediate military strike against Fenris Isle to eliminate Thule Ravenclaw and break the Scourge hold on Lake Lordamere.",al={"what next after hadrec","next quest hadrec"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Bethor mentioned by Hadrec?",a="Bethor Iceshard is a Forsaken mage dwelling in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, whose magical divinations helped uncover the exact nature and danger of Thule Ravenclaw's rituals.",al={"who is bethor","bethor iceshard"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Sepulcher coordinates the Horde's western defense in Lordaeron, securing the approaches to the Capital City ruins against both Scourge outposts and human survivors.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Thule Ravenclaw represents the enslaving will of the Lich King encroaching on their doorstep, making his destruction a vital matter of national survival."},kw={"fenris","hadrec","iceshard","ravenclaw","renferrel","sepulcher","silverpine","thule"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","quest:442","quest:446","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:fenris-isle","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="High Executor Hadrec",level="16",faction="Horde",id=448},src={"Report to Hadrec"}}
E["quest:449"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers' Report",z="silverpine",s="The Deathstalkers' Report is a crucial military courier assignment delivered to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher. After securing injured Deathstalkers in the northern wilds, you carry their gathered intelligence concerning unexpected Scourge activity back to Forsaken high command. This dispatch alters the Forsaken's assessment of their hold on Silverpine Forest.",h="The Deathstalkers' Report is a crucial military courier assignment delivered to High Executor Hadrec at the...",sec={{t="Frontline Intelligence",b="The Deathstalkers act as the eyes, ears, and daggers of the Dark Lady, pushing into the untamed wilderness ahead of standard military units. Near the border of Tirisfal and Silverpine, an advance patrol ran into catastrophic resistance while charting enemy movements. Though Deathstalker Quinn barely survived his injuries and Erland fought his way to safety, their scouting mission yielded intelligence essential to the Forsaken occupation of Silverpine Forest.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge Factor",b="When High Executor Hadrec reviews the sealed field report, it confirms dark news: the mindless forces of the Scourge have maintained a far heavier and more aggressive presence in Silverpine than Undercity strategists anticipated. Instead of merely securing abandoned human hamlets and pacifying rogue beasts, the Sepulcher command must brace for coordinated Scourge opposition while fighting to claim the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Deathstalker Report?",a="It is a field dispatch written by Deathstalker Rane Yorick on behalf of her wounded scouting cell. It compiles their observations regarding hostile threats, specifically unexpected Scourge activity in northern Silverpine Forest, and delivers that data straight to the regional commander at the Sepulcher.",al={"deathstalker report","what is the report","what did yorick give me"},it="item"},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander in charge of Forsaken operations in Silverpine Forest. Stationed at the Sepulcher, he coordinates scouts, defensive lines, and the broader campaign to push both the Scourge and hostile humans out of the region.",al={"hadrec","high executor hadrec","sepulcher commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the report's information a surprise to Hadrec?",a="The Forsaken leadership assumed the Scourge in Silverpine was scattered and minimal compared to the heavy fighting in Tirisfal Glades and the Plaguelands. The Deathstalkers' casualties and discoveries proved the Lich King's minions remain entrenched and dangerous even this far south.",al={"why surprised","hadrec reaction","scourge in silverpine"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the elite covert order of the Forsaken, serving as assassins, spies, and forward scouts directly under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's command. They operate throughout contested territories to root out threats before the regular army marches in.",al={"deathstalkers","deathstalker lore","forsaken rogues"},it="people"},{q="Where is the Sepulcher located?",a="The Sepulcher is a crypt and central base camp nestled in central Silverpine Forest, situated just west of the main north-south road. It serves as the primary garrison and resting point for Forsaken forces operating throughout the province.",al={"where is sepulcher","sepulcher location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Hadrec reads the report?",a="Recognizing the gravity of the situation and the mounting threats in Silverpine, Hadrec directs you onward to consult with other specialists stationed at the Sepulcher, starting with Apothecary Renferrel to aid in developing counters to regional threats.",al={"next quest","what now","after hadrec"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick need the report delivered so quickly?",a="Rane Yorick and his companions uncovered vital intelligence regarding Scourge activity and hostile threats in the wilds of Silverpine Forest. Because this information directly impacts the Forsaken's ability to secure and hold the region, High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher must receive it immediately so military command can respond.",al={"why does rane yorick want this done","rane yorick motivation","why send the deathstalker report"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Rane Yorick ask you to deliver the report instead of doing it himself?",a="Rane's scouting party is in no condition to travel. His fellow Deathstalker, Quinn, was severely wounded during their mission and is still slowly mending under Rane's care. With their unit immobilized and the report too urgent to delay, Rane must rely on an able-bodied traveler like you to carry the dispatch to the Sepulcher.",al={"why me rane yorick","why can't rane deliver it","why do i carry the report"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Delivering this intelligence directly supports the expansion of the Undercity and proves your reliability to High Executor Hadrec and the Deathstalker network.",["class:Rogue"]="The Deathstalkers represent the pinnacle of Forsaken espionage; carrying out their vital dispatches demonstrates your alignment with the Dark Lady's premier shadow operatives.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken's struggle to secure Silverpine against the Scourge is vital to establishing a secure Horde foothold across northern Lordaeron."},kw={"deathstalker","erland","hadrec","quinn","rane yorick","report","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"quest:435","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","quest:3221","quest:1886","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Rane Yorick",["end"]="High Executor Hadrec",level="11",faction="Horde",id=449},src={"The Deathstalkers' Report"}}
E["quest:452"] = {t="quest",n="Pyrewood Ambush",z="silverpine",s="Pyrewood Ambush is a critical strike coordinated by the Deathstalkers inside the cursed town of Pyrewood Village. By assassinating the local human council, the Forsaken hope to break Archmage Arugal's grip on the cursed inhabitants and weaken his fortress looming above.",h="Pyrewood Ambush is a critical strike coordinated by the Deathstalkers inside the cursed town of Pyrewood...",sec={{t="Striking the Puppets",b="Perched inside the town hall of Pyrewood Village, Deathstalker Faerleia lies in wait for the village leadership. While Archmage Arugal isolates himself within Shadowfang Keep tending to his dark sorceries, he relies on the local Pyrewood Council as figureheads to maintain order among the afflicted populace. Faerleia intends to wipe out this leadership cadre in a swift ambush, hoping that without the council's mediation, the feral worgen roaming the surrounding woods and village streets will break free from Arugal's dominion.",sp=0},{t="A Decapitation Strike",b="The ambush targets every sitting member of the municipal government, culminating in the death of Lord Mayor Morrison. By clearing out the councilors as they file into their meeting chamber, the Forsaken strike a severe blow to the village's administrative chain of command. The Undercity views this slaughter not merely as revenge, but as a strategic prerequisite for conquering Pyrewood Village outright and laying siege to the mad archmage in Shadowfang Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Faerleia?",a="Deathstalker Faerleia is an operative of the Forsaken's premier espionage and assassination guild, the Deathstalkers. Operating behind enemy lines, she established a foothold directly inside Pyrewood Village to coordinate strikes against Archmage Arugal's local infrastructure.",al={"faerleia","deathstalker faerleia","who gives pyrewood ambush"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Forsaken want the Pyrewood Council dead?",a="Arugal uses the council as political puppets to keep the cursed human villagers compliant and under control. The Forsaken believe that eliminating these leaders will throw Pyrewood into chaos and cause the worgen to turn against Arugal.",al={"why kill pyrewood council","pyrewood council purpose","pyrewood council lore"},it="motive"},{q="Who leads the Pyrewood Council?",a="The council is led by Lord Mayor Morrison, who oversees municipal matters alongside councilmen like Smithers, Thatcher, and Brunswick before the Deathstalkers ambush them.",al={"lord mayor morrison","pyrewood mayor","who runs pyrewood"},it="leader"},{q="Where does this ambush take place?",a="The ambush takes place inside the municipal town hall building within Pyrewood Village, located in southern Silverpine Forest just down the road from Shadowfang Keep.",al={"pyrewood ambush location","where is faerleia","town hall pyrewood"},it="place"},{q="What is the relationship between the Council and Arugal?",a="The council serves as Arugal's administrative mouthpiece. While Arugal remains locked away inside Shadowfang Keep conducting his dark experiments, the council manages the villagers who transform into ferocious beasts under the cover of night.",al={"arugal council","is council working for arugal","arugal control pyrewood"},it="ties"},{q="Does killing the council free Pyrewood from the curse?",a="No. Eliminating the council removes Arugal's mortal puppets, but it does not lift the lupine curse afflicting the villagers, leaving the Forsaken to contest a town filled with hostile, uncontrolled monsters.",al={"is pyrewood cured","does ambush cure worgen","curse broken pyrewood"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Who are you fighting in the Pyrewood ambush?",a="You are fighting the Pyrewood Council, led by Lord Mayor Morrison alongside councilmen like Smithers, Thatcher, and Brunswick. They govern Pyrewood Village under the influence of Archmage Arugal, acting as his puppet administrators to keep the cursed, mind-addled townsfolk obedient while Arugal conducts his dark affairs inside Shadowfang Keep.",al={"pyrewood council members","who is the target pyrewood ambush","who do you fight pyrewood ambush"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Deathstalker Faerleia need your help?",a="Deathstalker Faerleia is working deep behind enemy lines in hostile territory. The Council returns in waves, bringing multiple seasoned members including Lord Mayor Morrison. As skilled as Faerleia is as an assassin for the Dark Lady, she cannot take on the entire council at once without being overwhelmed, making your arrival vital to the ambush's success.",al={"why does faerleia need help","why me pyrewood ambush","why can't faerleia do it alone"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing southern Silverpine is vital to defending the Undercity's borders, and exterminating Arugal's sycophants brings them one step closer to claiming Pyrewood.",["class:Rogue"]="The ambush is classic Deathstalker tradecraft: infiltrating enemy strongholds, lying in wait, and eliminating enemy commanders in their own seat of power.",["faction:Horde"]="Disrupting Arugal's puppet network weakens the greater threat menacing the Horde's transit corridor through Silverpine Forest toward the southern borders."},kw={"arugal","deathstalker faerleia","faerleia","lord mayor morrison","pyrewood ambush","pyrewood council","shadowfang keep","silverpine forest"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-faerleia","npc:arugal","zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Deathstalker Faerleia",level="15",faction="Horde",id=452},src={"Pyrewood Ambush"}}
E["quest:460"] = {t="quest",n="Resting in Pieces",z="silverpine",s="Resting in Pieces begins when an adventurer recovers the animated, severed head of Alaric, a former servant of the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw on Fenris Isle. Alaric pleads to be carried across Fenris Keep to an unmarked grave near the stables where the rest of his remains lie buried.",h="Resting in Pieces begins when an adventurer recovers the animated, severed head of Alaric, a former servant...",sec={{t="A Bodyguard Betrayed",b="Before his gruesome fate, Alaric served as the chief servant and personal bodyguard to Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful Scourge-aligned mage operating out of Fenris Keep in Silverpine Forest. When the Plague of Undeath swept the region, Thule claimed he would use his arcane sorcery to protect Alaric from falling victim to it. Instead, the twisted ward trapped Alaric in a permanent, agonizing state of undeath, leaving his consciousness fully intact within his severed parts.",sp=0},{t="Plaything of the Rot Hides",b="After engineering the creation of the rot hide gnolls by infecting the local packs with necromantic decay, Thule turned on his own bodyguard. The necromancer decapitated Alaric and tossed his still-living, speaking head to the savage gnolls as a gruesome diversion. While the rot hides dragged his body to a hasty, shallow grave outside the keep's stables, they kept his head as a macabre plaything until an outsider intervened.",sp=0},{t="Reuniting the Pieces",b="Reaching the hastily dug dirt near the stables reunites Alaric's severed head with his headless torso. Though still shackled to the curse of unlife that Thule wove around him, having his parts restored brings Alaric a bitter measure of relief.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Alaric?",a="Alaric was the head servant and personal bodyguard of Thule Ravenclaw at Fenris Keep. Thule cast an unnatural spell on him under the guise of protecting him from the Plague of Undeath, which instead bound him into eternal unlife.",al={"alaric","who is the talking head","talking head silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Alaric beheaded?",a="Thule Ravenclaw beheaded Alaric shortly after completing his experiments to create the rot hide gnolls. The necromancer then tossed Alaric's severed, conscious head to the gnolls as a plaything.",al={"why is alaric a head","who cut off alarics head"},it="history"},{q="Where is Alaric's grave located?",a="His body lies in an unmarked, hastily dug shallow grave on Fenris Isle within the courtyard of Fenris Keep, close to the stable buildings.",al={"where is alarics body","shallow grave location","where is the grave fenris"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the rot hide gnolls?",a="The rot hide gnolls are the local gnoll population of Fenris Isle, transformed into rotting, undead-tainted horrors through the necromantic experiments of Thule Ravenclaw.",al={"rot hides","rot hide gnolls","fenris isle gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a human wizard and Scourge necromancer who seized Fenris Keep in the middle of Lake Lordamere, using it as a laboratory to corrupt the gnolls and spread the Scourge's influence.",al={"thule","thule ravenclaw"},it="people"},{q="What happens after you find the grave?",a="Once reunited with his remains, Alaric assists you in locating a hidden niche containing a powerful wand, which can then be returned to Dalaran's Magus Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",al={"what next resting in pieces","resting in pieces followup"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Alaric want his head brought to his grave?",a="Alaric is trapped in an agonizing unlife created by Thule Ravenclaw's warped protective spell. After being decapitated and tossed to the rot hide gnolls as a gruesome plaything, he fears his headless corpse was desecrated or obliterated. He wants to be returned to his makeshift grave on Fenris Isle to reunite with his remains and end his humiliating ordeal.",al={"why does the talking head need help","alaric motive","why take alaric to his grave"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Alaric need your help to reach his grave?",a="Alaric is merely a severed, animated head. Unable to move on his own, he was left entirely helpless while being kicked around as a toy by the rot hide gnolls occupying Fenris Keep. You are the first non-gnoll he has encountered who can physically carry him past the creatures and bury him properly.",al={"why does alaric need you","why can't alaric do it himself","talking head why me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Forsaken champions will recognize Thule Ravenclaw's treacherous spellcasting as emblematic of the cruel horrors inflicted by Scourge-aligned sorcerers across Lordaeron.",["class:Mage"]="Thule's corrupted ward—twisting defensive abjuration into an inescapable curse of severed undeath—stands as a stark warning of what happens when arcane magic is twisted by necromancy."},kw={"alaric","fenris isle","fenris keep","rot hide","shallow grave","silverpine","talking head","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:461","quest:491","subzone:fenris-keep","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:gnoll","topic:plague-of-undeath","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="A Talking Head",["end"]="Shallow Grave",level="17",faction="Horde",id=460},src={"Resting in Pieces"}}
E["quest:461"] = {t="quest",n="The Hidden Niche",z="silverpine",s="After uncovering the talkative remains of Alaric from a shallow grave outside Fenris Keep, adventurers are directed back inside the stronghold. Guided by the deceased human's memories, travelers seek out a forgotten alcove concealed behind a dusty shelf to grant him final repose and claim an old relic.",h="After uncovering the talkative remains of Alaric from a shallow grave outside Fenris Keep, adventurers are...",sec={{t="A Restless Request",b="Even after death, Alaric retains vivid memories of Fenris Keep during its better days. Relieved to be exhumed from a shallow, unceremonious dirt grave by Horde scouts, his skeletal remains refuse to simply be carried off to the Sepulcher. Instead, he bargains with vital information: a hidden niche inside the keep's southwestern tower containing an item deeply treasured by Thule Ravenclaw and his fellow mages.",sp=0},{t="Buried in the Walls",b="Navigating past the Rot Hide gnolls infesting the island fortress, travelers carry Alaric's remains up through the stone corridors. Tucked away behind a dusty bookshelf in the upper levels lies the secret compartment he spoke of. Once opened, Alaric asks only to be sealed away within the keep's ancient masonry, finding solace in resting inside the walls where he spent the happiest days of his life—far from the gnawing jaws of the gnolls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Alaric?",a="Alaric was Thule Ravenclaw's former head servant and bodyguard at Fenris Keep, beheaded by Thule after the creation of the Rot Hide gnolls. Discovered buried outside the fortress in a shallow grave, his animated spirit helps guide Horde adventurers in exchange for a proper resting place inside his beloved stronghold.",al={"alaric lore","who is alaric","whose bones are these"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the hidden niche located?",a="The hidden niche is concealed inside the southwestern tower of Fenris Keep, hidden behind an unassuming, dusty bookshelf on the upper floor.",al={"where is dusty shelf","where is the niche","hidden niche location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What item is hidden in the alcove?",a="Inside the concealed alcove rests an old wand once treasured by Thule Ravenclaw and his former peers from Dalaran, along with other remnants Alaric leaves for those who aided him.",al={"what is in the niche","fenris keep treasure","thule item"},it="item"},{q="Why does Alaric want to stay inside Fenris Keep?",a="Alaric considers the time he spent living within Fenris Keep to be the best days of his life. Sealing his remains within the stonework brings him peace and keeps him safe from the scavenger gnolls roaming the courtyards.",al={"why leave alaric in fenris","alaric resting place"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after finding the shelf?",a="After sealing Alaric into the niche and retrieving the wand, adventurers are directed back to the Undercity to deliver the relic to Bethor Iceshard.",al={"quest after hidden niche","what do i do with the wand"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why did Alaric tell you to leave his boots behind?",a="When his bones were exhumed from the shallow grave, Alaric humorously insisted on leaving his old boots in the dirt, remarking that they never fit him properly anyway.",al={"alaric boots","leave boots behind"}},{q="Why does Alaric need you to carry his remains to the niche?",a="Alaric is nothing more than a dismembered corpse buried in a shallow grave on Fenris Isle. Having been slain and dismembered, he has no physical power to move himself back into the fortress he once called home. He relies entirely on you to exhume his scattered remains, carry him through the hostile Gnoll-infested keep, and deposit him in the secret alcove.",al={"why does alaric need help","why me alaric","why carry alaric remains"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, dealing with restless, speaking remains is familiar business, though Alaric's yearning for peaceful rest in human ruins is a stark reminder of the lands they inherited.",["class:Mage"]="The hidden alcove preserves the arcane heritage of Fenris Keep, concealing artifacts tied directly to former Dalaran wizards like Thule Ravenclaw.",["faction:Horde"]="Reclaiming relics from the heart of Fenris Keep undermines Thule's foothold on Fenris Isle and assists the Forsaken's campaign to secure Silverpine Forest."},kw={"alaric","dusty shelf","fenris keep","hidden niche","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:460","quest:491","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Shallow Grave",["end"]="Dusty Shelf",level="18",faction="Horde",id=461},src={"The Hidden Niche"}}
E["quest:477"] = {t="quest",n="Border Crossings",z="silverpine",s="Border Crossings is an espionage task assigned by Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher to investigate Dalaran's covert operations in Silverpine Forest. By intercepting supply crates bound for the Dalaran encampment near Pyrewood Village, the Forsaken hope to uncover why the Kirin Tor are actively supporting the human bastion of Ambermill.",h="Border Crossings is an espionage task assigned by Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher to investigate...",sec={{t="Supplies on the Frontier",b="While Ambermill stands as the main stronghold of surviving human resistance in eastern Silverpine Forest, the magi of Dalaran have not left them to stand alone. Wagon shipments filled with supplies and arcana have been smuggled out of the Hillsbrad Foothills, crossing through Silverpine to supply forward outposts and staging grounds. One such logistical camp sits just north of Pyrewood Village, manned by Dalaran personnel watching the road.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken's Suspicion",b="Shadow Priest Allister and the Forsaken leadership at the Sepulcher find Dalaran's intense investment in Ambermill troubling. To them, a provincial town would hardly justify the Kirin Tor risking resources and lives deep within Forsaken-claimed territory unless some greater strategic or magical objective was at stake. Investigating the crates gives the Forsaken direct intelligence on what Dalaran is shipping west.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Cargo",b="Cracking open one of the wizards' crates reveals more than mere provisions. Amid carefully packed arcane paraphernalia lies a bundle of aged, yellowing maps illustrating Silverpine Forest and wider western Lordaeron, alongside an enigmatic magical pendant. Rather than common logistics, Dalaran appears to be conducting targeted cartographic and arcane reconnaissance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are Dalaran wizards active in Silverpine Forest?",a="Dalaran operates out of Ambermill to maintain a human and Alliance presence in western Lordaeron. Shadow Priest Allister suspects the Kirin Tor have a deeper, hidden motive beyond simply defending a rural hamlet, prompting the Forsaken to raid their supply lines.",al={"why is dalaran here","dalaran silverpine","why dalaran at ambermill"},it="why_here"},{q="Where are the Dalaran crates located?",a="The crates are stationed in an encampment maintained by Dalaran magi and guards situated directly north of Pyrewood Village, off the main road.",al={"crate location","where are the crates","pyrewood camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is inside the Dalaran crate?",a="Inside the crate is a collection of carefully packed items, topped by a bundle of aging survey maps of Silverpine Forest and western Lordaeron, as well as an intricate magical pendant.",al={"crate contents","what is in the box"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Who is Shadow Priest Allister?",a="Shadow Priest Allister is a prominent Forsaken leader stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, directing intelligence efforts and offensive strikes against human holdouts and Dalaran's incursions.",al={"shadow priest allister","who gives border crossings"},it="identity"},{q="How are the supplies getting into Silverpine Forest?",a="The shipments are ferried by wagon from Dalaran's territory in the Hillsbrad Foothills, crossing through the border pass into Silverpine before reaching staging camps near Ambermill and Pyrewood.",al={"dalaran supply route","hillsbrad wagons"},it="history"},{q="What follows the completion of this quest?",a="Discovering the cargo leads immediately into Maps and Runes, where you must deliver the unearthed maps and the pendant back to Shadow Priest Allister for study.",al={"what next","follow up quest","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister want this done?",a="Ambermill stands as a stubborn pocket of living human resistance in Silverpine Forest, fortified and sustained almost entirely by Dalaran's arcane backing. Shadow Priest Allister suspects the mages have a deeper, hidden agenda for investing heavily in such a backwater town. By intercepting the wagon shipments pouring into their outpost north of Pyrewood, the Forsaken hope to uncover Dalaran's true motives and eliminate a growing Alliance foothold right on the Undercity's doorstep.",al={"why does allister want the crate","shadow priest allister motive","why steal dalaran supplies"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken cannot tolerate an unchecked Dalaran outpost on their southern flank, especially one funneling supplies right under the Sepulcher's nose.",["class:Priest"]="Serving under Shadow Priest Allister gives Forsaken priests a direct hand in securing the domain of the Cult of Forgotten Shadow against holy and arcane rivals alike.",["class:Mage"]="Horde spellcasters have an avid interest in intercepting Dalaran's magical shipments to discern what secrets and protective wards the Kirin Tor are employing in Lordaeron."},kw={"ambermill","border crossings","dalaran crate","hillsbrad","pyrewood village","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:478","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:ambermill","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",["end"]="Dalaran Crate",level="14",faction="Horde",id=477},src={"Border Crossings"}}
E["quest:478"] = {t="quest",n="Maps and Runes",z="silverpine",s="Maps and Runes is a Forsaken reconnaissance mission in Silverpine Forest. After discovering a suspicious shipment shipped toward Ambermill, adventurers recover a rune-inscribed pendant to deliver to Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher for further investigation.",h="Maps and Runes is a Forsaken reconnaissance mission in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Hidden Cargo",b="While intercepting logistics around Ambermill, Horde agents uncover a Dalaran crate concealed along the border routes. Rather than mundane supplies, the container holds detailed regional charts and an enigmatic, rune-inscribed pendant. Recognizing the potential danger of Dalaran's arcane reach so close to their borders, scouts carefully retrieve the artifact to avoid alarming the surrounding human sentries.",sp=0},{t="Whispers at the Sepulcher",b="Returning to the Sepulcher, the recovered pendant is presented to Shadow Priest Allister. The Forsaken leadership recognizes that the Kirin Tor are operating within Ambermill with focused intent, yet the exact nature of their workings remains obscured. Unable to decipher the potent sorcery woven into the runes himself, Allister resolves to consult arcane experts among the undead to unravel Dalaran's plot.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Dalaran crate?",a="The crate contains strategic maps of the Silverpine region and a strange rune-inscribed pendant. These items reveal that Dalaran's wizards are actively planning maneuvers around the town of Ambermill.",al={"what was in the crate","crate contents","dalaran crate loot"},it="item"},{q="Who is Shadow Priest Allister?",a="Shadow Priest Allister is a prominent Forsaken authority stationed at the Sepulcher. He oversees local intelligence gathering and coordinates defensive efforts against hostile human remnants and Kirin Tor operatives in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is allister","shadow priest allister lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Forsaken concerned about Dalaran in Ambermill?",a="Ambermill serves as an active foothold for the Kirin Tor right on the border of Lordaeron lands claimed by the Forsaken. Any mobilization of arcane relics or secretive troop movements poses an immediate threat to the Undercity's dominion over Silverpine.",al={"why ambermill matters","forsaken dalaran conflict"},it="threat"},{q="Can Shadow Priest Allister decipher the pendant?",a="No. While Allister recognizes that the artifact belongs to Dalaran sorcerers, its specific enchantments elude his priestly craft, prompting him to seek the aid of someone with deeper arcane mastery.",al={"does allister know the runes","can allister read the pendant"}},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="The investigation continues with Dalar's Analysis, where the pendant is passed along to Dalar Dawnweaver, an arcane specialist at the Sepulcher capable of breaking down Kirin Tor magic.",al={"what is the next quest","after maps and runes"},it="next_step"},{q="What quest leads up to Maps and Runes?",a="This quest directly follows Border Crossings, in which the Forsaken assign an operative to inspect suspicious trade crates moving into Silverpine from the borders of Dalaran.",al={"prerequisite quest","maps and runes prereq"},it="origin",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Dalaran's surviving wizards maintain outposts uncomfortably close to Undercity territory. Recovering their enchanted talismans is vital to safeguarding Forsaken sovereignty in Silverpine.",["class:Mage"]="The rune-inscribed pendant displays signature Kirin Tor enchantment patterns, highlighting Dalaran's distinct tradition of shielding and arcane warding.",["class:Priest"]="Though Shadow Priest Allister wields formidable shadow magic, divine and shadowy disciplines prove ill-suited for untangling the intricate arcane formulas carved into the pendant.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Silverpine Forest from Alliance-aligned forces like the Kirin Tor ensures the Horde maintains a vital supply corridor across northern Lordaeron."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran crate","kirin tor","maps and runes","rune-inscribed pendant","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"quest:477","quest:481","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:ambermill","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Dalaran Crate",["end"]="Shadow Priest Allister",level="14",faction="Horde",id=478},src={"Maps and Runes"}}
E["quest:479"] = {t="quest",n="Ambermill Investigations",z="silverpine",s="Ambermill Investigations is a Forsaken mission assigned by Shadow Priest Allister from the Sepulcher. With Dalaran wizards weaving magic in the nearby town of Ambermill, the Forsaken must disrupt their spellwork and strip their magical foci to keep hold of Silverpine Forest.",h="Ambermill Investigations is a Forsaken mission assigned by Shadow Priest Allister from the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Threat from the East",b="The human town of Ambermill sits nestled in the hills of eastern Silverpine Forest, firmly occupied by wizards and defenders pledged to the Kirin Tor of Dalaran. As the mages engage in a vast, concerted ritual to weave magical energies, Shadow Priest Allister and his companion Dalar recognize an immediate peril. If the Kirin Tor are permitted to channel their power unchecked, the Forsaken risk being swept out of Silverpine entirely.",sp=0},{t="Disrupting the Weave",b="While Dalar scries and traces the flow of magic across the forest, Allister dispatches agents to Ambermill to strike directly at the practitioners. Dalaran conjurers, mages, and their protectors wear enchanted pendants that aid in focusing and coordinating their arts. Stripping these talismans from the slain sorcerers disrupts their ritual, buying the Sepulcher critical time to pinpoint the ringleader directing the arcane weave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Shadow Priest Allister targeting Ambermill?",a="The Kirin Tor mages entrenched in Ambermill are actively channeling powerful arcane energies. Allister fears that if their spellcasting succeeds, the Forsaken will lose control of Silverpine Forest.",al={"why attack ambermill","allister motive","ambermill threat"},it="motive"},{q="What are the Dalaran Pendants used for?",a="Dalaran conjurers, mages, and protectors wear these pendants as focuses for their craft. Taking them weakens the wizards' efforts and helps Allister analyze the Kirin Tor's magical progress.",al={"what are dalaran pendants","pendant purpose","why collect pendants"},it="item"},{q="Where is Ambermill located?",a="Ambermill lies along the eastern hills of Silverpine Forest. From the Sepulcher, head south along the main thoroughfare and follow the fork leading east into the town.",al={"ambermill location","how to get to ambermill","where is ambermill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Dalar, and how is he involved?",a="Dalar is a Forsaken practitioner stationed at the Sepulcher alongside Shadow Priest Allister, tasked with tracking and unmasking the magical sources fueling the Dalaran wizards in Ambermill.",al={"who is dalar","dalar role","dalar silverpine"},it="people"},{q="What happens after recovering the pendants?",a="Collecting the pendants reveals that the Dalaran ritual is already well advanced, led by an adept wizard who must be confronted directly to halt the spellcasting entirely.",al={"what happens next","ambermill investigations follow up","after dalaran pendants"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are Dalaran humans still in Silverpine Forest?",a="Dalaran maintained several outposts and settlements across the region prior to the Third War. Even after the kingdom's devastation, surviving Kirin Tor forces continue to hold Ambermill against the Scourge and Forsaken.",al={"why are dalaran humans here","kirin tor in silverpine","ambermill lore"},it="why_here"},{q="Who are you sent against in Ambermill?",a="Shadow Priest Allister sends you directly against the human forces holding the fortified town of Ambermill: Dalaran conjurers, mages, and their protectors. While Dalaran's ruined capital lies further east under an arcane shield, these wizards and guards maintain a stronghold here in Silverpine, actively channeling dangerous magic that threatens Forsaken control over the forest.",al={"who are the targets","ambermill enemies","who do i fight in ambermill"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Kirin Tor remnants in Ambermill sit right on the doorstep of the Undercity's territory, making their magical machinations an intolerable danger to Forsaken survival.",["class:Mage"]="Mages recognize the precise coordination required to weave large-scale arcane rituals, understanding why severing the Kirin Tor's enchanted foci disrupts their spellcraft.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Silverpine Forest keeps the western approaches to Lordaeron safe from Alliance-aligned outposts loyal to Dalaran."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalar","dalaran","kirin tor","pendant","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:482","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",level="16",faction="Horde",id=479,ri={"Dalaran Pendant"}},src={"Ambermill Investigations"}}
E["quest:480"] = {t="quest",n="The Weaver",z="silverpine",s="The Weaver is a strike mission assigned by Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher to halt Dalaran's magical operations in Silverpine Forest. A Dalaran archmage, Ataeric, is directing efforts to reactivate a powerful ley energy node in the region. By slaying the archmage and claiming his staff, the Forsaken disrupt Dalaran's occult ambitions and secure their grip on the surrounding lands.",h="The Weaver is a strike mission assigned by Shadow Priest Allister in the Sepulcher to halt Dalaran's magical...",sec={{t="Severing the Ley Thread",b="Following preliminary investigations into Ambermill and Dalaran's movements in Silverpine Forest, the Forsaken learned of a hazardous development: the wizards are attempting to harness and reactivate a dormant ley energy node. Left unchecked, access to such concentrated arcane power would allow Dalaran to fortify their position and threaten the Undercity's dominion over the southern reaches of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="The Archmage's Fall",b="Shadow Priest Allister recognizes that dismantling an operation of this magnitude requires cutting off its head. The effort is orchestrated by Archmage Ataeric, a formidable wizard cloistered behind wards and fellow magi. Striking him down and claiming his staff dissipates the gathered magic, casting the ley energies back into dormancy and thwarting the Kirin Tor's ambitions in the valley.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Weaver?",a="The Weaver refers to Archmage Ataeric, a powerful Dalaran spellcaster stationed in Silverpine Forest. He is tasked with weaving together and reactivating the latent magical ley energies running beneath the area.",al={"who is the weaver","archmage ataeric","ataeric weaver"},it="target"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want the archmage killed?",a="If Dalaran successfully taps into the dormant ley energy node, their magi would gain a vast source of arcane power right on the doorstep of the Undercity. Shadow Priest Allister sees this as an intolerable threat to Forsaken sovereignty and orders a swift assassination before the node becomes fully operational.",al={"why kill ataeric","forsaken dalaran conflict","why attack dalaran"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after Ataeric is defeated?",a="With Ataeric slain and his staff confiscated, the arcane network collapses. The gathered spells dissipate and the ley line recedes into dormancy, depriving the Kirin Tor of their primary foothold of arcane power in southern Silverpine.",al={"after the weaver","quest outcome","what happens to ley node"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Shadow Priest Allister, a Forsaken authority stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, provides the orders after analyzing earlier intelligence gathered from Dalaran's presence around Ambermill.",al={"who gives the weaver","allister quest","quest giver weaver"},it="identity"},{q="What is the significance of Ataeric's staff?",a="Archmage Ataeric's staff serves as the conduit and focal point for manipulating the regional ley energies. Retrieving it ensures that the magic unravels completely and provides Allister with an artifact that might be studied for the Forsaken's own designs.",al={"ataerics staff","archmage staff purpose","why take the staff"},it="item"},{q="Where does Dalaran's presence in Silverpine come from?",a="Despite the devastation of Dalaran during the Third War, remnants of the Kirin Tor maintain fortified enclaves, outposts, and arcane experiments in neighboring territories like Ambermill, attempting to re-establish control and harness vital magical reserves.",al={"dalaran in silverpine","why are dalaran mages in silverpine","ambermill dalaran"},it="place"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Dalaran's living magi actively dispute Forsaken control over the ruins of Lordaeron. Neutralizing their archmage is vital to securing the Sepulcher's perimeter.",["class:Mage"]="The manipulation of ley lines requires deep mastery over arcane geometry; slaying Ataeric reveals how vulnerable such delicate rituals are when their prime conduits fall.",["class:Priest"]="Shadow Priest Allister directs this operation not with spells of holy restoration, but with calculating will to extinguish an arcane catalyst before it blossoms.",["faction:Horde"]="Dalaran remnants remain hostile to the Horde, making any expansion of their arcane infrastructure a direct threat to Horde territory in northern Lordaeron."},kw={"allister","ambermill","ataeric","dalaran","kirin tor","ley energy","sepulcher","silverpine","weaver"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:479","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",level="22",faction="Horde",id=480,ri={"Ataeric's Staff"}},src={"The Weaver (quest)"}}
E["quest:481"] = {t="quest",n="Dalar's Analysis",z="silverpine",s="Dalar's Analysis is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest linking Shadow Priest Allister's espionage against Ambermill with the arcane research of Dalar Dawnweaver. After uncovering a rune-inscribed pendant from a Dalaran supply crate, adventurers bring the relic to Dalar at the Sepulcher for scrutiny. The artifact reveals that the surviving mages of Dalaran are marshaling significant magical power for a hidden initiative.",h="Dalar's Analysis is a Horde quest in Silverpine Forest linking Shadow Priest Allister's espionage against...",sec={{t="A Courier's Cargo",b="Following a raid on a Dalaran supply crate at a camp north of Pyrewood Village, Shadow Priest Allister receives a rune-inscribed pendant found beneath a bundle of old maps. Recognizing that its enchantment lies beyond his spiritual purview, Allister directs the relic to Dalar Dawnweaver, an arcane scholar stationed at the Sepulcher who is better suited to decipher Dalaran's magical warding.",sp=0},{t="Kirin Tor Machinations",b="Upon examining the pendant, Dalar Dawnweaver identifies it as a specialized conduit historically favored by high-ranking wizards of the Kirin Tor to channel potent magical energies. The sheer volume of such relics being funneled directly into the fortified town of Ambermill suggests the wizards are preparing an arcane undertaking of vast scale, prompting Dalar to probe past their magical wards to divine their true intentions.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the rune-inscribed pendant?",a="The pendant is an arcane artifact used by senior mages of the Kirin Tor to safely channel large amounts of magical energy. Its discovery in transit indicates that Ambermill is being supplied with powerful foci for high-level spellcraft.",al={"what is pendant","kirin tor pendant lore","ambermill pendant"},it="item"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister send the pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Shadow Priest Allister primarily deals with shadow magic and intelligence gathering for the Forsaken at the Sepulcher. Because the pendant is a complex arcane relic of Dalaran craftsmanship, it requires an arcane specialist like Dalar Dawnweaver to properly inspect its runes and deduce its purpose.",al={"why dalar","who is dalar dawnweaver","why send to sepulcher"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Ambermill and why are the Forsaken monitoring it?",a="Ambermill is a fortified human town in southeastern Silverpine Forest maintained by the mages of Dalaran. Situated deep within territory claimed by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the town presents an immediate military and magical threat to the Forsaken, prompting strict surveillance of its borders.",al={"why watch ambermill","ambermill wizards","dalaran in silverpine"},it="place"},{q="What happens after Dalar analyzes the pendant?",a="Recognizing that the Kirin Tor are amassing arcane conduits for a major endeavor, Dalar uses his own magic to scry through the defensive shields of Ambermill in the subsequent task, Dalaran's Intentions, to discover precisely what the wizards are planning.",al={"what comes next","after dalar's analysis","dalaran intent"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where can Dalar Dawnweaver be found?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is located inside the crypt at the Sepulcher, the primary Forsaken bastion in Silverpine Forest situated along the main road.",al={"dalar location","where is dalar","dalar dawnweaver silverpine"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Kirin Tor operating openly in Silverpine Forest?",a="Ambermill was an established holding of Dalaran before the Scourge devastated Lordaeron. Despite the fall of the capital and Dalaran itself, the surviving wizards have retained Ambermill as an active redoubt, clashing constantly with the Forsaken expansion.",al={"kirin tor silverpine","dalaran presence silverpine"},it="threat"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages will recognize the Kirin Tor pendant as a classic channeling tool used in traditional Dalaran spellweaving, showing that their old brethren are preparing an immense invocation.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, monitoring Dalaran's operations at Ambermill is crucial to safeguarding the borders of Silverpine and protecting the Sepulcher from hostile sorcery.",["faction:Horde"]="Thwarting the Kirin Tor's projects in Silverpine keeps the Eastern Kingdoms secure against resurgent Alliance-aligned magical factions."},kw={"ambermill","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran","kirin tor","pendant","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:478","quest:482","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",["end"]="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="14",faction="Horde",id=481},src={"Dalar's Analysis"}}
E["quest:482"] = {t="quest",n="Dalaran's Intentions",z="silverpine",s="Dalaran's Intentions is a Silverpine Forest quest delivered by Dalar Dawnweaver to Shadow Priest Allister. Having studied a rune-inscribed pendant bound for the Kirin Tor in Ambermill, Dalar realizes the wizards intend to tap a dormant ley energy node beneath the town, prompting the Forsaken leadership at the Sepulcher to plan a counter-offensive.",h="Dalaran's Intentions is a Silverpine Forest quest delivered by Dalar Dawnweaver to Shadow Priest Allister.",sec={{t="A Dormant Spark",b="While examining a rune-inscribed pendant recovered from a Dalaran supply crate, Dalar Dawnweaver remembers an old Kirin Tor survey. Ambermill was not chosen by the mages by coincidence; the quiet village rests directly atop a dormant ley energy node. Awaking such a subterranean nexus requires immense magical reserves, and the enchanted pendants worn by the wizards serve as key components in channeling and catalyzing that power.",sp=0},{t="The Threat to Silverpine",b="The Forsaken cannot tolerate a fortified, power-fueled Kirin Tor outpost threatening the southern approaches to the Sepulcher and Tirisfal Glades. Whatever grand ritual the magi are preparing, harnessing raw ley lines would grant Dalaran an enormous strategic advantage in Lordaeron. Dalar sends word urgently to Shadow Priest Allister to formulate a strategy that will stall the wizards' progress before their ritual reaches completion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Kirin Tor trying to do in Ambermill?",a="The wizards of Dalaran are attempting to reactivate a dormant ley energy node situated beneath Ambermill. Tapping this arcane vein would grant them tremendous power to establish a permanent presence and pursue their broader plans in Silverpine Forest.",al={"ambermill ley line","what are dalaran wizards doing in silverpine","ambermill purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Dalar send you to Shadow Priest Allister?",a="Shadow Priest Allister acts as a senior military and spiritual leader for the Forsaken based out of the Sepulcher. Dalar Dawnweaver provides arcane insight and research, but tactical decisions and offensive countermeasures against Dalaran fall under Allister's authority.",al={"why tell allister","who is allister","dalar dawnweaver allister"},it="next_step"},{q="How do the wizards' pendants tie into their plans?",a="Reawakening a dormant ley node demands massive reserves of power. The Dalaran wizards carry enchanted pendants that act as conduits and reservoirs for this magic. Depriving the mages of these pendants undermines their ability to complete the activation.",al={"kirin tor pendants","ambermill pendants","why collect pendants"},it="item"},{q="Why is Dalar Dawnweaver so concerned about the Kirin Tor's work in Ambermill?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver realizes that Ambermill rests upon a dormant ley energy node earmarked by the Kirin Tor. If the human wizards successfully awaken and harness that raw arcane power, it could grant Dalaran a formidable foothold right in the heart of Silverpine Forest. To secure the region for the Forsaken and eliminate a gathering magical threat, Dalar must ensure the Sepulcher's leadership takes immediate action to halt their work.",al={"why does dalar want this done","dalar dawnweaver motive","why stop kirin tor ambergrove"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Dalaran's presence so deep in Silverpine is a direct threat to the Forsaken's borders; stopping their ley line ritual protects the roads between Tirisfal and the southern borders.",["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages will recognize the Kirin Tor's methods: tapping dormant ley lines is an efficient way to establish a powerful arcane beachhead without hauling massive power sources across wilderness.",["class:Priest"]="Shadow Priest Allister directs the Forsaken defense at the Sepulcher, blending cold military pragmatism with the dark teachings of the Cult of Forgotten Shadow to purge living threats."},kw={"ambermill","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran's intentions","kirin tor","ley energy","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:481","quest:479","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",["end"]="Shadow Priest Allister",level="14",faction="Horde",id=482},src={"Dalaran's Intentions"}}
E["quest:516"] = {t="quest",n="Beren's Peril",z="silverpine",s="Beren's Peril is a Horde quest directed by Shadow Priest Allister from the Sepulcher. Agents of the Forsaken have caught wind of a hidden conclave of Scourge massing inside a secluded cave tucked into the southern Silverpine hills, aiming to strike them down before an offensive can begin.",h="Beren's Peril is a Horde quest directed by Shadow Priest Allister from the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Preemptive Strike",b="Word reached Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher that mindless servants of the Lich King were massing deep within southern Silverpine Forest. Left unchecked, these Scourge forces posed an immediate threat to Forsaken operations throughout the region. Rather than waiting for the assault to land, Allister directs scouts to take the initiative and eliminate the gathering horde inside their secluded lair before they can mobilize.",sp=0},{t="The Hidden Cave",b="Beren's Peril itself is an obscure cavern network carved into the hills south of the Dalaran-aligned settlement of Ambermill. The treacherous terrain makes the cavern easy to overlook, approached only by navigating around the southern slopes. Within its shadows dwell the Ravenclaw drudgers and guardians, entrenched remnants of the plague whose destruction helps ensure the Forsaken maintain their tenuous hold over the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Beren's Peril?",a="Beren's Peril is a secluded cave located in the mountainous hills of southern Silverpine Forest, situated south of Ambermill. It serves as a hideout for Scourge remnants known as the Ravenclaw undead.",al={"berens peril","where is berens peril","what is this cave"},it="place"},{q="Who assigns the mission to Beren's Peril?",a="Shadow Priest Allister, stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, gives the quest to Horde adventurers after learning that hostile undead are staging an offensive from the cave.",al={"who gives berens peril","quest giver berens peril","shadow priest allister quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking the undead there?",a="The undead residing in Beren's Peril are loyal to the Lich King and part of the Scourge. The Forsaken broke free from the Lich King's control and actively fight to purge his lingering minions from their lands.",al={"why kill undead","why fight ravenclaw","arent forsaken undead"},it="motive"},{q="How do you find the entrance to the cave?",a="The cave is tucked into the hills south of Ambermill. Due to the steep ridges, the entrance must be approached from the southern face of the hills rather than directly from the north.",al={"how to get to berens peril","cave entrance location","where is the cave entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What enemies inhabit Beren's Peril?",a="The cave is inhabited by Scourge thralls, specifically Ravenclaw Drudgers and Ravenclaw Guardians, who appear to be gathering for an assault against nearby settlements.",al={"berens peril mobs","what is inside berens peril"},it="target"},{q="What role does Dalaran play in this mission?",a="Dalaran has no direct role in the quest itself, though human wizards from Dalaran occupy Ambermill nearby. Allister notes their presence merely as a landmark to help scouts locate the hidden cave.",al={"dalaran connection","ambermill connection"},it="allies"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, rooting out Scourge remnants like those at Beren's Peril is a matter of pure survival, cementing their sovereignty against the lingering grip of the Lich King.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing out hidden pockets of Scourge along the borders of Silverpine helps stabilize northern Lordaeron for the Horde as a whole.",["class:Priest"]="Operating under the orders of Shadow Priest Allister, dark casters assist in securing the Sepulcher's authority by snuffing out rival undead horrors."},kw={"ambermill","beren's peril","berens peril","ravenclaw drudger","ravenclaw guardian","scourge","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","subzone:ambermill","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",level="21",faction="Horde",id=516,ri={"Ravenclaw Drudger","Ravenclaw Guardian"}},src={"Beren's Peril (quest)"}}
E["quest:6321"] = {t="quest",n="Supplying the Sepulcher",z="silverpine",s="Supplying the Sepulcher is a logistical task issued by Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. To keep the local Deathguard detachment equipped against feral horrors and Scourge prowling the woods, an urgent weapon requisition must be routed via bat handler Karos Razok toward weapon suppliers in the Undercity.",h="Supplying the Sepulcher is a logistical task issued by Deathguard Podrig at the Sepulcher in Silverpine...",sec={{t="Arming the Front Line",b="While Deathguard Podrig reports that the Sepulcher is relatively well-stocked, continuous attrition in Silverpine Forest consumes equipment at an alarming rate. Between feral beasts, prowling Scourge remnants, and aggressive local threats, frontline gear wears down or gets abandoned in skirmishes. Under orders from Executor Hadrec, Podrig drafts a direct requisition order addressed to Gordon Wendham, a weapon dealer operating out of the capital. Securing a steady flow of replacement blades and armor is essential if the Forsaken hope to retain their fragile footholds outside Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0},{t="The Flight Network",b="Moving critical correspondence and military supplies through Silverpine's mist-choked roads on foot is slow and prone to ambush. To bypass these perils, the Forsaken rely on captive, trained vampire bats. Handing Podrig's requisition to bat handler Karos Razok integrates foot soldiers into the broader aerial logistics network of the Undercity, establishing the aerial transit lines that tie outlying garrisons directly to Sylvanas's capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Podrig's order?",a="Deathguard Podrig inspected the Sepulcher's armory on behalf of Executor Hadrec. While provisions and general gear were sufficient, weapons were needed to replace those broken or lost in skirmishes against the Scourge and other forest threats.",al={"why podrig order","what is podrigs requisition","purpose of supplying the sepulcher"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Gordon Wendham?",a="Gordon Wendham is a weapon merchant stationed in the Undercity. Podrig directs the requisition specifically to him to fulfill the garrison's need for new arms.",al={"who is gordon wendham","gordon wendham undrcity"},it="people"},{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok is the bat handler stationed at the Sepulcher. He oversees the roost of dread bats used to transport messengers, scouts, and supplies across Lordaeron.",al={"karos razok role","who is the bat handler"},it="people"},{q="Why use bats instead of road couriers?",a="Silverpine Forest is infested with hostile beasts, roving Scourge, and other dangerous factions. Couriers traveling by road face constant ambush, making aerial bat routes the fastest and safest link to the Undercity.",al={"why fly to undercity","why use bats"}},{q="What threats does the Sepulcher face?",a="The Sepulcher is surrounded by hostile forces, including lingering Scourge undead, worgen, wild beasts, and regional human factions, necessitating constant combat readiness and steady equipment replacements.",al={"sepulcher threats","why do deathguards need weapons"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this task lead next?",a="Delivering the order to Karos Razok prompts him to arrange direct flight transport to the Undercity, where the requisition can be delivered directly to Gordon Wendham.",al={"what quest is next","next after supplying the sepulcher"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deathguard Podrig need this supply order delivered?",a="Deathguard Podrig conducted an inventory under Executor Hadrec's orders to ensure the Sepulcher remains fully armed. While general supplies are stable, ongoing skirmishes in Silverpine Forest against the Scourge and other prowling threats have cost the guards many of their weapons in the field. To keep the outpost from becoming defenseless, Podrig urgently needs this requisition sent to Gordon Wendham in the Undercity so replacement arms can be secured.",al={"why does podrig want this done","podrig motive","why order weapons"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Podrig send you instead of handling the delivery himself?",a="Podrig is on active guard duty maintaining the Sepulcher's defenses alongside Executor Hadrec. With hostile Scourge roaming the surrounding woods, every Deathguard is needed to secure the perimeter and hold the camp. An able-bodied traveler provides the ideal courier to liaise with the bat master without pulling a soldier away from post.",al={"why send me","why doesnt podrig go","why rely on an adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Maintaining outposts like the Sepulcher ensures the Forsaken can project force beyond Tirisfal Glades and secure the surrounding wilderness for the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="Establishing and maintaining reliable flight networks between garrisons and capital cities is fundamental to coordinated military defense across contested regions."},kw={"bat handler","deathguard","gordon wendham","hadrec","karos razok","podrig","requisition","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok","npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge"},m={start="Deathguard Podrig",["end"]="Karos Razok",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6321},src={"Supplying the Sepulcher"}}
E["quest:8645"] = {t="quest",n="Obsidian the Elder",z="silverpine",s="Obsidian the Elder is an encounter with an ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival. Situated in Silverpine Forest near the Sepulcher, he honors travelers who come to pay homage to the ancient traditions of Azeroth. Visiting him provides a Coin of Ancestry and his blessing.",h="Obsidian the Elder is an encounter with an ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit in the Shadow of the Sepulcher",b="Amid the blighted pine woods and desolate tombs of Silverpine Forest, the presence of Elder Obsidian offers a rare moment of peace. Positioned just beside the cemetery at the Sepulcher, this spectral elder watches over a region caught between the shadows of the Forsaken and the feral beasts of the wild. He greets those who approach not as faction warriors, but as wayfarers honoring ancient wisdom.",sp=0},{t="Veneration of the Ancestors",b="Elder Obsidian is part of the Cenarion Circle's annual Lunar Festival, a time dedicated to honoring the elders who shaped Azeroth in ages past. Travelers who seek him out receive a Coin of Ancestry and his heartfelt praise for continuing to venerate the olden races, proving that even in grim, plague-touched corners of the world, older traditions endure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Elder Obsidian?",a="Elder Obsidian stands just to the right of the cemetery in the Sepulcher, the primary Horde outpost in central Silverpine Forest.",al={"elder obsidian location","where is elder obsidian","obsidian silverpine spot"}},{q="What is the purpose of seeking out Elder Obsidian?",a="Visiting Elder Obsidian completes a holiday task for the Lunar Festival, granting a Coin of Ancestry and festive favor from the ancient elders.",al={"why visit elder obsidian","what does obsidian give","elder obsidian reward"}},{q="Can Alliance players visit Elder Obsidian?",a="While the Sepulcher is a heavily fortified Horde settlement, Lunar Festival elders are generally peaceful to all who pay homage. However, Alliance travelers must brave the hostile Forsaken guards stationed nearby.",al={"is obsidian horde only","alliance elder obsidian","can alliance talk to obsidian"}},{q="Who are the elders during the Lunar Festival?",a="The elders are spectral projections and spirits of respected ancestors from ancient races. During the Lunar Festival, they manifest across Azeroth to share their wisdom and reward those who honor history.",al={"who are elders","lunar festival elders lore","what are elder spirits"}},{q="Why is an elder present in Silverpine Forest?",a="The elders appear across all corners of Azeroth to remind mortals of the ancient world before modern conflicts. Even in lands newly claimed by the Forsaken, elder spirits persist.",al={"why silverpine elder","elder in undead lands","sepulcher elder lore"}},{q="What are Coins of Ancestry used for?",a="Coins of Ancestry earned from elders like Obsidian can be brought to Lunar Festival emissaries in Moonglade and capital cities to trade for festive garments, recipes, and seasonal trinkets.",al={"coin of ancestry use","what to do with coins","lunar coins"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Resting right beside the Sepulcher cemetery, Elder Obsidian is exceptionally easy and safe for Horde members questing through Silverpine to visit.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance wanderers seeking Elder Obsidian's blessing must sneak or fight their way deep into the heart of Silverpine Forest and skirt the Forsaken guards at the Sepulcher.",["race:Undead"]="Elder Obsidian offers a poignant contrast to the grim reality of the Sepulcher, acknowledging that travelers still recognize the olden races despite the tragedies that befell Lordaeron.",["class:Druid"]="As emissaries aligned with the Cenarion Circle's seasonal celebrations, honoring elders like Obsidian reflects the druidic commitment to remembering the ancient world."},kw={"ancestors","coin of ancestry","elder obsidian","lunar festival","obsidian","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"npc:elder-obsidian","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:horde"},m={start="Elder Obsidian",id=8645},src={"Obsidian the Elder"}}
E["quest:91859"] = {t="quest",n="A Curious Pair",z="silverpine",s="A Curious Pair begins when Trevan Rol notices an unusual duo passing through the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Under the banner of the Earthen Ring, a tauren was seen traveling alongside a high elf—an alliance rare enough in Horde territory to prompt immediate suspicion.",h="A Curious Pair begins when Trevan Rol notices an unusual duo passing through the Sepulcher in Silverpine...",sec={{t="Eyes in the Sepulcher",b="The Sepulcher is a grim waystation where strangers are scrutinized carefully, especially those claiming diplomatic business. When two representatives purporting to belong to the Earthen Ring passed along the road, local scout Trevan Rol caught sight of them. While a tauren walking under the shamanic order's mantle surprised no one, his cloaked companion struck the Forsaken as exceedingly bizarre: an unmistakable high elf.",sp=0},{t="A Peculiar Partnership",b="The presence of a quel'dorei traveling openly alongside a member of the Horde's shamanic circles naturally raises questions for the Forsaken sentries. The Earthen Ring typically concerns itself with the balance of the elements and rarely fields high elves in Lordaeron, let alone as companions to tauren envoys. To verify where this unusual pair went and what business they might have in the forest, travelers are directed to consult Deathguard Baldren at the edge of town.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the two travelers mentioned in this quest?",a="According to Trevan Rol, the travelers presented themselves as Earthen Ring dignitaries. One was a tauren, typical of the shamanic organization, but his traveling companion was identified as a cloaked high elf.",al={"who is the curious pair","who passed through sepulcher","who were the travelers"},it="people"},{q="Why is a high elf traveling with a tauren so unusual?",a="High elves have historical ties to the Alliance and arcane magic, while tauren are devoted members of the Horde and deep practitioners of shamanism. Seeing members of these two peoples traveling together through Horde-controlled Silverpine Forest under the Earthen Ring is an exceedingly rare and suspicious sight.",al={"why is high elf with tauren weird","tauren and high elf lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Who starts the quest A Curious Pair?",a="The quest is given by Trevan Rol in the Sepulcher, an outpost located in Silverpine Forest.",al={"quest giver","where to pick up a curious pair"},gp=true},{q="Where do I find Deathguard Baldren?",a="Deathguard Baldren stands on watch near the entrance of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, keeping watch over travelers along the road.",al={"baldren location","where is baldren"},gp=true},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an ancient organization of shamans dedicated to preserving the balance of the elements and healing spiritual discord throughout the world. While mostly comprised of shamans like tauren and orcs, their diplomats occasionally travel into distant lands.",al={"earthen ring lore","what is earthen ring"},it="identity"},{q="Is the high elf an enemy to the Forsaken?",a="It is not immediately clear. Trevan Rol notes that the elf was cloaked and traveling under diplomatic pretense alongside a tauren, leading the Forsaken to question their purpose rather than attack outright.",al={"are they hostile","is elf an enemy"},it="hostile"},{q="Why does Trevan Rol want me to investigate the travelers?",a="Trevan Rol is baffled and suspicious after spotting a cloaked high elf travelling openly alongside a tauren under the banner of the Earthen Ring. Silverpine is dangerous Horde territory, and a member of the quel'dorei passing through without explanation is an extraordinary anomaly. Trevan wants to uncover what this odd pair is doing in Forsaken lands, but having exhausted what little he witnessed, he sends you to the town entrance to see what the sentries caught.",al={"why does trevan care","trevan rol motive","why investigate the travelers"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The mention of the Earthen Ring traveling alongside an elf is unusual even to experienced shamans, who know the Ring's traditions rarely involve the quel'dorei.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren adventurers may feel conflicted seeing one of their kin traveling alongside an elven stranger through Lordaeron, drawing the sharp eyes of Forsaken sentries.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken guarding the Sepulcher, any outsider slipping through Silverpine Forest warrants close scrutiny, especially given Lordaeron's fractured political climate."},kw={"curious pair","deathguard baldren","earthen ring","high elf","sepulcher","silverpine forest","tauren","trevan rol"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},m={start="Trevan Rol",["end"]="Deathguard Baldren",level="22",faction="Horde",id=91859},src={"A Curious Pair"},fv=true}
E["quest:99"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="Arugal's Folly culminates in a dangerous investigation into the curse gripping Pyrewood Village. Dalar Dawnweaver tasks Horde operatives with obtaining enchanted shackles from the villagers to decode Archmage Arugal's twisted handiwork. Unraveling these bindings exposes the tragic magic holding the settlement under the shadow of the worgen.",h="Arugal's Folly culminates in a dangerous investigation into the curse gripping Pyrewood Village.",sec={{t="The Dual Lives of Pyrewood",b="South of the Sepulcher lies Pyrewood Village, a settlement caught in an uncanny state of existence. Under the daylight sun, its residents go about their lives as ordinary human peasants, fearful and insular. Yet as twilight falls over the forest, their human forms tear apart into savage Moonrage worgen, roaming the streets under Arugal's sway. Dalar Dawnweaver seeks to unravel the exact arcane bindings causing this diurnal horror.",sp=0},{t="Shattering the Shackles",b="To analyze the enchantment holding Pyrewood in thrall, Dawnweaver requires enchanted Pyrewood Shackles taken directly from the transformed townsfolk. Rather than simple iron, these restraints thrum with the residual sorcery of Arugal's failed wards. By studying their arcane composition, the Forsaken mage hopes to comprehend the mechanisms of the beastly transformation and devise a way to finally bring down the rogue archmage of Shadowfang Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do the people of Pyrewood Village turn into worgen at night?",a="Archmage Arugal cast twisted enchantments over Pyrewood Village. By day, his spells maintain an illusion or dormant state of humanity, but nightfall causes the townsfolk to transform into Moonrage worgen under his control.",al={"pyrewood day night","pyrewood curse","why human then wolf"},it="target"},{q="What are the Pyrewood Shackles?",a="They are enchanted bindings worn by the cursed residents of Pyrewood Village. Arugal used them as part of his magic over the town, and Dalar Dawnweaver uses their residual energy to study the curse.",al={"pyrewood shackle","arugal shackles"},it="item"},{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He spearheads the Forsaken's magical investigation into Archmage Arugal's summoned worgen.",al={"dalar dawnweaver lore","who is quest giver sepulcher"},it="identity"},{q="Does finishing this quest cure Pyrewood Village?",a="No. The retrieved shackles provide Dalar Dawnweaver with the magical insight needed to understand Arugal's magic, but the curse continues to hold Pyrewood in perpetual torment.",al={"can you cure pyrewood","do pyrewood people get cured"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="How does Arugal control the villagers?",a="Through reckless enchantments and enchanted shackles, Arugal bound the villagers to his will, forcing them into beastly forms that guard the approach to his domain at Shadowfang Keep.",al={"arugal pyrewood connection","how does arugal control them"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after completing the Arugal's Folly quest chain?",a="This assignment marks the final chapter of the Arugal's Folly chain. The knowledge gathered allows the Forsaken to fully assess the threat of Shadowfang Keep and plan Arugal's downfall.",al={"after arugals folly","arugals folly finale"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want the Pyrewood Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is studying the bizarre enchantments that Archmage Arugal has cast across Silverpine Forest. By analyzing the magic bound within the villagers' shackles, Dalar hopes to unravel Arugal's so-called remedies, master the secrets of his wild spells, and gather the vital knowledge required to ultimately bring down the mad mage and undo his reckless sorcery.",al={"why does dalar want this","dalar dawnweaver motive","why collect pyrewood shackles"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken view Pyrewood Village with cold fascination and ruthless pragmatism, keen to dismantle Arugal's enchantments to secure southern Silverpine.",["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, Arugal's shackles are a grim reminder of how Kirin Tor sorcery can spiral into madness when mixed with otherworldly summoned beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing these shackles breaks Arugal's mystical stranglehold over the road leading south toward the Greymane Wall."},kw={"arugal","arugal's folly","dalar dawnweaver","moonrage worgen","pyrewood shackles","pyrewood village","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","subzone:pyrewood-village","npc:arugal","topic:worgen","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:421"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="15",faction="Horde",id=99,ri={"Pyrewood Shackle"}},src={"Arugal's Folly (4)"}}
E["subzone:ambermill"] = {t="subzone",n="Ambermill",z="silverpine",s="Ambermill is a fortified human settlement in central Silverpine Forest, situated just southwest of Lordamere Lake. Originally a Gilnean lumber village, it is now occupied by surviving wizards and apprentices of Dalaran who are tapping into ancient ley lines. Their presence represents a dangerous outpost of human resistance on the southern borders of the Forsaken realm.",h="Ambermill is a fortified human settlement in central Silverpine Forest, situated just southwest of Lordamere...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Dalaran",b="Before the Third War, Ambermill was a quiet lumber town on lands owned by the Gilnean nobleman Darius Crowley. When King Genn Greymane erected the Greymane Wall to seal his kingdom away, Ambermill was left stranded outside alongside Pyrewood Village. In the chaotic aftermath of Lordaeron's fall, the surviving wizards of the Kirin Tor moved in and fortified the settlement. Dalaran spellscribes, conjurors, and apprentices now patrol its buildings and stables, using Ambermill as a forward redoubt against the undead.",sp=0},{t="Tapping the Ley Lines",b="The Kirin Tor's interest in Ambermill extends far beyond simple territorial defense. The village rests directly atop a dormant ley line energy node. Forsaken spies and Deathstalkers monitoring the town have discovered that the Dalaran magi are attempting to reactivate this nexus for large-scale arcane work. If completed, the surge of magical power could threaten the Forsaken's fragile hold on Silverpine Forest, prompting Shadow Priest Allister and the Deathstalkers to orchestrate sabotage, thefts of Kirin Tor documents, and assassinations across the mill grounds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are Dalaran wizards occupying a village in Silverpine?",a="Following the devastation of Dalaran during the Third War, surviving Kirin Tor forces moved into Ambermill to establish an outpost of living human resistance. More importantly, the village sits directly atop a dormant ley line energy node that the wizards are working to reactivate.",al={"why are wizards here","who controls ambermill","kirin tor silverpine"},it="purpose"},{q="Was Ambermill always part of Dalaran?",a="No. Ambermill was originally a lumber village belonging to the kingdom of Gilneas, located on estates held by Lord Darius Crowley. It was effectively cut off from its homeland when King Genn Greymane sealed the Greymane Wall.",al={"ambermill history","who owned ambermill","gilneas ambermill"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to attack Ambermill?",a="Ambermill serves as an active hostile base near the heart of Silverpine Forest. The Forsaken fear that if the Kirin Tor succeeds in drawing power from the local ley lines, the humans will establish a staging ground powerful enough to break undead control over the southern roads.",al={"forsaken ambermill","why kill ambermill wizards"},it="conflict"},{q="What are the Deathstalkers searching for in Ambermill?",a="Forsaken Deathstalkers learned from captured human prisoners that the wizards in Ambermill keep secured documents detailing Dalaran's secret plans and military intentions, making the settlement a primary target for covert infiltration and theft.",al={"ambermill documents","mennet carkad ambermill"},it="item"},{q="What is Ambermill?",a="Ambermill is a fortified human settlement nestled in the hills of central Silverpine Forest, southwest of Lake Lordamere. Originally a quiet Gilnean logging outpost complete with a town hall, stables, and mills, it has been repurposed into a heavily guarded military and magical encampment. Its buildings hum with arcane energy as spellcasters and guards maintain a firm perimeter against the hostile forest.",al={"what is ambermill","amber mill overview","tell me about ambermill"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to Ambermill?",a="Ambermill originally belonged to Lord Darius Crowley of Gilneas. When King Genn Greymane erected the colossal Greymane Wall to seal off their homeland from Lordaeron's troubles, Ambermill and nearby Pyrewood were stranded on the outside, sparking deep political outrage. After the Scourge ravaged the region and smashed Dalaran during the Third War, surviving Kirin Tor forces moved in and fortified the town to preserve a strategic foothold in Silverpine.",al={"ambermill history","amber mill backstory","history of ambermill"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in Ambermill?",a="Ambermill is occupied and run entirely by Kirin Tor personnel from Dalaran. Its grounds are patrolled by Dalaran Protectors, conjured arcane serpents, apprentices, and spellscribes, while senior conjurors oversee mystical operations from within the town hall and surrounding buildings. Local service workers, like the tailor Avelina Lilly, have also provided provisions and clothing to the resident magi.",al={"who controls ambermill","ambermill residents","who is at amber mill"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Ambermill dangerous?",a="Ambermill is extremely hazardous to anyone aligned with the Forsaken or the Horde. The Kirin Tor forces stationed here view the undead as an existential threat and will attack trespassers on sight. In addition to martial sentries, the settlement is guarded by skilled spellcasters who wield potent offensive magic, summoning protective arcane wards and serpent servitors to annihilate intruders.",al={"is ambermill hostile","danger in amber mill","is amber mill safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Forsaken operatives, Ambermill represents one of the few remaining pockets of living human resistance in Silverpine, threatening southern logistics and harboring dangerous arcane secrets.",["class:Mage"]="The settlement demonstrates the Kirin Tor's desperate efforts to rebuild their magical influence after the Scourge sacked Dalaran, focusing their surviving mages on raw ley line manipulation."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran","darius crowley","greymane wall","kirin tor","ley line","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran","npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:479","quest:482","quest:1999","subzone:greymane-wall","npc:darius-crowley"},src={"Ambermill"}}
E["subzone:beren-s-peril"] = {t="subzone",n="Beren's Peril",z="silverpine",s="Beren's Peril is a secluded mountain cavern tucked in the rocky hills southwest of Ambermill in Silverpine Forest. It serves as an entrenched redoubt for rogue Scourge loyalists serving the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, plotting against the nearby Forsaken.",h="Beren's Peril is a secluded mountain cavern tucked in the rocky hills southwest of Ambermill in Silverpine...",sec={{t="A Hidden Threat in the Hills",b="Tucked away high in the crags southwest of Ambermill, Beren's Peril consists of a shadowed cave and winding mountain path hidden from the main roadway. Following the devastation of the Third War, rogue Scourge undead under the command of the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw fortified this enclave. Rather than bowing to the Dark Lady or retreating north, Ravenclaw's thralls—regents, guardians, and drudgers—gathered here in secret to muster an assault against the Forsaken base at the Sepulcher. Their presence was uncovered by Forsaken scouts, turning the quiet cliffside into an active warzone for Horde operatives sent to eliminate the threat before an attack could materialize.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Beren's Peril?",a="It is a cave and surrounding hillside pass located southwest of Ambermill in Silverpine Forest, situated between the central highway and the Ambermill side road.",al={"berens peril","where is berens peril","beren's peril cave"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Beren's Peril?",a="The cave is occupied by Scourge undead loyal to the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, including Ravenclaw guardians, drudgers, and regents.",al={"who lives at berens peril","enemies at berens peril","ravenclaw undead"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about this location?",a="Forsaken scouts discovered that the undead holed up inside Beren's Peril were amassing troops and arming for an impending assault on the Sepulcher, prompting Shadow Priest Allister to order preemptive strikes against them.",al={"allister berens peril","why attack berens peril","sepulcher threat"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful necromancer operating in Silverpine Forest who maintained control over pockets of mindless and hostile Scourge minions, using sites like Beren's Peril and Fenris Keep to menace the region.",al={"thule ravenclaw","thule silverpine"},it="leader"},{q="What happened at Beren's Peril?",a="Following the Third War, this secluded cave complex in the Silverpine hills became a staging ground for renegade undead. Forsaken scouts tracking threats to the region discovered that hostile undead loyal to the rogue necromancer Thule Ravenclaw had amassed within the caverns, secretly preparing an assault against the nearby Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher.",al={"beren's peril history","what happened at berens peril","berens peril lore"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Beren's Peril dangerous?",a="Yes, Beren's Peril is extremely dangerous. The hillside cave is swarming with hostile undead under the sway of Thule Ravenclaw, including Ravenclaw drudgers, guardians, and regents. Any traveler venturing into the caverns risks being overwhelmed by these organized undead before they can launch their strike against the Sepulcher.",al={"berens peril danger","how dangerous is beren's peril","is berens peril safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Ravenclaw minions at Beren's Peril are a bitter reminder of the Scourge's lasting grip, threatening the safety of the Sepulcher and requiring swift, merciless eradication by Sylvanas's loyalists.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the rugged paths of Silverpine Forest means clearing out rogue undead nests before they can sever supply lines between the Sepulcher and the southern territories."},kw={"allister","ambermill","beren's peril","berens peril","ravenclaw drudge","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:516","quest:446","npc:shadow-priest-allister","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:ambermill","topic:forsaken","topic:third-war"},src={"Beren's Peril"}}
E["subzone:dawning-isles"] = {t="subzone",n="Dawning Isles",z="silverpine",s="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of low-lying islets situated within Lordamere Lake along the eastern edge of Silverpine Forest. Once idyllic retreats, they have succumbed to the blight of the Plague of Undeath and are overrun by aggressive murlocs and contending military factions.",h="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of low-lying islets situated within Lordamere Lake along the eastern edge of...",sec={{t="Blight on the Lake",b="Before the Third War, the Dawning Isles were known as scenic keys resting on the calm, clear waters of Lordamere Lake. When the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron, corruption seeped into the lake's shallows. The vegetation turned pallid and rotting, driving away idyllic peacefulness. Today, the Vile Fin murloc tribe dominates the muddy shores and tangled brush, aggressively defending their burgeoning colonies from anyone seeking to traverse the lake.",sp=0},{t="A Staging Ground",b="Because of their proximity to the capital, the Dawning Isles occupy a perilous strategic position. The Scarlet Crusade has used these desolate islets as a beachhead to launch probing assaults against the Undercity and the Ruins of Lordaeron. In response, Forsaken forces regularly deploy to contest the waters, turning what was once a quiet chain of islands into a frontline battleground between the living zealots and the undead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dawning Isles located?",a="The Dawning Isles are located in Lordamere Lake, bordering the eastern boundary of Silverpine Forest and resting just west of the Ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"dawning isles location","where is dawning isles","dawning islands map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit the Dawning Isles?",a="The islands are primarily infested by the Vile Fin tribe of murlocs, which thrives along the corrupted shorelines. In the past, dangerous bog beasts also prowled the islets, though they have largely vanished in favor of the teeming murloc population.",al={"mobs on dawning isles","what lives on dawning isles","dawning isle monsters"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the trees and shores rotting here?",a="The islands were tainted during the Third War when the Plague of Undeath swept Lordaeron. The water and soil absorbed the blight, poisoning the vegetation and leaving the islets murky, sickly, and decayed.",al={"why are dawning isles blighted","lake blight dawning isles"},it="ruin"},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade interested in these islands?",a="The islands offer a convenient staging ground across Lordamere Lake from which the Scarlet Crusade can mount skirmishes and strikes directly against the Forsaken holding the Ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"scarlet crusade dawning isles","crusaders in lordamere lake"},it="conflict"},{q="What are the Dawning Isles?",a="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of low keys rising out of the waters of Lordamere Lake along northeastern Silverpine Forest. Once considered an idyllic and serene retreat on the lake's crystalline surface, the archipelago has since fallen into decay under the lingering blight of the Plague of Undeath.",al={"what are dawning isles","dawning isles lore","about dawning isles"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Dawning Isles?",a="Once pristine islets upon Lordamere Lake, the Dawning Isles were ruined by the spread of the Plague of Undeath, turning their vegetation sickly and rotting the shores. Dangerous creatures overran the islands, and more recently, the Scarlet Crusade seized them as a staging ground to launch assaults against the Forsaken at the Ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"dawning isles history","what happened at dawning isles"},it="history",add=true},{q="Are the Dawning Isles dangerous?",a="Yes, they are exceptionally perilous. Beyond the lingering rot of the Plague, the isles are overrun by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs that have multiplied in great numbers, alongside heavily armed detachments of the zealous Scarlet Crusade who attack anyone entering their territory.",al={"is dawning isles safe","how dangerous are dawning isles","dawning isles danger"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Controlling the Dawning Isles is essential for safeguarding the western approaches to the Undercity against Scarlet Crusade incursions across Lordamere Lake.",["faction:Alliance"]="The blighted islands serve as a grim reminder of how far the corruption of the Scourge reached into Lordaeron's most scenic waters."},kw={"dawning isles","lordaeron","lordamere lake","scarlet crusade","silverpine forest","vile fin"},rel={"subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:silverpine","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:murloc","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Dawning Isles"}}
E["subzone:dead-field"] = {t="subzone",n="Dead Field",z="silverpine",s="The Dead Field is a blighted, abandoned farmstead situated in northern Silverpine Forest. Once quiet rural farmland, it has been seized by the Rot Hide gnolls and transformed into a forward staging ground for Scourge forces. Repeated Forsaken attempts to clear the area have faltered under the command of the banshee Nightlash.",h="The Dead Field is a blighted, abandoned farmstead situated in northern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Blighted Staging Ground",b="Little remains of the original farmstead in the northern reaches of Silverpine Forest, its previous living occupants long lost to the Third War. Today, the ruined plot serves as a base of operations for the Rot Hide gnolls, who act as willing servants to the Scourge. As their numbers swelled, Deathstalker scouts passing through the region noted signs of imminent military mobilization threatening Forsaken supply lines and outposts. Small Forsaken assaults against the farm have repeatedly failed, turned back by the wailing apparition Nightlash—a banshee who manifests whenever her gnoll thralls are endangered.",sp=0},{t="Ravenclaw's Ambition",b="The Rot Hide gnolls do not act alone. Their operations in the Dead Field are orchestrated from afar by the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, based out of Fenris Isle. Intending to assert Scourge dominance over Silverpine and drive Sylvanas's forces out of Lordaeron, Ravenclaw projects magical apparitions to the farmstead to survey his undead horde and issue warnings to Forsaken intruders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Dead Field?",a="The Dead Field is a decrepit, blighted farmstead located in northern Silverpine Forest. Once an ordinary human farm, it has fallen into ruin and is now occupied by Scourge-aligned Rot Hide gnolls.",al={"dead field silverpine","where is dead field","what happened to dead field"},it="place"},{q="Why are there gnolls at the farm?",a="These Rot Hide gnolls are under the sway of the Scourge. They use the farmstead as a forward staging ground to gather forces and prepare attacks against Forsaken positions in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"why rot hide gnolls","rot hides dead field","scourge gnolls"}},{q="Who is Nightlash?",a="Nightlash is a Scourge banshee commanding the Rot Hide gnolls at the farm. Whenever Forsaken strike forces assault the encampment, she materializes to defend her servants, repelling previous attempts to reclaim the land.",al={"nightlash banshee","banshee in dead field","who protects the gnolls"}},{q="Who commands the Scourge forces here?",a="The encampment answers to Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful necromancer operating from nearby Fenris Isle. He coordinates the gnolls through apparitions and magical oversight to harass Forsaken expansion.",al={"who controls dead field","thule ravenclaw dead field","who is in charge"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happened to the farm at the Dead Field?",a="The farm was once a homestead in northern Silverpine Forest, though the names and fates of the original farmers have been lost to the Third War. When the kingdom fell, the land fell into decrepitude, and Scourge agents moved in. Rather than cultivating crops, the Scourge turned the abandoned grounds into an outpost, rallying undead gnolls and preparing to menace nearby Forsaken holdings.",al={"dead field history","what happened at dead field","who lived at dead field"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who controls the Dead Field?",a="The farm is occupied by the Rot Hide gnolls, who serve the Scourge as foot soldiers. Above them lurks the banshee Nightlash, who oversees the outpost and appears whenever her minions are assaulted. The necromancer Thule Ravenclaw coordinates their movements from afar, using apparitions to direct their efforts against the Forsaken.",al={"who runs dead field","who lives at dead field","dead field residents"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Why is the Dead Field abandoned?",a="Like much of northern Silverpine, the farm collapsed when the Scourge overran Lordaeron. The inhabitants were killed or driven away, and no living souls remained to tend the soil or maintain the buildings. Left untended amidst plagued soil, the decaying barns and ruined fences were quickly seized by the Scourge as a forward staging ground.",al={"why is dead field ruined","why is dead field abandoned","dead field ruin"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is the Dead Field dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for anyone traveling alone. The Rot Hide gnolls gather here in growing numbers, pointing to imminent Scourge aggression. Repeated Forsaken raids have failed to dislodge them because Nightlash manifests swiftly to protect her servants, turning any direct confrontation into a lethal clash against both feral gnolls and ethereal wails.",al={"how dangerous is dead field","dead field threat","is dead field safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Scourge foothold at the Dead Field poses an immediate threat to the road between the Sepulcher and northern Lordaeron, demanding swift extermination.",["class:Rogue"]="Deathstalker recon teams monitor the farm closely; infiltrating the gnoll ranks and striking their command structure is a critical tactical priority."},kw={"banshee","dead field","deathstalkers","nightlash","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:437","quest:446","quest:1886","zone:silverpine","topic:gnoll","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},src={"Dead Field"}}
E["subzone:decrepit-ferry"] = {t="subzone",n="Decrepit Ferry",z="silverpine",s="The Decrepit Ferry is a ruined dock on the eastern shore of Silverpine Forest that once provided passage across Lordamere Lake to Fenris Isle. Following the fall of Lordaeron, the ferry was destroyed, its operator murdered, and the shoreline overrun by undead and vicious Rot Hide gnolls.",h="The Decrepit Ferry is a ruined dock on the eastern shore of Silverpine Forest that once provided passage...",sec={{t="A Lifeline Cut Short",b="Before the Third War, this dock bustled with daily traffic across Lordamere Lake. Local farmers brought fresh produce down to the water, selling their crops directly to the wealthy lord of Fenris Isle and his household. For a modest fee, the ferryman carried trade goods, messengers, and visiting nobles back and forth between the mainland and the keep. That peaceful commerce ended abruptly when the Scourge swept through the kingdom. The ferryman was brutally killed, the boats were smashed, and the pier fell into decay.",sp=0},{t="A Corrupted Shoreline",b="Today, the docks are a hazard to any traveler passing along the lake shore. With the ferry out of commission, Fenris Isle sits isolated across the water, while the ruins themselves crawl with ghouls, skeletal warriors, and roving Rot Hide gnolls. What was once an orderly point of transit has become another festering pocket of danger in Silverpine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Decrepit Ferry used for originally?",a="It was the main crossing point between mainland Silverpine and Fenris Isle. Local farmers used the ferry to haul their harvests across Lordamere Lake to sell to the island's noble lord, paying the local ferryman a small fare for each voyage.",al={"ferry history","what was this dock","why is there a ferry here"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the ferry and its ferryman?",a="When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, the dock was attacked. The ferryman was murdered, the boats and crossing gear were destroyed, and the location was abandoned to the undead.",al={"what happened to ferryman","who broke the ferry"},it="history"},{q="What monsters lurk around the ferry docks now?",a="The shoreline is infested with remnants of the Scourge, including ghouls and skeletal warriors, alongside dangerous Rot Hide gnolls prowling the nearby banks.",al={"decrepit ferry mobs","what lives at the ferry"},it="threat"},{q="Can you still take a boat to Fenris Isle from here?",a="No. The ferry was wrecked during the invasion and lies in ruins. Anyone wishing to reach Fenris Isle must swim or find alternative passage across the lake.",al={"take boat to fenris","how to get to fenris isle","does the ferry work"},gp=true},{q="What is the Decrepit Ferry?",a="The Decrepit Ferry is the ruined remains of a once-busy dock along the eastern shore of Silverpine Forest. Before the fall of Lordaeron, it served as the vital crossing point over Lake Lordamere to Fenris Isle, ferrying local farmers, travelers, and supplies out to the island estate.",al={"what is decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry silverpine","decrepit ferry docks"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is the Decrepit Ferry ruined and abandoned?",a="When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, the ferry service came to a violent end. The ferryman was murdered by the undead onslaught, the vessels were smashed, and the docks fell into utter neglect as monstrous predators overran the surrounding shores.",al={"why is it abandoned","why is decrepit ferry ruined","decrepit ferry destroyed"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is the Decrepit Ferry dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely perilous for unwary travelers. The abandoned docks and waterside are swarming with aggressive ghouls, restless skeletal warriors, and feral Rot Hide gnolls, making any attempt to linger near the landing a deadly proposition.",al={"is decrepit ferry dangerous","decrepit ferry threats","is it safe here"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Decrepit Ferry?",a="It earned its grim name from the shattered, rotting state left behind after the Third War. What was once a sturdy, bustling lifeline to Fenris Isle has decayed into weathered timbers, smashed debris, and waterlogged ruin.",al={"why is it called decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry name","origin of the name decrepit ferry"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The ruins are a grim reminder of Lordaeron's fall, now overrun by mind-numbing Scourge remnants and filthy gnolls that threaten Forsaken operations in eastern Silverpine."},kw={"decrepit ferry","fenris isle","ferryman","ghouls","lordamere lake","rot hide","scourge","silverpine forest"},rel={"subzone:fenris-isle","zone:silverpine","topic:gnoll","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","quest:438"},src={"Decrepit Ferry"}}
E["subzone:deep-elem-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Deep Elem Mine",z="silverpine",s="Deep Elem Mine is an excavation site nestled in the heart of Silverpine Forest. Once an active operation, it was overrun when Archmage Arugal's dark magic swept through the region, transforming its miners into savage worgen.",h="Deep Elem Mine is an excavation site nestled in the heart of Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Den of Beasts",b="Situated central to Silverpine Forest, the Deep Elem Mine once served the living inhabitants of Lordaeron as an ordinary resource vein. When Archmage Arugal unleashed the lupine nightmare upon the forest, his feral curse spread deep into the tunnels. The laborers inside succumbed to the affliction, turning into vicious worgen who abandoned their pickaxes to claim the cavern as a predatory lair.",sp=0},{t="Grimson and Forsaken Ambition",b="The pack within the mine is commanded by Grimson the Pale, the former mine foreman who retained his cunning even after his monstrous transformation. Recognizing the strategic value of the tunnels and their ore, the Forsaken at the Sepulcher take a keen interest in reclaiming the site. Under orders backed by the authority of Dreadlord Varimathras, Forsaken agents seek to sever Grimson's head and purge the beasts so the Horde can secure the mine's wealth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside Deep Elem Mine?",a="The mine is infested with hostile worgen afflicted by Archmage Arugal's magic. They are led by their former human foreman, Grimson the Pale, who now rules the pack deep within the tunnels.",al={"whats in deep elem mine","deep elem mine mobs","who lives in deep elem mine"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want Deep Elem Mine cleared?",a="The Forsaken seek to exploit the mine's natural mineral wealth to bolster their war efforts in Lordaeron. Dalar Dawnweaver and the leadership at the Sepulcher intend to claim its resources in the name of Dreadlord Varimathras once the worgen are eradicated.",al={"forsaken mine interest","why clear deep elem mine","who wants the mine"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Grimson the Pale?",a="Grimson was originally the mortal foreman overseeing operations at Deep Elem Mine. After Arugal's feral curse transformed the workers, Grimson became a cunning worgen alpha who retained enough intellect to command the pack inhabiting the mine.",al={"who is grimson","grimson the pale lore","deep elem mine boss"},it="leader"},{q="How did the worgen get into the mine?",a="They were not outsiders who moved in; the original miners were transformed by the spread of Archmage Arugal's curse across Silverpine Forest, turning the workforce into monsters where they worked.",al={"why are there worgen in the mine","worgen origin deep elem mine","how did miners turn"},it="history"},{q="What is Deep Elem Mine?",a="Deep Elem Mine is an old mining site carved into the hills of central Silverpine Forest. Once a regular working excavation under human overseers, it has ceased ordinary operations and fallen under the control of feral worgen spawned by Archmage Arugal's dark sorcery.",al={"deep elem mine","what is deep elem","deep elem mine silverpine"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why was Deep Elem Mine abandoned?",a="The mine fell when Archmage Arugal's fell sorcery spread across the hills of Silverpine. Rather than simply being overrun from without, the mine collapsed from within when its own foreman, Grimson the Pale, succumbed to the worgen curse and turned the site into a den for feral beasts.",al={"why is deep elem mine abandoned","deep elem mine ruined","what ruined deep elem mine"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Deep Elem Mine dangerous?",a="Deep Elem Mine is extremely perilous to wander into unprepared. Its dark tunnels are swarming with savage worgen driven by predatory instincts, all united under the ruthless command of their former overseer, Grimson the Pale.",al={"deep elem mine danger","is deep elem mine safe","threats in deep elem mine"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing the mine is both an economic necessity and a direct mandate from the Sepulcher to break Arugal's encroaching grip on central Silverpine.",["profession:Mining"]="Though currently hazardous due to the feral pack residing within, the mine represents one of Silverpine's richest subterranean mineral deposits."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","deep elem mine","grimson the pale","silverpine forest","varimathras","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","quest:99","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","topic:worgen","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","npc:varimathras"},src={"Deep Elem Mine"}}
E["subzone:fenris-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Fenris Isle",z="silverpine",s="Fenris Isle is a large, mist-shrouded island in Lordamere Lake, bordering the eastern edge of Silverpine Forest. Once home to a bustling Lordaeron military stronghold, the island now lies under the iron grip of undead Rot Hide gnolls and a rogue Scourge necromancer.",h="Fenris Isle is a large, mist-shrouded island in Lordamere Lake, bordering the eastern edge of Silverpine...",sec={{t="A Fallen Stronghold on the Lake",b="Before the Third War devastated northern Lordaeron, Fenris Isle served as a vital outpost for the kingdom, anchored by Fenris Keep. When the Scourge tore through the realm, the garrison was slaughtered or fled into exile, leaving the island abandoned to the dead. In the years since, the island became a stronghold for the Rot Hide gnolls—vile, plague-ridden creatures who established a crude empire across the lake's shores. The Forsaken of Silverpine Forest keep a vigilant watch on the island, viewing its entrenched inhabitants as a severe threat to their northern territories.",sp=0},{t="The Master of Fenris Keep",b="The Rot Hide gnolls do not act alone. Within the crumbling stone halls of Fenris Keep dwells Thule Ravenclaw, a cunning necromancer formerly aligned with the Kirin Tor who turned to the dark arts of the Scourge. Thule bent the native gnolls to his will, using dark sorcery to animate their fallen kin and fortify the island against intrusion. From this isolated sanctuary, Thule oversees the lake's ferry crossings, prompting Forsaken scouts and Horde forces to launch preemptive strikes to break his hold on the archipelago.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Fenris Isle?",a="Fenris Isle is an island located in Lordamere Lake off the eastern coast of Silverpine Forest. Prior to the Third War, it served as a fortress redoubt for the Kingdom of Lordaeron, but it is now infested with plague-ridden gnolls and servants of the Scourge.",al={"where is fenris isle","fenris isle lore","what is this island"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Fenris Isle right now?",a="The island is occupied by the Rot Hide gnolls under the command of Thule Ravenclaw, a rogue necromancer aligned with the Scourge who directs them from Fenris Keep.",al={"who runs fenris isle","fenris isle bosses","who lives on fenris isle"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to the humans who used to live here?",a="During the Third War, the human defenders and inhabitants of Fenris Keep were either murdered or driven away as the Scourge overran Lordaeron. The fortress was left ruined until gnolls and necromancers claimed the empty ramparts.",al={"what happened to fenris keep humans","who built fenris keep"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in attacking the island?",a="The Forsaken consider the entrenched Scourge forces and Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle an active security threat to their holdings in Silverpine Forest. The Horde launches incursions across Lordamere Lake to eliminate Thule Ravenclaw and dismantle his operations.",al={"assault on fenris isle lore","why do horde attack fenris isle","forsaken fenris isle"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Fenris Keep in ruins?",a="Fenris Keep once served as a thriving military stronghold for the kingdom of Lordaeron. When the Scourge swept across the northern realms during the Third War, the fortress fell. Its defenders and inhabitants were slaughtered or driven into flight, leaving the outpost abandoned to decay until Thule Ravenclaw and his gnolls claimed the wreckage.",al={"why is fenris isle abandoned","fenris keep ruined","what ruined fenris keep"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Fenris Isle dangerous?",a="Fenris Isle is extremely perilous. The island is thoroughly infested by the Rot Hide gnolls and ruled by the rogue wizard Thule Ravenclaw. Surrounded by the murky waters of Lordamere Lake, any explorer who crosses to the island faces aggressive, diseased beasts and dark spellcasting within the dilapidated keep.",al={"is fenris isle safe","fenris isle dangers","threats on fenris isle"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Fenris Isle represents an intolerable Scourge bastion in their own backyard, requiring relentless strikes to keep Thule Ravenclaw's rot-hides from overrunning Silverpine's eastern waters.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers are enlisted by Forsaken commanders to board boats across Lordamere Lake, storm the island's defenses, and assassinate the renegade necromancer orchestrating attacks from Fenris Keep."},kw={"fenris isle","fenris keep","lordamere lake","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"subzone:fenris-keep","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:silverpine","quest:442","quest:446","quest:439","subzone:decrepit-ferry","topic:scourge"},src={"Fenris Isle"}}
E["subzone:fenris-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Fenris Keep",z="silverpine",s="Fenris Keep is an isolated stone fortress situated atop Fenris Isle in the heart of Lordamere Lake. Once a strategic stronghold housing Lordaeron troops, it has fallen into the hands of the Scourge under the rogue mage Thule Ravenclaw.",h="Fenris Keep is an isolated stone fortress situated atop Fenris Isle in the heart of Lordamere Lake.",sec={{t="A Fallen Bastion of Lordaeron",b="Before the Third War, Fenris Keep held strategic importance for the Kingdom of Lordaeron, stationing a sizable contingent of troops to safeguard Lordamere Lake. When the undead Scourge swept across the land, the island fortress was overwhelmed along with the rest of the realm. Rather than crumbling into forgotten ruin, it was seized by Thule Ravenclaw, a traitorous former wizard of the Kirin Tor. Ravenclaw allied himself with the Scourge, subjugated the resident gnolls with foul necromancy to create the ravenous Rot Hide pack, and entrenched himself deep inside the keep's stone halls.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge on Lordamere",b="Today, Fenris Keep serves as the seat of Ravenclaw's power and an imminent threat to the Forsaken securing Silverpine Forest. From this bastion, Thule directs legions of Rot Hide gnolls that violently assail anyone daring to set foot on the isle. Because Fenris Isle sits mere miles across the water from the Tirisfal border, the Forsaken of the Sepulcher and Undercity actively dispatch champions to batter down the keep's defenses and put an end to the rogue necromancer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Fenris Keep?",a="Fenris Keep is a fortified stone castle situated on Fenris Isle in Lordamere Lake. Formerly a military stronghold for the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron, it is currently held by the undead Scourge.",al={"fenris keep lore","what is fenris keep","fenris castle"},it="place"},{q="Who rules Fenris Keep right now?",a="The keep is ruled by Thule Ravenclaw, a former Kirin Tor mage who betrayed the living to serve the Scourge. He commands an army of undead-tainted Rot Hide gnolls from within the fortress.",al={"who controls fenris keep","fenris keep boss","master of fenris isle"},it="residents"},{q="Why are there gnolls inside Fenris Keep?",a="The local gnoll population was subjugated by Thule Ravenclaw through dark magic and disease, twisting them into the Rot Hide gnolls. They serve as Ravenclaw's loyal shock troops and guards throughout the castle and the surrounding island.",al={"rot hide gnolls fenris","why gnolls in keep","fenris gnolls"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about Fenris Keep?",a="Fenris Keep provides the Scourge with a defensible base on Lordamere Lake, directly menacing Forsaken movements through eastern Silverpine Forest and Tirisfal Glades. Sylvanas's forces cannot leave an active Scourge commander unchecked so close to their borders.",al={"why forsaken attack fenris","forsaken fenris keep","undercity fenris"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to Fenris Keep?",a="Fenris Keep once held immense strategic value, housing a sizable garrison of the Kingdom of Lordaeron's military amidst the waters of Lordamere Lake. When the Third War swept the land, the Scourge overran the fortress. Rather than being cleansed, it fell into the hands of Thule Ravenclaw, a renegade Kirin Tor mage who allied with the Lich King and transformed the local gnoll tribes into ravenous undead minions.",al={"fenris keep history","what happened at fenris keep","fenris keep lore"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is Fenris Keep ruined?",a="Fenris Keep fell to ruin when the Scourge decimated Lordaeron's defenses during the Third War. The military garrison that once maintained the fortress was slaughtered, leaving the structures untended and rotting. Today, it stands as a decaying stronghold dominated by necromantic magic and feral, flesh-eating gnolls.",al={"why is fenris keep abandoned","who destroyed fenris keep","fenris keep ruins"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Fenris Keep dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The fortress and surrounding island crawl with the Rot Hide gnolls, who hungrily attack anyone setting foot on their shores. Within the keep itself resides Thule Ravenclaw, a dangerous necromancer wielding dark magic over his monstrous servants.",al={"fenris keep danger","is fenris keep safe","how dangerous is fenris keep"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde—and the Forsaken in particular—Fenris Keep represents a lingering Scourge stronghold that must be eradicated to safeguard Silverpine Forest and the waterways of Lordamere Lake.",["class:Mage"]="The master of Fenris Keep, Thule Ravenclaw, represents a grim betrayal of the Kirin Tor's teachings, having twisted Dalaran's arcane knowledge into the dark arts of the Scourge."},kw={"fenris isle","fenris keep","lordaeron","lordamere lake","rot hide","scourge","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"subzone:fenris-isle","quest:446","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken","topic:gnoll","quest:366"},src={"Fenris Keep"}}
E["subzone:forsaken-rear-guard"] = {t="subzone",n="Forsaken Rear Guard",z="silverpine",s="In the current era of Silverpine Forest, the bleak land north of the Sepulcher is known as the Dead Field. No fortified camp stands here; travelers find only the blighted, haunted earth of Lordaeron's fallen days.",h="In the current era of Silverpine Forest, the bleak land north of the Sepulcher is known as the Dead Field.",sec={{t="A Contested Expanse",b="With no barracks or garrison of its own, this expanse north of the Sepulcher remains part of the Dead Field. The Forsaken maintain patrols along the road, but the ground itself is withered, haunted by remnants of the Third War and encroaching feral beasts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Forsaken Rear Guard?",a="No fortified Forsaken position stands here in Year 25. The land north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest is the blighted expanse known as the Dead Field.",al={"forsaken rear guard lore","rear guard silverpine","who is at the rear guard"},it="place"},{q="Where is this area located in Silverpine Forest?",a="It lies along the main road north of the Sepulcher, in northern Silverpine Forest where Forsaken scouts monitor wild predators and hostile forces.",al={"rear guard location","where is dead field","silverpine rear guard spot"},gp=true},{q="Why was this land called the Dead Field?",a="Like much of Silverpine Forest, the soil and vegetation withered during the Third War under the Scourge's corrupting plague, leaving behind lifeless fields populated by feral scavengers and wandering horrors.",al={"dead field history","why dead field","dead field name meaning"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, keeping the northern roads past the Sepulcher clear is crucial to maintaining supply lines and holding territory against hostile forces in northern Silverpine.",["faction:Horde"]="The central paths of Silverpine Forest are treacherous, and Horde travelers moving south toward the Greymane Wall must stay alert amid the blighted wilderness."},kw={"dead field","forsaken","forsaken rear guard","silverpine","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"subzone:dead-field","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","topic:forsaken","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Forsaken Rear Guard"}}
E["subzone:greymane-wall"] = {t="subzone",n="Greymane Wall",z="silverpine",s="The Greymane Wall is a massive stone bulwark spanning the southern frontier of Silverpine Forest. Built by King Genn Greymane after the Second War, it seals the kingdom of Gilneas away from the outside world behind impenetrable, locked gates.",h="The Greymane Wall is a massive stone bulwark spanning the southern frontier of Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Monument to Isolation",b="Following the Second War, King Genn Greymane grew resentful of the Alliance of Lordaeron, particularly the taxes required to maintain the orc internment camps and build Nethergarde Keep. Deciding Gilneas had given enough of its coin and blood for foreign troubles, Greymane withdrew from the Alliance and ordered a colossal barrier raised across the head of the peninsula. In doing so, he abandoned lands belonging to Lord Darius Crowley—including Pyrewood Village and Ambermill—leaving them stranded on the northern side of the stones. When the Third War brought the Plague of Undeath and countless desperate refugees to its foot, the gates remained pitilessly barred.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Seclusion",b="While the rampart successfully kept the armies of the Scourge from overrunning the peninsula, safety brought a dark price. Gilnean forces briefly opened the gates during the war to fight the undead, only to be overwhelmed. In desperation, King Greymane ordered Archmage Arugal to summon the feral worgen. Though the beasts drove back the Scourge, they turned on their summoners. Greymane's soldiers retreated and sealed the gates shut once more, but infected fighters carried the beastly contagion back inside. Behind the cold, silent wall, internal rebellion and a creeping curse now tear the isolated kingdom apart.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What lies beyond the Greymane Wall?",a="Behind the wall lies the peninsula kingdom of Gilneas. Ruled by King Genn Greymane, it completely isolated itself from Lordaeron and the rest of the world before the Third War, barring all commerce and communication.",al={"what is behind the wall","where does greymane wall lead","what kingdom is behind the wall"},it="place"},{q="Can you open the gates of the Greymane Wall?",a="No. The massive portcullis and iron-banded doors are firmly barred from the southern side. Gilneas has severed all contact with the outside world, and nothing enters or leaves.",al={"how to get past greymane wall","can you open greymane wall","open the gate"},gp=true},{q="Why was the wall built here instead of farther south?",a="The wall utilized the surrounding mountainous terrain as a natural barrier. Building along this ridge forced the kingdom to abandon the northern holdings of Lord Darius Crowley—including Pyrewood Village and Ambermill—sowing bitter domestic dissent within Gilneas.",al={"why did they build it here","why cut off pyrewood","crowley lands cut off"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to the refugees who fled here during the Third War?",a="When the Scourge ravaged Lordaeron, masses of fleeing human refugees gathered outside the wall begging for entry. King Greymane refused to unseal the gates to protect his kingdom, and the desperate refugees were eventually slaughtered by the undead outside.",al={"scourge refugees wall","refugees outside greymane wall"},it="history"},{q="What is the Greymane Wall?",a="The Greymane Wall is a colossal stone bulwark spanning the southern frontier of Silverpine Forest. Commissioned by King Genn Greymane after the Second War, it seals the kingdom of Gilneas away from Lordaeron and the rest of the world behind massive, impenetrable gates.",al={"what is greymane wall","greymane wall","giant wall in silverpine"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Greymane Wall?",a="It is named after King Genn Greymane, the ruler of Gilneas who ordered its construction. Chafing at high taxes to support the Alliance's orc internment camps and weary of foreign wars, Greymane erected the colossal barrier to isolate his nation completely.",al={"why is it called greymane wall","who named greymane wall","greymane name origin"},it="name",add=true},{q="Who controls the Greymane Wall?",a="The wall belongs entirely to the isolationist kingdom of Gilneas, ruled by King Genn Greymane. While Gilnean sentries keep watch from the safe side of the great ramparts, the outside perimeter is utterly abandoned to the wilderness and whatever shadows wander Silverpine.",al={"who controls greymane wall","who guards the wall","who lives at greymane wall"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Greymane Wall dangerous?",a="The wall itself is an impassable stone barrier, but the lands outside its gate are perilous. Silverpine Forest is overrun with feral worgen, vengeful spirits, and hostile beasts that prey upon any traveler who lingers too close to the silent, barred entrance.",al={"is greymane wall safe","is it dangerous near the wall","threats at greymane wall"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Greymane Wall stands as a bitter reminder of Gilnean abandonment. When Lordaeron fell to the Scourge, Greymane turned a deaf ear to his former allies, leaving them to rot outside his gates.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken who now claim Silverpine Forest, the wall forms an impassable southern border, sealing away a human kingdom whose intentions and inner strength remain entirely unknown."},kw={"arugal","darius crowley","genn greymane","gilneas","greymane wall","pyrewood","silverpine"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:ambermill","topic:worgen","npc:arugal","npc:darius-crowley","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:scourge"},src={"Greymane Wall"}}
E["subzone:ivar-patch"] = {t="subzone",n="Ivar Patch",z="silverpine",s="The Ivar Patch is a blighted pumpkin farm located in northern Silverpine Forest. Once a thriving agricultural homestead of Lordaeron, its residents were wiped out during the Third War and transformed into ravenous, mindlessly hostile ghouls.",h="The Ivar Patch is a blighted pumpkin farm located in northern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Ruined Harvest",b="Before the Third War swept through Lordaeron, this pumpkin patch was a prosperous homestead owned by a farmer named Ivar, who employed a lively crew of farmhands and servants. When the Scourge unleashed the Plague of Undeath across the countryside, the farm was consumed completely. Rather than rising with their minds intact like the free-willed Forsaken, Ivar, his family, and his laborers were reduced to rotting, feral ghouls bound to prowl the ruined soil.",sp=0},{t="The Deathstalker Ambush",b="When the Forsaken began securing northern Silverpine, three Deathstalkers—Rane Yorick, Quinn Yorick, and Erland McKree—scouted the region to evaluate local threats. Passing through the Dead Field, the patrol was ambushed by the feral pack at the patch. Quinn was badly mauled by Ivar himself, now known as Ivar the Foul. With Quinn gravely wounded, the Yoricks fortified themselves inside the farm's old ruined house while McKree pressed on alone toward Malden's Orchard.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the farm and its owner?",a="The farm was struck down by the Plague of Undeath during the Third War. Farmer Ivar, his family, and his workers all succumbed, rising again as feral, rotting ghouls under the lingering sway of the Scourge.",al={"ivar patch history","who was ivar","what happened to ivar"},it="history"},{q="Why are there Deathstalkers hiding inside the house?",a="Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick were part of a scouting reconnaissance squad dispatched to gauge regional threats in Silverpine Forest. While passing through, they were ambushed by the ghouls, and Quinn was severely injured by Ivar the Foul, forcing them to take refuge inside the dilapidated farmhouse.",al={"deathstalkers at ivar patch","why are forsaken here","quinn yorick farmhouse"},it="people"},{q="Are the ghouls here part of the Forsaken?",a="No. The ghouls roaming the pumpkin fields are mindless Scourge remnants created by the Plague of Undeath. They lack free will and will attack any living travelers or Forsaken on sight.",al={"are these ghouls forsaken","scourge in ivar patch","why are ghouls hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="Where is the Ivar Patch located?",a="The Ivar Patch lies in northern Silverpine Forest, north of the Dead Field and just south of the road leading toward Malden's Orchard.",al={"ivar patch location","where is ivar patch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Ivar Patch?",a="The Ivar Patch was once a prosperous pumpkin farm in northern Silverpine Forest, filled with busy fields, farmhands, and servants. Today, it lies ruined and overgrown, its fertile soil spoiled by the Third War and overrun by feral undead.",al={"what is ivar patch","ivar patch lore","ivar farm"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Ivar Patch?",a="The land takes its name from its former owner, Ivar. He once managed the estate and employed numerous servants to tend the pumpkins, but during the Third War he fell to the plague, rising as the foul ghoul who now haunts the grounds.",al={"who was ivar","why called ivar patch","ivar name origin"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the Ivar Patch dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Mindless, ravenous ghouls wander the blighted pumpkins, attacking any living or undead travelers who trespass. Even trained Forsaken scouts like the Deathstalkers were ambushed and badly wounded trying to pass through.",al={"ivar patch danger","is ivar patch safe","threats at ivar patch"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The ruined farm stands as a bitter reminder of the Plague of Undeath that tore Lordaeron apart, showing the horrifying mindless fate the Forsaken narrowly escaped.",["faction:Horde"]="Culling the ravenous ghouls at the patch is vital to securing the northern roadway between Silverpine Forest and the safety of Undercity."},kw={"deathstalkers","ghouls","ivar patch","ivar the foul","pumpkin patch","quinn yorick","rane yorick","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:425","quest:1886","npc:quinn-yorick","zone:silverpine","subzone:dead-field","subzone:malden-s-orchard","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge"},src={"Ivar Patch"}}
E["subzone:malden-s-orchard"] = {t="subzone",n="Malden's Orchard",z="silverpine",s="Malden's Orchard is a ruined farmstead in northern Silverpine Forest, named after the human owner who fled during the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. Long abandoned, its dark evergreen trees sit overgrown while vicious black worgs stalk the grounds. The orchard's crumbling cottage served as a temporary refuge for a stranded Forsaken scout cut off from his unit.",h="Malden's Orchard is a ruined farmstead in northern Silverpine Forest, named after the human owner who fled...",sec={{t="A Blighted Harvest",b="Before the Third War, this homestead supplied fresh fruit to the towns of Lordaeron, tended by a farmer named Malden. When the Scourge tore through the kingdom, Malden abandoned his land to flee the plague. In the years since, the orchard has choked under the dark, encroaching mists of Silverpine Forest. The evergreen trees remain unpruned and their fruit rots ungathered on blighted boughs, leaving the plot entirely reclaimed by wild predators.",sp=0},{t="Trapped in the Cottage",b="The overgrown orchard has become a hunting ground for territorial black worgs, making it a hazardous route through northern Silverpine. During a reconnaissance mission for the Deathstalkers, the scout Erland McKree was dispatched to survey the area but found himself overwhelmed by the beasts. Pinned inside Malden's dilapidated cottage for days, Erland survived only until Forsaken reinforcements could break through the pack and escort him back to his fellow scouts at the Ivar Patch.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Malden?",a="Malden was a human farmer who lived here before the fall of Lordaeron. He abandoned the orchard and fled for his life when the Scourge invaded the realm during the Third War.",al={"malden lore","who owned the orchard","who is malden"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the orchard full of worgs?",a="With no living tenders to defend the farmstead, wild black worgs prowling Silverpine Forest claimed the dense grove and abandoned yard as their pack territory.",al={"why are there worgs here","malden orchard dogs","worg infestation"},it="threat"},{q="Who is trapped inside the cottage?",a="Deathstalker Erland McKree was trapped inside the cottage. Sent on a reconnaissance mission by the Forsaken, he was ambushed by the orchard's worgs and holed up inside until aid arrived.",al={"cottage scout","who is in the house","deathstalker in the cabin"},it="people"},{q="Does anyone harvest fruit from this orchard now?",a="No. The dark trees have not been tended in years, and their fruit rots on the branches amidst the decay spreading through Silverpine Forest.",al={"is the fruit edible","malden's orchard harvest","can you pick fruit"},it="today"},{q="What is Malden's Orchard?",a="Malden's Orchard is an overgrown fruit grove and homestead nestled in northern Silverpine Forest. Once a quiet farmstead tended by living human hands, its dark, evergreen trees now stand neglected, their unpicked fruit left to rot amid the gloom of the woods.",al={"what is maldens orchard","maldens orchard silverpine","about maldens orchard"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to Malden's Orchard?",a="When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, its original owner was forced to abandon the cottage and flee for his life. The farmstead fell into silent disrepair until vicious black worgs overran the grove, turning the once-peaceful orchard into a savage den.",al={"history of maldens orchard","maldens orchard lore","what happened here maldens orchard"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why was Malden's Orchard abandoned?",a="The farm was abandoned during the Third War when the Plague of Undeath and the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, forcing its master to flee. Left without caretakers, the wilderness reclaimed the land and hungry predators moved in to claim the grounds.",al={"why is maldens orchard ruined","why was it abandoned maldens orchard","who ruined maldens orchard"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Malden's Orchard dangerous?",a="Yes. A dense pack of ravenous black worgs has completely overrun the orchard. Their presence is lethal enough that even a trained Forsaken Deathstalker was pinned down inside the lone cottage for days, unable to step outside without facing certain death.",al={"maldens orchard danger","is it safe at maldens orchard","threats at maldens orchard"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Malden's Orchard?",a="The orchard is named after its former human owner, Malden, who tended the trees and lived in the small homestead here before the Scourge tore through the kingdom.",al={"why is it called maldens orchard","maldens orchard name origin","who named maldens orchard"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the orchard is a reminder of human ruin and a contested piece of northern Silverpine that Deathstalker scouts must secure against feral beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="Travelers moving south from the Sepulcher or the Tirisfal border must tread carefully around the orchard due to the aggressive worg packs nesting on the farm."},kw={"cottage","erland mckree","ivar patch","malden","malden's orchard","maldens orchard","silverpine","worgs"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:ivar-patch","npc:quinn-yorick","quest:1886","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Malden's Orchard"}}
E["subzone:north-tide-s-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="North Tide's Hollow",z="silverpine",s="North Tide's Hollow is a rugged wilderness pocket in Silverpine Forest located just north of the Sepulcher. Haunted by feral Moonrage worgen loyal to the rogue Archmage Arugal, the clearing serves as a base of operations for the beasts stalking the coastal woods.",h="North Tide's Hollow is a rugged wilderness pocket in Silverpine Forest located just north of the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Feral Foothold",b="Tucked away in the dense timber north of the Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher, North Tide's Hollow is dominated by the savage Moonrage pack. These feral worgen, brought into Lordaeron through the reckless sorcery of Archmage Arugal, have established crude encampments throughout the hollow. Built with only the barest necessities required by the hardy beasts, these rough shelters provide a forward staging ground dangerously close to Forsaken travel routes.",sp=0},{t="Under Shadowfang's Shadow",b="Unlike ordinary wilderness predators, the worgen of North Tide's Hollow answer to the sinister will emanating from Shadowfang Keep. Their proximity to both the western shoreline and the main road through Silverpine makes them a constant menace to Forsaken couriers and patrols attempting to secure the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is North Tide's Hollow?",a="North Tide's Hollow is located in western Silverpine Forest, situated just to the north of the Forsaken outpost known as the Sepulcher, near the coastal bluffs.",al={"north tides hollow location","where is north tides hollow","hollow location"},gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit North Tide's Hollow?",a="The hollow is infested with Moonrage worgen, supernatural wolf-beasts bound to the madness of Archmage Arugal.",al={"who lives here","north tides hollow enemies","mobs in north tides hollow"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the worgen live in crude camps here?",a="While worgen are vicious and wild, the Moonrage pack retains enough cunning to organize basic encampments. Being naturally resilient and hardened, they require only the most primitive shelters and survival necessities to endure the Lordaeron wilderness.",al={"worgen camps","why do worgen have tents"}},{q="Who controls the worgen in this area?",a="The worgen throughout Silverpine Forest, including those in North Tide's Hollow, are the servants and creations of the mad Archmage Arugal, who directs them from his lair in Shadowfang Keep.",al={"who leads the worgen","worgen master"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is North Tide's Hollow?",a="North Tide's Hollow is a rugged wilderness hollow located in Silverpine Forest, situated just north of the Sepulcher. It is known primarily as a wild encampment and haunting ground for the ferocious Moonrage worgen that roam the pine woods under the influence of Archmage Arugal.",al={"what is north tides hollow","north tide hollow info","tell me about north tides hollow"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is North Tide's Hollow dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely dangerous for lone travelers. The hollow is overrun by savage Moonrage worgen who attack any interlopers on sight. These feral beasts have established crude camps throughout the area, making the hollow a perilous threshold for anyone journeying north of the Sepulcher.",al={"is north tides hollow safe","how dangerous is north tides hollow","north tide hollow threats"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Positioned uncomfortably close to the Sepulcher, the Moonrage pack in North Tide's Hollow poses an immediate threat to Forsaken sovereignty and logistical lines in Silverpine."},kw={"arugal","beachhead","moonrage","north tide's hollow","sepulcher","silverpine forest","worgen"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","topic:worgen","npc:arugal"},src={"North Tide's Hollow"}}
E["subzone:north-tide-s-run"] = {t="subzone",n="North Tide's Run",z="silverpine",s="North Tide's Run is the windswept northwestern shoreline of Silverpine Forest, skirting the edge of the Great Sea. Marked by a lonely campfire and a half-sunken shipwreck, this stretch of sand is known as a secluded trial ground for traveling druids seeking harmony with the waters.",h="North Tide's Run is the windswept northwestern shoreline of Silverpine Forest, skirting the edge of the Great...",sec={{t="A Lonely Coastal Outpost",b="Stretching along the northwest edge of Silverpine Forest, North Tide's Run consists of cold sand, pounding surf, and a strip of the Great Sea. Its most unmistakable landmark is a partially submerged shipwreck tilted precariously in the shallows near the beach. Aside from the wreckage, the only sign of habitation is a humble campfire tended by Wallace the Blind, who keeps a quiet vigil beside the lapping tide.",sp=0},{t="Waters of the Sea Lion",b="Despite its bleak atmosphere, North Tide's Run holds sacred importance for Horde initiates walking the path of Cenarius. Young tauren druids are directed here on pilgrimage to recover underwater relics lost to the waves, testing their lung capacity and endurance to earn the blessing of the aquatic form.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is North Tide's Run?",a="It is the northwestern shoreline and coastal shelf of Silverpine Forest, bordered by the Great Sea. It is characterized by its sunken ship, tidal waters, and bleak, quiet strand.",al={"north tides run","where is north tides run","what is this beach"},it="place"},{q="Who is Wallace the Blind?",a="Wallace the Blind is a hermit who has pitched a small camp and fire right at the water's edge along the beach, sitting quietly near the sunken vessel.",al={"wallace blind","wallace the blind silverpine","who is the guy at the fire"},it="residents"},{q="Why do druids come to North Tide's Run?",a="Tauren druids travel here on pilgrimage during their trials to commune with the spirits of the sea. By braving the depths near the shoreline to recover lost pendant fragments, they earn the power to assume aquatic form.",al={"druid quest silverpine beach","aquatic form silverpine","why tauren here"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the sunken ship in the water?",a="The wreck is a partially submerged vessel resting in the shallows just off the sand. Its presence serves as a navigational landmark for travelers combing the coast.",al={"shipwreck north tides run","sunken boat silverpine beach","ship wreck"},it="history"},{q="Is North Tide's Run dangerous?",a="North Tide's Run is relatively quiet compared to the haunted heartlands of Silverpine, but it is far from harmless. The cold waters of the Great Sea conceal hidden depths and dangerous marine life, while wandering beasts roam the desolate shoreline. Beyond the wandering hermit Wallace the Blind, you will find no friendly shelter here, leaving travelers largely exposed to the perils of the northern coast.",al={"is north tides run safe","north tides run danger","threats north tides run"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids, this cold coast represents a vital rite of passage, housing the submerged trial components necessary to master the sea lion form.",["race:Tauren"]="Far from the warm plains of Mulgore, North Tide's Run is one of the few places in Lordaeron that young tauren travel to early in their spiritual journeys."},kw={"aquatic form","druid trial","great sea","north tide's run","shipwreck","silverpine forest","wallace the blind"},rel={"zone:silverpine","quest:31","topic:druid","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"North Tide's Run"}}
E["subzone:olsen-s-farthing"] = {t="subzone",n="Olsen's Farthing",z="silverpine",s="Olsen's Farthing was once a flourishing farmstead situated along the primary trade road running through Silverpine Forest. In the wake of the Third War, the fields fell into ruin and became overrun by reanimated thralls bound to the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw.",h="Olsen's Farthing was once a flourishing farmstead situated along the primary trade road running through...",sec={{t="A Blighted Homestead",b="Before the plague consumed Lordaeron, Olsen's Farthing was a busy agricultural homestead with direct access to Silverpine's main overland trading route. Today, its tilled fields are choked with weeds, its structures lie broken, and any memory of honest farming has been erased by Scourge necromancy. Undead thralls, bound as slaves and raiders under the command of Thule Ravenclaw, wander the barren grounds to slaughter any travelers who stray too close.",sp=0},{t="The Grasp of Ravenclaw",b="The shambling horrors haunting Olsen's Farthing are not mindless wanderers, but servants answering to Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful necromancer operating from Fenris Isle in the center of Lake Lordamere. Using dark sorcery to animate and enslave the dead of the surrounding countryside, Thule's reach extends through Olsen's Farthing and poses a direct threat to the Forsaken seeking to secure the northern reaches of Silverpine Forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Olsen's Farthing before the Third War?",a="It was a productive roadside farmstead supporting local commerce along Silverpine Forest's main trade thoroughfare, feeding the settlements of Lordaeron before the kingdom fell to the Scourge.",al={"olsens farthing history","what was this place","who lived at olsens farthing"},it="history"},{q="Why is the farm infested with undead?",a="The farm was destroyed during the Third War and its remnants were seized by the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, who raised the dead as thralls and raiders to terrorize travelers along the road.",al={"why are there undead here","who controls the undead at olsens farthing","ravenclaw slaves silverpine"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a dangerous necromancer aligned with the Scourge who orchestrates undead incursions across Silverpine Forest from his stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"who is thule ravenclaw","thule ravenclaw lore","who commands ravenclaw raiders"}},{q="Does the Horde or Forsaken hold any presence here?",a="No. The farm is completely overrun by hostile undead loyal to Thule Ravenclaw, making it hostile ground for Forsaken scouts and Horde travelers alike.",al={"is olsens farthing horde","do forsaken live at olsens farthing","is there a quest hub here"},it="today"},{q="What is Olsen's Farthing?",a="Olsen's Farthing is a ruined farmstead situated along the trade road running through Silverpine Forest. Once a thriving piece of rural farmland, it has fallen into decay and ruin following the devastation of the Third War.",al={"what is olsens farthing","olsens farthing silverpine","olsen farmstead"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who lives at Olsen's Farthing?",a="No living farmers remain. Instead, the grounds are inhabited and overrun by the Ravenclaw undead—slaves and raiders serving the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, who commands them from nearby Fenris Isle.",al={"who controls olsens farthing","who is at olsen farthing","olsens farthing inhabitants"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Olsen's Farthing dangerous?",a="Yes. The farmstead poses a severe hazard to any travelers along the road. The undead bound to Thule Ravenclaw ravenously assault anyone who steps into the ruined fields and crumbling farm buildings.",al={"is olsens farthing safe","olsens farthing danger","threats at olsens farthing"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, places like Olsen's Farthing are grim reminders of the lingering Scourge threat that seeks to enslave the dead rather than liberate them.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the raiders from Olsen's Farthing is vital for securing the supply road linking the Sepulcher to the north and the road toward Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"fenris isle","lordaeron farm","olsen's farthing","olsens farthing","ravenclaw raiders","ravenclaw slaves","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:446","zone:silverpine","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Olsen's Farthing"}}
E["subzone:pyrewood-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Pyrewood Village",z="silverpine",s="Pyrewood Village is an isolated human settlement nestled in southern Silverpine Forest beneath Shadowfang Keep. Originally part of Gilneas before being stranded outside the Greymane Wall, its living residents harbor a horrific secret brought upon them by the mad archmage Arugal.",h="Pyrewood Village is an isolated human settlement nestled in southern Silverpine Forest beneath Shadowfang...",sec={{t="A Town Severed",b="Pyrewood was once a prosperous Gilnean settlement owned by Lord Darius Crowley. When King Genn Greymane chose to isolate his kingdom behind the massive Greymane Wall following the Second War, Pyrewood and its neighbor Ambermill were abandoned on the northern side. Cut off from their homeland, the townsfolk were left entirely defenseless during the Third War as the Scourge marched across Lordaeron. Though they managed to survive the initial wave of the undead, their true nightmare began when the mage Arugal took refuge in the fortress above.",sp=0},{t="The Moonrage Curse",b="From the towers of Shadowfang Keep, Archmage Arugal unleashed otherworldly beasts upon the surrounding lands, ultimately cursing the living population of Pyrewood. By the light of day, the citizens appear as normal human villagers, quietly maintaining their town hall, blacksmith, and chapel, even offering trade to visiting Alliance travelers. Yet as soon as the sun dips beneath the horizon, a terrible transformation occurs: every resident shifts into a savage, bloodthirsty worgen of the Moonrage pack, turning on anyone unfortunate enough to linger within the walls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Pyrewood Village attack me at night?",a="The villagers are afflicted by a dark curse cast by Archmage Arugal of Shadowfang Keep. During the day, they retain their human forms and normal faculties, but each night they transform into ravenous Moonrage worgen who attack all outsiders on sight.",al={"pyrewood hostile at night","pyrewood worgen shift","why are they worgen"},it="danger"},{q="Why is Pyrewood outside the Greymane Wall?",a="King Genn Greymane ordered the Greymane Wall constructed to seal Gilneas off from the outside world following the Second War. Lord Darius Crowley strongly opposed the wall because it cut off his northern holdings, including Pyrewood and Ambermill, leaving their residents to fend for themselves.",al={"why outside the wall","is pyrewood gilnean","darius crowley pyrewood"},it="origin"},{q="Can Alliance players visit Pyrewood safely?",a="Yes, but strictly during daylight hours. Alliance travelers can walk among the townsfolk and trade with the village merchants while the sun is up. Once darkness falls, however, the entire village transforms into hostile worgen regardless of your faction.",al={"alliance pyrewood friendly","can alliance go to pyrewood","pyrewood vendors"},it="ties"},{q="How does the Horde view Pyrewood?",a="The Forsaken view the village as an intolerable threat on their southern border. Under the direction of agents like Deathstalker Faerleia, the Horde seeks to assassinate the village's council and sever Pyrewood's ties to Arugal.",al={"forsaken pyrewood","horde hostile pyrewood","deathstalker faerleia pyrewood"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood Village is a human settlement nestled in southern Silverpine Forest, situated just outside the Greymane Wall and beneath Shadowfang Keep. Originally part of Gilneas under Lord Darius Crowley, it was cut off from its homeland when King Greymane sealed the borders. The village miraculously survived the Scourge during the Third War, maintaining its town hall, chapel, and blacksmith. By day, its hardy human inhabitants carry on their daily lives and welcome friendly Alliance travelers, even as dark magic looms over them from the keep above.",al={"what is pyrewood","pyrewood village lore","pyrewood info"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood was stranded when King Genn Greymane built his massive wall, abandoning Lord Darius Crowley's lands to the wider world. During the Third War, the village endured the onslaught of the Scourge, standing as one of the few surviving human enclaves in Lordaeron. However, true tragedy struck when Archmage Arugal unleashed his summoned worgen upon Baron Silverlaine's nearby keep. After claiming the stronghold, Arugal placed a terrible curse upon Pyrewood's surviving villagers, binding their fates to his mad experiments.",al={"history of pyrewood","what happened at pyrewood","pyrewood history"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood is inhabited by its surviving Gilnean townsfolk and governed by a local ruling council. Though Lord Darius Crowley was historically their lord before the Wall closed, the villagers now govern themselves under desperate circumstances. Tragically, their true master is Archmage Arugal, who watches from Shadowfang Keep. By day, craftsmen, guards, and councilors run the town in human guise, but come nightfall, they all succumb to the worgen curse.",al={"who leads pyrewood","pyrewood residents","who controls pyrewood village"},it="residents",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The village represents a tragic remnant of living humanity in Lordaeron, willing to trade with travelers by day before succumbing to a horrific curse each night.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken, Pyrewood is a lingering pocket of hostile humans and monstrous worgen serving Archmage Arugal right on the border of their lands."},kw={"arugal","crowley","greymane wall","moonrage","pyrewood","pyrewood village","shadowfang","silverpine"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:greymane-wall","subzone:ambermill","topic:worgen","quest:452","npc:deathstalker-faerleia"},src={"Pyrewood Village"}}
E["subzone:sepulcher"] = {t="subzone",n="Sepulcher",z="silverpine",s="The Sepulcher is the primary Forsaken settlement and stronghold in Silverpine Forest. Once an ordinary Lordaeron graveyard and burial crypt overlooking the western coast, it now serves as a fortified sanctuary for the Horde against surrounding regional threats.",h="The Sepulcher is the primary Forsaken settlement and stronghold in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Sanctum in the Fog",b="Perched in the hills above the Lordaeron coastline, the Sepulcher was originally a quiet cemetery and crypt alongside the western road. In the wake of the Third War, the newly emancipated Forsaken repurposed the ancient stone vault and its grounds into an essential outpost. Surrounded by hostile forces on all sides—the feral worgen to the south, wandering Scourge remnants to the east, and Kirin Tor wizards watching from Ambermill—the Sepulcher provides a rare haven of safety, supplies, and command for travelers marching through Silverpine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Sepulcher before the Forsaken moved in?",a="Before the Third War and the fall of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, it was simply a roadside cemetery and stone crypt where local villagers buried their dead.",al={"sepulcher history","what was the sepulcher","who built the sepulcher"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Sepulcher so vital to the Forsaken?",a="It serves as the Forsaken's sole fortified hub in Silverpine Forest. From this central position, Forsaken scouts and commanders can monitor encroaching Dalaran mages, Scourge holdouts, and the spreading beastly worgen menace lurking near Shadowfang Keep.",al={"why is sepulcher important","forsaken in silverpine","role of the sepulcher"},it="purpose"},{q="Are travelers belonging to other Horde races welcome here?",a="Yes. While the base is managed and inhabited entirely by Forsaken deathguards, merchants, and apothecaries, it functions as an official Horde refuge offering respite and trade to orcs, trolls, and tauren passing through the region.",al={"can orcs go to sepulcher","is the sepulcher horde friendly","horde at sepulcher"},it="residents"},{q="What threats surround the Sepulcher?",a="The settlement is hemmed in by hostile powers: Scourge forces roam to the east, the Kirin Tor holds Ambermill to the southeast, and ferocious worgen stalk the woods to the south.",al={"threats to sepulcher","enemies in silverpine","what attacks sepulcher"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Sepulcher?",a="The Sepulcher is the primary Forsaken settlement and stronghold in Silverpine Forest. Nestled in the hills overlooking the western Lordaeronian coastline, it serves as the operational hub for Horde efforts throughout the region, offering a safe harbor complete with scouts, merchants, and trainers.",al={"what is sepulcher","sepulcher silverpine","what is the sepulcher"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Sepulcher?",a="Before the Forsaken fortified it as an outpost, the site was simply a graveyard and crypt alongside the Silverpine road. A sepulcher is a tomb or burial vault, and the Forsaken kept the fitting name when they converted the ancient crypt into their military base.",al={"why is it called sepulcher","sepulcher name meaning","why called sepulcher"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the Sepulcher dangerous?",a="Within its perimeter, the Sepulcher is a secure haven guarded by Forsaken sentries. Outside its boundaries, however, the area is perilous. Hostile worgen prowl to the south, Scourge lurk to the east, and Kirin Tor agents watch from the southeast, making the outpost an isolated refuge in hostile territory.",al={"is the sepulcher safe","danger sepulcher","is sepulcher safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Sepulcher is the staging ground for the Forsaken's struggle to pacify Silverpine Forest, directing operations against lingering Scourge loyalists, Kirin Tor remnants, and feral worgen.",["faction:Horde"]="For any Horde traveler venturing south from Tirisfal Glades, the Sepulcher offers the only reliable refuge, repair, and flight hub for miles."},kw={"crypt","deathguard","forsaken outpost","graveyard","sepulcher","silverpine forest","silverpine sepulcher"},rel={"zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:scourge","topic:worgen","topic:lordaeron","topic:third-war","quest:446"},src={"Sepulcher"}}
E["subzone:shadowfang-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowfang Keep",z="silverpine",s="Perched on a rugged bluff overlooking Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest, Shadowfang Keep is the dark lair of the mad Archmage Arugal and his feral worgen. Formerly known as Silverlaine Keep, the fortress fell to ravenous wolf-beasts summoned during the Third War, leaving its ancient halls haunted by the slain nobility and crawling with lupine horrors.",h="Perched on a rugged bluff overlooking Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest, Shadowfang Keep is the...",sec={{t="Fall of the Silverlaines",b="Before the Third War, this towering fortress was called Silverlaine Keep, the ancestral seat of Baron Silverlaine and the center of authority for nearby Pyrewood Village. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, desperate wizards sought forbidden means to stem the undead tide. Relying on the dimensional research of the Dalaran mage Ur, the Archmage Arugal summoned the extra-dimensional worgen into Azeroth. The savage beasts tore through the Scourge, but quickly spiraled out of control. Rampaging across southern Silverpine, the pack besieged the stronghold, slaughtering Baron Silverlaine, his family, and Commander Springvale's defenders. Guilt and grief shattered Arugal's sanity; rather than flee, he claimed the fortress, renaming it Shadowfang Keep and adopting the monstrous predators as his 'children.'",sp=0},{t="A Haunted Bastion",b="Today, Shadowfang Keep serves as the epicenter of a growing wolf curse that plagues Silverpine Forest. Arugal dwells in the highest observatory, flanked by his ravenous worgen—including the Moonrage and Shadowfang packs—and sinister beasts like his massive pet wolf, Fenrus. Below his sanctum, the restless ghosts of the keep's former lords, such as Baron Silverlaine and Commander Springvale, remain trapped in torment, cursed to endlessly defend the halls they failed to protect in life. From atop these walls, Arugal extends his insidious influence down into Pyrewood Village and the surrounding woodlands, posing a dire threat to the neighboring Forsaken who seek to purge the forest of his madness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Shadowfang Keep called before Arugal took over?",a="It was originally named Silverlaine Keep. It was the ancestral fortress of Baron Silverlaine, a nobleman whose forces, led by the paladin Commander Springvale, oversaw Pyrewood Village and the surrounding lands before the worgen overrun.",al={"original name","who used to own shadowfang","silverlaine keep"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Arugal summon the worgen here?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge was relentlessly crushing the forces of Dalaran and raising slain wizards into undeath. Against the warnings of the Kirin Tor, Archmage Arugal used the research of the wizard Ur to summon extra-dimensional worgen to turn the tide. While they decimated the undead, the beasts quickly turned on the living and ran wild across Silverpine.",al={"why did arugal summon worgen","arugal backstory","how did worgen get here"},it="motive"},{q="Who rules Shadowfang Keep right now?",a="The keep is held by Archmage Arugal. Driven mad with guilt over releasing the monsters, he embraced the worgen as his own 'children' and rules from the fortress heights alongside his deadly pack.",al={"current master of shadowfang","who lives in shadowfang keep","arugal keep"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are there ghosts in Shadowfang Keep?",a="The ghosts belong to Baron Silverlaine, Commander Springvale, and the keep's former household. When the worgen swarmed the keep and slaughtered everyone inside, the inhabitants' spirits remained bound to the stone, cursed to wander the ruined corridors.",al={"silverlaine ghost","commander springvale ghost","undead inside shadowfang"},it="threat"},{q="What connection does Pyrewood Village have to the keep?",a="Pyrewood sits in the shadow of the keep and was historically governed by Baron Silverlaine. Under Arugal's creeping influence, the villagers were afflicted with the worgen curse, appearing as ordinary humans by day but transforming into rabid beasts under the night sky.",al={"pyrewood and shadowfang","pyrewood village curse"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What is Shadowfang Keep?",a="Shadowfang Keep is a haunted stronghold perched high on a rocky bluff in southern Silverpine Forest, looming directly over Pyrewood Village near the Greymane Wall. Originally the ancestral seat of Baron Silverlaine, the fortress was overrun by feral worgen summoned during the Third War. Today, it stands as the secluded lair of the mad Archmage Arugal, guarded by ravenous beastmen, spectral defenders, and twisted sorcery.",al={"what is shadowfang keep","shadowfang keep lore","shadowfang castle"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Shadowfang Keep?",a="During the Third War, Archmage Arugal sought to repel the Scourge by using the research of Ur to summon extra-dimensional worgen into Azeroth. Though the beasts slaughtered the undead, they quickly ran rampant across Silverpine and laid siege to Baron Silverlaine's stronghold. The worgen butchered the baron, his family, and his garrison. Driven mad by guilt and horror, Arugal embraced the beasts as his own 'children,' claimed the fallen keep, and renamed it Shadowfang.",al={"shadowfang keep history","what happened to silverlaine keep","fall of shadowfang"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is Shadowfang Keep ruined?",a="The fortress fell into ruin when Arugal's rampaging worgen besieged and overwhelmed its defenders, slaughtering Baron Silverlaine and his entire household. Rather than restoring the noble estate, the deranged archmage allowed the halls to crumble into darkness, filling the courtyard and ramparts with savage beasts and the tormented ghosts of the slain nobles who perished during the massacre.",al={"why is shadowfang keep ruined","shadowfang keep destroyed","why is it abandoned"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Shadowfang Keep dangerous?",a="Shadowfang Keep is exceptionally lethal. Behind its iron gates lurk packs of ferocious worgen, Arugal's colossal pet worgen Fenrus, and bloodthirsty cultists. In addition to the living beasts, the restless, vengeful spirits of Baron Silverlaine and his slain soldiers haunt the halls, while Archmage Arugal commands deadly arcane curses from atop the castle ramparts.",al={"is shadowfang dangerous","shadowfang keep dangers","how dangerous is shadowfang"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Shadowfang Keep?",a="Originally known as Silverlaine Keep after its ruling noble, the fortress was renamed Shadowfang Keep by Archmage Arugal after his summoned worgen overran it. He bestowed the name in honor of the savage, shadowy wolf-beasts he adopted as his beloved children and the dark packs that now stalk its halls.",al={"shadowfang keep name","why is it named shadowfang","how did shadowfang get its name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken, Arugal's worgen are an unpredictable menace sprawling right on the doorstep of the Undercity's outer territory in Silverpine, demanding swift extermination.",["class:Mage"]="Shadowfang Keep stands as a grim reminder of Kirin Tor arrogance, showing the disaster of delving into extra-dimensional summoning without restraint."},kw={"arugal","fenrus","pyrewood","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","springvale","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:commander-springvale","subzone:pyrewood-village","topic:worgen","quest:1014","subzone:greymane-wall"},src={"Shadowfang Keep"}}
E["subzone:shining-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Shining Strand",z="silverpine",s="The Shining Strand is the strip of shoreline hugging Lordamere Lake along eastern Silverpine Forest, stretching south from the Ruins of Lordaeron toward the rugged foothills of Alterac. Once dominated by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs, the shores are now contested ground where Forsaken encampments watch the water and skirmish with encroaching worgen.",h="The Shining Strand is the strip of shoreline hugging Lordamere Lake along eastern Silverpine Forest...",sec={{t="A Contested Coastline",b="Running along the eastern edge of Silverpine Forest, the Shining Strand borders the misty waters of Lordamere Lake. In earlier days, the Vile Fin tribe of murlocs established several aggressive settlements along these shallows, posing a deadly hazard to anyone attempting to travel the lake road. While the Vile Fins have largely shifted their presence eastward to the Dawning Isles, the shore remains far from peaceful. Forsaken scouts and apothecaries have established footholds along the strand, contending with feral worgen roaming out from the deep woods and keeping a watchful eye on both the waters and the hills bordering Alterac.",sp=0},{t="Alchemical Harvest",b="Beyond its strategic position between Lordaeron and the southern borders, the Shining Strand and its neighboring waters drew early attention from the Royal Apothecary Society. The late Apothecary Berard recorded notes on unusual hardened tumors harvested from the local Vile Fin murlocs, theorizing that their corrupted anatomy could serve as a valuable catalyst in concocting a new plague for Sylvanas Windrunner's fledgling nation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Shining Strand located?",a="The Shining Strand is the eastern shoreline of Silverpine Forest, bordering the waters of Lordamere Lake. It begins just south of the Ruins of Lordaeron and ends against the rough hills that separate Silverpine from the Alterac Mountains.",al={"shining strand location","where is shining strand","silverpine coast"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats are found along the Shining Strand?",a="Forsaken encampments along the strand contend regularly with prowling worgen that emerge from the Silverpine woods. While the Vile Fin murlocs previously held strongpoints on the shore, most have relocated to the nearby Dawning Isles, though aquatic threats still lurk in the shallows.",al={"shining strand monsters","what is on shining strand","shining strand enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society interested in this area?",a="The late Apothecary Berard documented that the native Vile Fin murlocs carried hardened tumors with unique physiological traits. The Society saw these growths as promising ingredients in their ongoing research to develop a lethal new plague.",al={"apothecary berard","shining strand plague","new plague tumor"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did the local murlocs go?",a="After pressure from Forsaken forces securing the shoreline, the Vile Fin tribe relocated their major encampments off the mainland coast to the Dawning Isles in Lordamere Lake.",al={"where are murlocs silverpine","vile fin location","shining strand murlocs"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Shining Strand?",a="The Shining Strand is the eastern shoreline of Silverpine Forest along the waters of Lordamere Lake. It extends southward from the outskirts of the Ruins of Lordaeron down to the jagged hills separating Silverpine from the Alterac Mountains.",al={"what is shining strand","shining strand lore","where is the strand"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at the Shining Strand?",a="The shoreline was once dominated by settlements of the Vile Fin murloc tribe, creating a treacherous stretch for travelers. The Forsaken eventually drove the murlocs offshore to the Dawning Isles, establishing their own shoreline outposts while clashing with the feral worgen prowling the woods.",al={"shining strand history","what happened at the strand"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Shining Strand dangerous?",a="Yes. Though the Forsaken displaced the native Vile Fin murlocs who once raided the coast, the area remains perilous. Encroaching worgen beasts roam the nearby woods and shores, frequently clashing with Forsaken encampments established along the strand.",al={"is shining strand dangerous","shining strand dangers"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Holding the Shining Strand protects the Undercity's southern lake flank and provides valuable specimens for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into a new plague.",["faction:Horde"]="The strand offers a clear, if perilous, transit corridor along Lordamere Lake connecting the northern approaches of Silverpine to the passages heading toward the Alterac Mountains."},kw={"apothecary berard","dawning isles","lordamere lake","shining strand","silverpine forest","vile fin","worgen"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:dawning-isles","quest:367","topic:forsaken","topic:murloc","topic:worgen","zone:alterac"},src={"Shining Strand"}}
E["subzone:skittering-dark"] = {t="subzone",n="Skittering Dark",z="silverpine",s="The Skittering Dark is an abandoned mine and shadowy woodland hollow in western Silverpine Forest. Infested by aggressive Skitterweb spiders and their massive matriarch, the cavern and its surrounding woods are littered with webbed cocoons containing unwary beasts and travelers.",h="The Skittering Dark is an abandoned mine and shadowy woodland hollow in western Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Webbed Hollow",b="Tucked into the hills just east of the western coast of North Tide's Run, the Skittering Dark was once a working mine. Today, the shafts are completely choked with cobwebs, serving as the sprawling nest of the Skitterweb arachnids. Under the watch of a monstrous matriarch deep underground—and the shadowy weaver Krethis haunting the exterior—the spiders hunt anything that strays too close. Their silk-wrapped larder includes indigenous bears, worgs, and wandering worgen from the nearby woodlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Skittering Dark?",a="It is an abandoned mine in western Silverpine Forest that has been entirely overrun by giant Skitterweb spiders. The cavern network and surrounding trees are thick with sticky webbing and predatory arachnids.",al={"skittering dark mine","what is this mine","spider cave silverpine"},it="place"},{q="What is inside the cocoons littering the area?",a="The Skitterwebs prey on local wildlife like bears and worgs, but their webs also trap feral worgen from the surrounding woods.",al={"webbed cocoons","who is in the webs","spider victims"}},{q="Who leads the spiders in the mine?",a="The brood is led by the Skitterweb Matriarch, a massive spider nesting deep within the darkened tunnels of the mine shaft.",al={"spider boss","skittering dark boss","matriarch"},it="leader"},{q="Where is the Skittering Dark located?",a="It sits nestled against the hills in western Silverpine Forest, just east of the shoreline known as North Tide's Run.",al={"skittering dark location","how to find skittering dark"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives in the Skittering Dark?",a="The mine and surrounding hollow are overrun by Skitterweb spiders. They lurk in dark crevices and spin thick webs across the rocky slopes and tunnels, commanded from deep within by a massive broodmother known as the Skitterweb Matriarch. A formidable rare spider named Krethis the Shadowspinner is also known to prowl the slopes just outside.",al={"who lives in skittering dark","skittering dark inhabitants","what creatures live in skittering dark"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Skittering Dark dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. The aggressive Skitterweb spiders will ambush anyone foolish enough to draw near their nests. A grim testament to their ferocity litters the ground: sticky cocoons wrapping bears, worgs, ferocious worgen, and even shipwrecked orc survivors who washed ashore from the western coast, all preserved for the brood's next feeding.",al={"how dangerous is skittering dark","is skittering dark dangerous","danger of skittering dark"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is the mine in the Skittering Dark abandoned?",a="The mine was once worked before the plague and war devastated Lordaeron, but whatever mortal enterprise once extracted ore here collapsed long ago. Left completely unattended during the kingdom's fall, the subterranean shafts and shadowed tunnels offered a fertile, secluded breeding ground for monstrous arachnids, completely driving out any lingering industry.",al={"why is skittering dark abandoned","who mined skittering dark","why did miners leave skittering dark"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Skittering Dark?",a="The name reflects both the grim nature of the abandoned shaft and the ceaseless rustle of the swarm within. Beneath the perpetual gloom of Silverpine's shadowed hills and cavern walls, the only constant sound is the chittering and scuttling of thousands of spider legs moving through the dark.",al={"why is it called skittering dark","skittering dark name origin","how did skittering dark get its name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Orcs venturing into Silverpine should take note: the Skitterwebs actively drag stranded Horde survivors from the nearby coastal shipwreck into their webbed dens."},kw={"krethis","matriarch","mine","north tide's run","silverpine","skittering dark","skitterweb","spider"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:north-tide-s-run","subzone:forsaken-rear-guard","topic:worgen","topic:forsaken"},src={"Skittering Dark"}}
E["subzone:south-tide-s-run"] = {t="subzone",n="South Tide's Run",z="silverpine",s="South Tide's Run is the lonely southwestern coastline of Silverpine Forest, stretching along the cold waters of the Great Sea. Flanking the forested interior, these damp sands and surf serve as the southern complement to North Tide's Run.",h="South Tide's Run is the lonely southwestern coastline of Silverpine Forest, stretching along the cold waters...",sec={{t="The Western Shore",b="Stretching along the southwestern edge of Silverpine Forest, South Tide's Run forms a desolate boundary between the woods and the Great Sea. Unlike the protected eastern roads that lead down toward the Greymane Wall, this open shore takes the brunt of the western tides, serving as a bleak coastal wilderness largely untouched by the settlements inland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is South Tide's Run located?",a="South Tide's Run occupies the southwestern coastline of Silverpine Forest, bordering the open expanse of the Great Sea.",al={"where is south tides run","south tides run location","south tide run map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does South Tide's Run differ from North Tide's Run?",a="Both are long stretches of beach defining Silverpine Forest's western shoreline, but South Tide's Run covers the southern portion of the coast, whereas North Tide's Run extends along the northwest near the border with Tirisfal Glades.",al={"north tides run vs south tides run","difference between tide runs"}},{q="Are there any settlements along South Tide's Run?",a="There are no major towns or outposts along the beach itself. Most Forsaken activity remains inland near the main thoroughfares, leaving the shoreline isolated.",al={"towns in south tides run","who lives in south tides run"},it="residents"},{q="What is South Tide's Run?",a="South Tide's Run is the southwestern coastal stretch of Silverpine Forest, running alongside the waters of the Great Sea. Together with North Tide's Run to the north, it forms the western shoreline of the region.",al={"what is south tides run","south tides run info","south tide run"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called South Tide's Run?",a="It takes its name from its position along Silverpine Forest's coast, serving as the southern counterpart to North Tide's Run along the edge of the Great Sea.",al={"why south tides run","south tides run name meaning","south tide run name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The wild southwestern coast lies far from the protection of the Sepulcher, making it an empty frontier rarely trodden by the Forsaken."},kw={"great sea","silverpine coast","silverpine forest","south tide's run","south tides run"},rel={"subzone:north-tide-s-run","zone:silverpine"},src={"South Tide's Run"}}
E["subzone:valgan-s-field"] = {t="subzone",n="Valgan's Field",z="silverpine",s="Valgan's Field is an abandoned wheat farm nestled in northern Silverpine Forest, overlooking Lordamere Lake. Once a picturesque homestead, it now lies desolate and overrun by the feral Moonrage worgen unleashed by Archmage Arugal.",h="Valgan's Field is an abandoned wheat farm nestled in northern Silverpine Forest, overlooking Lordamere Lake.",sec={{t="A Ruined Homestead",b="Situated just west of the Shining Strand and north of the nearby river, Valgan's Field was once a prosperous wheat farm offering scenic views of Lordamere Lake. That peaceful life vanished when the Scourge tore through Lordaeron, forcing its owner, Valgan, to flee or meet his end. Left untended, the ruined structures fell into the claws of feral Moonrage worgen prowling down from Shadowfang Keep. Before the Third War, the mage Arugal spent time here, leaving behind remnants of his arcane research that now draw the attention of the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Valgan?",a="Valgan was the human farmer who owned and worked this homestead before the Third War. When the Scourge swept across northern Lordaeron, Valgan either died or fled into exile, leaving the farm to fall into ruin.",al={"valgan","who is valgan","valgans field history"},it="name"},{q="Why are worgen roaming Valgan's Field?",a="The feral Moonrage pack infesting the farm was summoned into Silverpine Forest by Archmage Arugal. Driven mad by guilt and dark magic, Arugal unleashed the beasts against the Scourge, but quickly lost control as they spread across the forest.",al={"why are there worgen here","moonrage worgen valgan","who brought the worgen"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the Forsaken interested in this farm?",a="Archmage Arugal resided at the farm before the war and left behind valuable spellbooks. The Forsaken seek out these lost writings in their campaign to understand and counter Arugal's terrifying magic.",al={"valgans field quest","why forsaken care about valgans field","arugal spellbook farm"},it="purpose"},{q="What rare threats appear near the farm?",a="Aside from the packs of Moonrage worgen haunting the fields, a dangerous beast known as Nightlash is occasionally spotted prowling the surrounding perimeter.",al={"nightlash","rare spawn valgans field","monsters at valgan"},it="threat"},{q="What is Valgan's Field?",a="Valgan's Field is a desolate, abandoned wheat farm situated in northern Silverpine Forest, resting just west of the Shining Strand and east of the main road. Before the plague tore through Lordaeron, it was a peaceful homestead overlooking Lordamere Lake. Today, like much of the forest, it lies overgrown, unkempt, and haunted by deadly predators.",al={"what is valgans field","valgan farm","valgans field silverpine"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Valgan's Field?",a="Before the Third War, the archmage Arugal spent time here, leaving behind remnants of his arcane research. When the Scourge swept through Silverpine, the homestead fell into ruin as its owner was driven off or slaughtered. Later, when Arugal unleashed the worgen upon the region from Shadowfang Keep, feral Moonrage worgen overran the fields, claiming the broken farm as their territory.",al={"valgans field history","what happened to valgan farm"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is Valgan's Field ruined?",a="The farm was abandoned when the Scourge marched across northern Lordaeron, devastating the rural settlements. Any hope of reclaiming the land vanished when Arugal summoned the otherworldly worgen, whose Moonrage pack infested the fields and made human habitation impossible.",al={"why is valgans field abandoned","why is valgan farm ruined","ruin of valgans field"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Valgan's Field dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for lone travelers. The abandoned farmstead is prowled by vicious Moonrage worgen spawned from Arugal's dark magic. In addition to the ravenous pack, dangerous beasts such as the shadow prowler Nightlash are known to stalk the perimeter.",al={"how dangerous is valgans field","valgans field threats"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, clearing Valgan's Field is essential to securing the road through Silverpine and recovering Arugal's notes before his monstrous pets spread further north.",["class:Mage"]="Arugal's abandoned research at the farm offers a sobering warning of the catastrophic perils of unchecked summoning and extraplanar magic."},kw={"arugal","moonrage","nightlash","shining strand","silverpine forest","valgan","valgan's field","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","quest:99","topic:worgen","zone:silverpine","subzone:shining-strand","subzone:lordamere-lake","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Valgan's Field"}}
E["zone:silverpine"] = {t="zone",n="Silverpine Forest",z="silverpine",s="Silverpine Forest is an eerie, mist-laden woodland stretching along Lordaeron's western coast between Tirisfal Glades and the sealed Greymane Wall. Haunted by the lingering scars of the Scourge plague, it serves as the contested southern frontier of the Forsaken. Travelers here face feral worgen roaming the shadows, diseased gnolls, and hostile human enclaves.",h="Silverpine Forest is an eerie, mist-laden woodland stretching along Lordaeron's western coast between...",sec={{t="A Haunted Frontier",b="Once celebrated as a lush wonder of Lordaeron through which noble travelers journeyed to Capital City, Silverpine Forest has withered under the touch of the Third War. Ghostly fogs weave between dying, silver-barked pines, and ruined farmsteads sit abandoned to the wilderness. To the north lies Tirisfal Glades, while the eastern shore borders Lordamere Lake. To the south stands the imposing and shut Greymane Wall, sealing off the isolationist kingdom of Gilneas from the surrounding chaos. The Forsaken maintain their central outpost at the Sepulcher, striving to secure the woods from enemies on all sides.",sp=0},{t="The Worgen and Shadowfang",b="Silverpine's most infamous peril is the worgen curse. High above the southwest woods sits Shadowfang Keep, the former seat of Baron Silverlaine, now dominated by the mad Dalaran archmage Arugal. Seeking to repel the Scourge during the Third War, Arugal summoned extra-dimensional wolf-beasts. The creatures turned on their summoners, spreading a lycanthropic curse across the southern woods. In Pyrewood Village, ordinary-looking human villagers go about their chores by daylight, but transform into savage worgen beneath the night sky.",sp=0},{t="Rival Enclaves and the Scourge",b="The Forsaken claim to Silverpine is hotly contested by living and undead factions alike. To the east on Fenris Isle, Thule Ravenclaw leads a force of Scourge remnants while commanding the plague-addled Rot Hide gnolls that plague northern farmlands. In the south, human mages from Dalaran hold the fortified settlement of Ambermill, conducting mystical research and opposing Forsaken expansion. The Royal Apothecary Society and High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher wage a brutal, multifaceted campaign to eliminate these threats and test virulent new plagues.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Greymane Wall at the southern border?",a="The Greymane Wall is a massive stone barrier built by King Genn Greymane to completely isolate his kingdom of Gilneas from the rest of Lordaeron. When the Scourge ravaged the continent during the Third War, Gilneas locked its gates and refused outside aid, leaving the lands north of the wall—including southern Silverpine—to fend for themselves.",al={"why is there a giant wall","greymane wall lore","gate to gilneas"},it="place"},{q="Why do the villagers of Pyrewood Village attack at night?",a="The inhabitants of Pyrewood Village suffer from Archmage Arugal's worgen curse. By day, they retain human form and maintain their daily routines, remaining friendly to the Alliance. When the moon rises, the curse takes hold, transforming the entire population into savage, bloodthirsty worgen that violently attack anyone nearby.",al={"pyrewood village mystery","pyrewood worgen","why are pyrewood humans hostile at night"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful necromancer serving the Scourge. Operating out of Fenris Keep on Fenris Isle within Lordamere Lake, he commands legions of undead and exerts influence over the diseased Rot Hide gnolls across eastern Silverpine, directly threatening the Forsaken's eastern flank.",al={"who leads fenris isle","thule ravenclaw lore","scourge on fenris isle"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Dalaran occupying Ambermill?",a="Ambermill is held by wizards of Dalaran led by Archmage Ataeric. Operating from the village, these human mages monitor Forsaken movements, study the magical afflictions plaguing the forest, and seek to contain the nearby worgen outbreak radiating from Shadowfang Keep.",al={"ambermill mages","why is the alliance in ambermill","dalaran in silverpine"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Sepulcher?",a="The Sepulcher is the primary Forsaken military outpost and travel hub in Silverpine Forest. Under the command of High Executor Hadrec, it serves as the base of operations for Deathguard patrols, Deathstalker scouts, and the Royal Apothecary Society as they fight to secure the forest.",al={"horde town in silverpine","where is the flight path","sepulcher lore"},it="place",nx={14,15}},{q="Can Alliance players quest in Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine Forest has no Alliance quest hubs or friendly towns; all local quests are exclusively for the Horde. Alliance adventurers typically only enter the forest when traveling from Southshore to explore Shadowfang Keep or to battle hostile Forsaken forces.",al={"is silverpine horde only","alliance quests in silverpine","can alliance go to silverpine"},gp=true},{q="What is Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine Forest is a vast, ancient woodland along the rugged western coast of Lordaeron, directly south of Tirisfal Glades and bounded on the east by Lordamere Lake. Once a lush and verdant wood protected by the Alliance, it is now shrouded in ghostly mists, sickly pale pines, and eerie silence broken only by distant howling. The Forsaken hold sway over the north from the Sepulcher, but their claim is constantly contested by Scourge remnants, savage Rot Hide gnolls, Dalaran wizards, and the cursed worgen of Shadowfang Keep.",al={"what is silverpine","tell me about silverpine","silverpine forest lore"},it="place",add=true,nx={9,10}},{q="What happened at Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine once resembled the pristine wilderness of the Hinterlands, but the Third War ruined it. When the Lich King's Scourge swept south, undead armies torched farmsteads, slaughtered the rural population, and tainted the land with the plague of undeath. King Genn Greymane sealed Gilneas behind his massive wall, abandoning northern lands like Pyrewood and Ambermill. To repel the Scourge, Archmage Arugal unleashed savage worgen, but the curse spread out of control. With Lordaeron shattered, the blighted woods became a contested battleground.",al={"silverpine history","what happened here silverpine","fall of silverpine"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who used to live here before the Forsaken?",a="Before the Third War, Silverpine was inhabited by human farmers, miners, and soldiers of Lordaeron and Gilneas. Southern territories such as Pyrewood Village and Ambermill belonged to the Gilnean nobleman Lord Darius Crowley before the Greymane Wall severed them from the rest of the kingdom. Fenris Isle housed a bustling Lordaeron military garrison at Fenris Keep. Most of these former inhabitants perished during the Scourge invasion, fled south to the sealed wall, or succumbed to undeath and the worgen curse.",al={"who lived in silverpine before","silverpine former residents","past inhabitants of silverpine"},it="people",add=true},{q="Why is the forest so dead looking?",a="The forest bears the deep, lingering scars of the Third War. Silverpine marks the southernmost extent where the Scourge's plague of undeath visibly corrupted the flora, draining the vitality from the soil and leaving the ancient silver-barked pines pale, sickly, and shedding blighted needles. With Lordaeron destroyed and Gilneas walled off, no caretakers remained to heal the ravaged groves or tend the scorched cropland, leaving cold mists and rot to settle over the woods.",al={"why is silverpine dying","why does silverpine look dead","blighted trees silverpine"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Silverpine Forest dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. Wild predators like blighted bears, giant spiders, and ferocious worgs prowl beneath the trees. Plague-ridden Rot Hide gnolls violently slaughter travelers along the roads, while human mages from Dalaran fortify Ambermill against Horde intrusion. To the south, the feral Moonrage worgen terrorize the valleys under the sway of Archmage Arugal. Outside the fortified sanctuary of the Sepulcher, survival requires constant vigilance.",al={"how dangerous is silverpine","threats in silverpine","is it safe here"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why did the Horde send me to Silverpine?",a="You were sent south from Tirisfal Glades to reinforce the Forsaken frontier. The Undercity considers Silverpine vital to securing its southern border, but its hold is fragile and stretched thin. High Executor Hadrec and the Deathguard require capable champions to drive back encroaching Scourge necromancers, eliminate hostile gnolls, monitor Dalaran's covert maneuvers, and contain the bloodthirsty worgen threatening to overrun the woodlands.",al={"why am i in silverpine","horde silverpine arrival","why send me here"},it="arrival",add=true,nx={13}},{q="Is this still Forsaken land?",a="The Forsaken claim Silverpine as sovereign territory of the Undercity, but their control is heavily contested. While they maintain firm dominion over northern Silverpine and the fortified haven of the Sepulcher, they do not hold undisputed sway over the entire forest. Hostile Rot Hide gnolls rule the eastern waters, Dalaran wizards occupy Ambermill, and Arugal's feral worgen dominate the southwestern reaches.",al={"does forsaken own silverpine","who controls silverpine","forsaken territory silverpine"},it="today",add=true},{q="Who built the Sepulcher?",a="Before the Third War, the Sepulcher was simply a large, quiet human graveyard and roadside crypt built by the people of Lordaeron to inter their dead along the western highway. Following Lordaeron's fall, the surviving Forsaken seized the burial grounds and refitted the crypt into a fortified military outpost, caravan station, and logistical headquarters for their southern operations.",al={"who made the sepulcher","sepulcher origin","history of the sepulcher"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken based at the Sepulcher?",a="Nestled defensibly in the western hills, the Sepulcher offers the Forsaken a natural vantage overlooking the coast and the main road. Positioned between the Scourge in the east, Dalaran to the southeast, and feral worgen to the south, it serves as the only secure outpost where Deathguard patrols and Royal Apothecary researchers can coordinate defenses and protect the route to Tirisfal.",al={"why are forsaken at sepulcher","sepulcher forsaken base why","importance of sepulcher"},it="purpose",add=true},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander of Forsaken operations in Silverpine Forest, stationed at the Sepulcher. Stern and pragmatic, he directs the Deathguard and Deathstalker scouts in pacifying the wilderness, uncovering hidden threats, and orchestrating strikes against hostile forces such as Thule Ravenclaw and the Rot Hide gnolls.",al={"hadrec","who is hadrec","high executor hadrec silverpine"},it="in_charge",add=true,nx={17}},{q="Who does High Executor Hadrec answer to?",a="Hadrec answers directly to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen of the Forsaken, and her high command in the Undercity. As a senior officer of the Deathguard, his mandate is to secure the borders of her newborn kingdom and eliminate any power that could compromise Forsaken sovereignty.",al={"who is hadrec's boss","hadrec superior","who does hadrec report to"},it="leader",add=true},{q="Who are the Rot Hide gnolls and why are they here?",a="The Rot Hides are a vicious clan of gnolls inhabiting Silverpine Forest, operating primarily out of Fenris Isle and prowling the shores of Lordamere Lake. Unlike common gnolls, they are afflicted by the plague of undeath, bearing patchy gray fur and rheumy, yellow eyes. They wage a brutal guerrilla war against the Forsaken, scavenge battlefields, and fiercely assault anyone who nears their camps.",al={"rot hide gnolls","why are gnolls in silverpine","rothide gnoll silverpine"},it="threat",add=true,nx={19}},{q="Who is controlling the Rot Hide gnolls?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls are under the thrall of Thule Ravenclaw, a treacherous necromancer aligned with the Scourge. From his stronghold on Fenris Isle, Thule uses dark magic to manipulate these blighted beasts, sending them to exhumed battlefields to harvest fresh corpses for his growing legions of undead.",al={"who commands rot hides","rot hide master","who leads the rothides"},sp=1,it="threat",add=true},{q="What is the Dead Fields?",a="The Dead Field is a blighted expanse of farmland in central Silverpine, along the road leading toward Lordamere Lake. Once a peaceful agricultural homestead, it became a mass killing ground during the Third War when the Scourge overran Lordaeron. Today, it is an open graveyard littered with shallow graves and disturbed earth.",al={"dead fields silverpine","the dead field","what are the dead fields"},it="place",add=true,nx={21}},{q="Why are the gnolls digging in the Dead Fields?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls are excavating the Dead Field to unearth the human corpses buried there during the Third War. Acting on the orders of Thule Ravenclaw, they dig up bodies and preserved remains to supply the necromancer with raw material for constructing Scourge constructs and reinforcing his undead army on Fenris Isle.",al={"why are rothides digging","gnolls dead fields why","gnoll digging corpses"},sp=1,it="motive",add=true},{q="What's on Fenris Isle?",a="Fenris Isle is a large island situated within Lordamere Lake off Silverpine's eastern shore. It is dominated by Fenris Keep, a former military fortress of Lordaeron that has fallen into dark disrepair. Today, the island serves as a heavily fortified redoubt swarming with Rot Hide gnolls and the undead minions of Thule Ravenclaw.",al={"fenris isle","what is on fenris isle","fenris keep"},it="place",add=true,nx={23}},{q="Why does Hadrec want Fenris Isle attacked?",a="Hadrec recognizes Fenris Isle as the beating heart of the Scourge threat in eastern Silverpine. Leaving Thule Ravenclaw entrenched in Fenris Keep gives the Scourge an unassailable staging ground to raise undead gnolls, raid supply caravans, and threaten the eastern approach to Tirisfal. Striking the island is crucial to breaking Thule's power and securing the lake.",al={"why attack fenris isle","hadrec fenris isle motive","assault on fenris isle reason"},sp=1,it="motive",add=true},{q="Are the Dalaran wizards in Ambermill working with the Alliance?",a="Yes. While Dalaran focuses heavily on rebuilding its devastated city, the Kirin Tor forces stationed at Ambermill remain openly friendly to the Alliance and fiercely hostile to the Horde. Dalaran frequently dispatches aid to Silverpine's surviving human enclaves, opposing Forsaken expansion and working closely with southern remnants.",al={"ambermill dalaran alliance","is dalaran with alliance here","kirin tor alliance silverpine"},it="allies",add=true},{q="Who is Arugal and what is 'Arugal's Folly'?",a="Archmage Arugal was a Dalaran wizard who, in desperation to defend against the Scourge during the Third War, turned to forbidden magic and summoned monstrous wolf-beasts known as worgen. However, the feral beasts turned on Gilnean soldiers and innocent locals alike, spreading a ravenous lycanthropic curse across southern Silverpine. Driven mad by guilt and horror at what he had unleashed, Arugal retreated into Shadowfang Keep, adopting the worgen as his 'children.'",al={"arugal","arugals folly","who was arugal","archmage arugal lore"},it="history",add=true,nx={26,27}},{q="Where did the worgen come from?",a="The worgen are otherworldly wolf-beasts pulled across dimensions by Archmage Arugal. King Genn Greymane ordered the use of desperate measures to hold off the Scourge besieging the Greymane Wall, leading Arugal to conjure these ancient creatures into Silverpine, where their contagious bite quickly spread a transformative curse among the human defenders.",al={"where did worgen come from","worgen origin silverpine","how did worgen get here"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Is Arugal still alive?",a="Yes, Archmage Arugal is very much alive. Shrouded in madness, he resides high atop the towers of Shadowfang Keep, overlooking Pyrewood Village. From his fortress, he directs his pack of Shadowfang worgen and guards his twisted lupine domain from anyone bold enough to breach his gates.",al={"is arugal alive","where is arugal now","arugal status"},it="threat",add=true},{q="What is Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood Village is a human settlement nestled in southwestern Silverpine, directly beneath the imposing cliffs of Shadowfang Keep. Originally part of Lord Darius Crowley's Gilnean lands, it was stranded when the Greymane Wall was sealed before the Third War. Its surviving inhabitants struggle to maintain a semblance of normal life by day, though an ancient darkness consumes them once the sun sets.",al={"pyrewood village lore","what is pyrewood","pyrewood town"},it="place",add=true},{q="Where does all this lead after Silverpine?",a="Once you have stabilized Silverpine by confronting Thule Ravenclaw and purging Arugal in Shadowfang Keep, your journey typically leads east across the mountains into the Hillsbrad Foothills to support the Forsaken at Tarren Mill. Alternatively, many Horde travelers take a zeppelin to Kalimdor to campaign through the vast plains of the Barrens.",al={"where to after silverpine","next zone after silverpine","silverpine next step"},it="next_step",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Silverpine Forest?",a="You likely followed the southbound road out of Tirisfal Glades, passing through the mountain pass southwest of the Undercity ruins. Forsaken characters finish securing their northern home in Tirisfal and naturally press south into Silverpine to expand the fledgling empire. Alternatively, Horde travelers from other continents arrive via zeppelin outside Undercity before walking down the coast, while rare adventurers coming from the south might cross through Hillsbrad Foothills to reach these blighted woodlands.",al={"how did i get here","how do i reach silverpine","path to silverpine forest"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Silverpine Forest?",a="You are here to help the Forsaken secure their southern frontier against mounting perils. Reporting to High Executor Hadrec and the Deathstalkers at the Sepulcher, you must counter the diseased Rot Hide gnolls raiding from the Dead Fields and Fenris Isle, root out Scourge necromancers like Thule Ravenclaw, and keep close watch on Dalaran's wizards entrenched at Ambermill. Farther south, you will also investigate the ravenous wolf-beasts terrorizing Pyrewood Village and the shadow cast by Shadowfang Keep.",al={"what is my mission here","why was i sent to silverpine","what are we doing in silverpine forest"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Silverpine represents the immediate front line of Forsaken expansion south of Tirisfal Glades, where the Royal Apothecary Society tests new concoctions and the Deathguard battles lingering Scourge agents.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance explorers will find a profoundly hostile forest, punctuated only by a fragile Dalaran garrison at Ambermill and the tragic, cursed villagers of Pyrewood Village.",["class:Mage"]="The presence of Ambermill and the fall of Archmage Arugal into lupine madness make Silverpine a grim cautionary tale of Kirin Tor magic gone disastrously astray."},kw={"ambermill","arugal","fenris isle","greymane wall","pyrewood","rot hide","sepulcher","shadowfang","silverpine","silverpine forest"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:ambermill","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:greymane-wall","quest:1014","zone:tirisfal"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Silverpine Forest (Classic)","Silverpine Forest"}}
